{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do","id":163144,"title":"Forum Game - What Does This Charm Do?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-08T22:03:56-07:00","id":163144,"title":"Forum Game - What Does This Charm Do?","content":"I have The Boredom, and it feels like it's been a while since someone introduced a forum game, so here we go.<br /> <br /> Things begin when I drop in a fictional Charm name at the end of my post. The next poster then describes its general effect, splat of origin, and Ability/Attribute/whatever tie, and then ends with one or more (let's say no more than three) new fictional Charm names for the next poster to define. If there are multiple Charm names, the new poster doesn't need to feel obligated to define all of them.<br /> <br /> Minor ground rules for how loose this is meant to be:<br /> - A name doesn't need to be defined as a Charm: the new poster could say it's a Sorcery spell, Evocation, Rank, Knack, innate ability on a behemoth or other creature, whatever.<br /> - Given the above, &quot;Splat of origin&quot; and &quot;Ability/Attribute/whatever&quot; may not neatly apply, but eh, just give some idea about what uses it and how.<br /> - Non-canon splats and the like -- whether written up, conceptualized, or made up for the sake of the answer -- are A-OK! Just try to give some vague notion of what they are. Ditto utterly speculative concepts.<br /> - Mechanics and balance (for any or no edition) are fine if you wanna, but a general and cool effect for the name is the important thing.<br /> - If you're moved to develop details in an answer in addition to those three, go nuts with sharing them!<br /> - <b>NEW (12/21/14)</b> : If a full week has passed without any response to the current name(s), a new poster may respond to any unused prior name. Try to aim for something recent, though no biggie.<br /> <br /> ... Oh, and apologies to anyone coming in here disappointed for having expected something related to Dexter's Laboratory. &gt;_&gt;<br /> <br /> EDIT: Around two weeks later, the whim has struck me to listing all of these in a log. Just the first page for now, I think. I may add descriptions and a second list sorting them all into categories, but that'll come later.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">#) Name (Name by | Effect by) - Category<br /> <br /> <b>1) </b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=163184#post163184\"><b>Kinetic Triumvirate Proposition</b></a> (Gaius | Ulfsarkar) - Sidereal Socialize Charm<br /> <b>2) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=163210#post163210\">All Devouring Consumption of Knowledge Technique </a></b>(Ulfsarkar | JayTee) - Lunar Knack (Intelligence?)<br /> <b>3) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=163218#post163218\">Heaven's Lonely Sight</a></b> (JayTee | Arteliex) - Sidereal Archery Charm<br /> <b>4) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=163250#post163250\">Shattering Sky Prana</a></b> (Arteliex | Korhal_IV) - Martial Arts Charm (Storm Serpent Style)<br /> <b>5) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=163895#post163895\">Fitful Luster Stance</a></b> (Korhal_IV | Robert Vance) - Dragon-Blooded Resistance Charm<br /> <b>6a) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=163915#post163915\">Running Through the Night Royalty</a> </b>(Robert Vance | Tiresias) - Abyssal Socialize Charm<br /> <b>6b)</b> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=163919#post163919\"><b>Running Through the Night Royalty</b></a>(Robert Vance | semicasual) - Solar Performance Charm<br /> <b>7) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=163945#post163945\">Carefree Improvisation Method</a> </b>(semicasual | Pyrosorc) - Sidereal Socialize Charm<br /> <b>8a)</b> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=163960#post163960\"><b>Thousandth Sunburst Maw</b></a> (Tiresias | MrInsecure) - Infernal Brawl Charm<br /> <b>8b)</b> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=163988#post163988\"><b>Thousandth Sunburst Maw</b></a> (Tiresias | The Hanged Man) - First and Forsaken Lion Panoply Charm<br /> <b>9) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=163994#post163994\">The Heart Dies Slowly</a></b> (MrInsecure | Bronze Tiger) - Solar Integrity Charm<br /> <b>10) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=164011#post164011\">Endless Cycle Conflux</a></b> (Bronze Tiger | turkeygiant) - Solar Lore Charm<br /> <b>11) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=164071#post164071\">Pilfered Perfection of Power</a></b> (turkeygiant | Imrix) - Lunar Appearance Charm<br /> <b>12)</b> <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=164080#post164080\">Hungry Spear Unchained</a></b> (Imrix | The MG) - Abyssal Melee Charm<br /> <b>13) Centipede Skin Curse</b> ( | ) - </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Charm Name:</b> Kinetic Triumvirate Proposition","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":". 12-21-2014, 05:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T22:48:53-07:00","id":163184,"title":"","content":"<b>Kinetic Triumvirate Proposition</b><br /> Splat of Origin: Sidereal<br /> Ability: Socialize<br /> <br /> It is a fact of social interaction that in any group of three, two will turn again one. A Sidereal takes this further and can conspire with spirits of air to bring low a foe. <br /> <br /> The Sidereal makes ROLL and if successful deals DAMAGE and knocks the target down. This ability cannot be used while not in creation or Yu-shan.<br /> <br /> All Devouring Consumption of Knowledge Technique","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>1","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27-ulfsarkar","name":"Ulfsarkar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T22:56:59-07:00","id":163210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulfsarkar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=163184#post163184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All Devouring Consumption of Knowledge Technique</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunar Shapeshifting Knack. Kill the target, eat the heart to not only gain their shape, but also his knowledge, allowing perfect (with a capital P) mimicry and the ability to add that person as a &quot;contacts&quot; background so you can draw on their knowledge at any time.<br /> <br /> Heaven's Lonely Sight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T23:13:27-07:00","id":163218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=163210#post163210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Heaven's Lonely Sight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Splat: Sidereal<br /> Ability: Archery<br /> <br /> As long as the Sidereal is alone and has no assistance from allies, and is at Long Range, he may continue to make Unexpected attacks against any target in his line of sight. Once chosen, the Target may not be changed without a reactivation of this Charm. Additionally, as long as the Sidereal may move, the Target may not close distance with the Sidereal, remaining at Long Range until the Charm ends in (archery) rounds.<br /> <br /> <br /> Shattering Sky Prana","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/697-arteliex","name":"Arteliex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar697_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T00:13:38-07:00","id":163250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arteliex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=163218#post163218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shattering Sky Prana</div> </div> </div> </div>Prerequisites: Martial Arts 5, Essence 3, Thunder-Meets-Ground Stance, Storm Serpent Form<br /> Cost 5m, 1wp<br /> Type: Supplemental, Combo-OK<br /> <br /> The storm sifu's wrath cannot be stayed by mere distance; she forms her will into a gust as strong as steel, and strikes all her opponents at once. The martial artist makes up to (Essence) attacks at targets she can see within (25*Essence) yards. No target may be struck more than once.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Fitful Luster Stance","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/K9a6Pmp.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/998-korhal_iv","name":"Korhal_IV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"592"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T12:31:22-07:00","id":163895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korhal_IV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=163250#post163250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fitful Luster Stance</div> </div> </div> </div>Dragon-Blooded Resistance. The Terrestrial's anima hardens into a crystalline shell, converting its anima flux into a sporadic defensive boost instead of a recurring damage effect. <br /> <br /> Running Through the Night Royalty","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T12:48:00-07:00","id":163915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=163895#post163895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Running Through the Night Royalty</div> </div> </div> </div>Abyssal Socialize<br /> <br /> As the Deathknight saunters through the darkness, the echo of her footsteps calls out to the denizens of the night. The Abyssal rolls Charisma + Socialize as a social influence against all criminals, thieves and murders in the area, benefiting from any intimacies towards crime that these blackguards might possess. Those who fall under the Abyssal's influence seek her out and willingly join her criminal gang until the sun next rises. <br /> <br /> <b>Thousandth Sunburst Maw </b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T12:51:41-07:00","id":163919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=163895#post163895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dragon-Blooded Resistance. The Terrestrial's anima hardens into a crystalline shell, converting its anima flux into a sporadic defensive boost instead of a recurring damage effect.<br /> <br /> Running Through the Night Royalty</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm reminded of a thing I saw once where a nobleman smuggled a prisoner out of a secure area by dressing her up like a prostitute and then stumbling through the halls with her with some wine and a lot of yelling. Everyone else studiously ignored them, enabling their escape.<br /> <br /> Solar Performance Charm.<br /> Prerequisites: Performance 4, Essence 4, Heart-Compelling Method<br /> Cost: 3m, 1 WP<br /> Duration: 1 Scene<br /> <br /> No one wants to impede the path of important people on private errands, or admit to being a witness to their passage. A Solar in a hurry to be somewhere can activate this charm and find that crowds of people will part before him - people are just naturally inclined to make way, and look away. Anyone caught by the effect of this charm gains a temporary intimacy that will make them disinclined to talk about or remember the Solar. The benefits of this charm extends to anyone who is traveling with the Solar who does not interact with the crowd.<br /> <br /> Carefree Improvisation Method<br /> <br /> EDIT: Whoops, ninja'd. Sorry, Tiresias.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":". 06-09-2014, 04:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T13:18:09-07:00","id":163945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=163919#post163919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Carefree Improvisation Method</div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereal Socialise. The exalt may not know a taboo or otherwise shameful secret of the target, but they don't really care. They make a wild accusation against the target as part of activating this charm, which Fate will make sure they can later find evidence for.<br /> <br /> I'll let someone answer Tiresias' one rather than keeping two going at once.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1414-pyrosorc","name":"Pyrosorc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T13:38:21-07:00","id":163960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=163915#post163915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <b>Thousandth Sunburst Maw </b></div> </div> </div> </div> Infernal Brawl When the Green Sun erupts, all is consumed in diseased sunfire. This supplements a Brawl attack, making it deal lethal damage and allowing the Infernal to gain one health for every two damage he deals. However, if the attack deals no damage, the Infernal instead takes (Essence) damage, as his own sunfire consumes his immortal flesh. Next Charm: The Heart Dies Slowly","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;We do not quit playing because we grow old, we grow old because we quit playing.&quot; - Oliver Wendell Holmes","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/283-mrinsecure","name":"MrInsecure","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T14:03:29-07:00","id":163994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrInsecure</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=163960#post163960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Heart Dies Slowly</div> </div> </div> </div>Solar Integrity - A solar never gives up on the the things he cares about. This Charm permanently makes it so that any positive intimacy the Exalt possesses takes twice as long to degrade by any means, and even Charms which automatically remove intimacies must be used twice. <br /> <br /> New Charm: Endless Cycle Conflux <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/777-bronze-tiger","name":"Bronze Tiger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T14:29:02-07:00","id":164011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bronze Tiger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=163994#post163994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New Charm: Endless Cycle Conflux</div> </div> </div> </div>Solar-Lore: The Solar enters a deep meditative state throwing his mind back into past ages. Surveying a blinding white landscape, the Solar sees golden figures coalesce out of the light, the embodiment of his exaltation's past incarnations. The Solar may seek advise from these knowledgeable echoes of who they once were, though there is no guarantee that they will give clear or even truthful answers.<br /> <br /> New Charm: Pilfered Perfection of Power","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T15:01:09-07:00","id":164071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=164011#post164011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New Charm: Pilfered Perfection of Power</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunar Appearance; by stealing a small piece of the target (usually blood or hair), the Moonchild may cloak their magics in an illusory guise of acts the target might commit. With the gnarled fingerbone of an aged Terrestrial in their grip, the Lunars fluid-flesh agility is obscured behind lightning speed and helpful winds, while the Lunatic's passionate entreaties burn with Draconic fire.<br /> <br /> New Charm: Hungry Spear Unchained","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are no problems, only plothooks.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1P2AuLM6D1Et9mWQVJp-ugWujFJhTi2VwQBtOazOW1Mg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Terrifying Argent Witches Hub</a><br /> <i>Originally posted by </i><b><i>Dex Davican</i></b><br /> I need them for my collection: <i>Enormous Gonads of 2012: A Retrospective.</i>","edited":{"userid":920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/920-imrix","user":"Imrix","date":". 06-09-2014, 06:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/920-imrix","name":"Imrix","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T15:11:49-07:00","id":164080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Imrix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=164071#post164071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hungry Spear Unchained</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Abyssal Melee</b><br /> Death's Lawgiver whispers to a weapon, enlightening it to the purpose of all steel. Anyone who wields it must then cut down the living, starting with those they love and hate.<br /> <br /> New Charm: <b>Centipede Skin Curse</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T15:39:34-07:00","id":164099,"title":"","content":"Centipede Skin Curse<br /> <b>Type: </b>Infernal<br /> <b>Ability: </b>Resistance<br /> When using this charm, an Infernal grows hard bug-like plates all over his body, giving him additional soak against bashing and lethal damage for the remainder of the scene. This charm may be purchased multiple times. The second purchase grants additional points of bashing and lethal soak, but causes the Infernal to suffer a small mobility penalty when using this charm. The third purchase grants additional soak and causes short spines to grow out of the plates, allowing him to inflict lethal damage with unarmed and grapple attacks. At the fourth purchase, the Infernal may choose to commit motes spent to activate this charm, allowing it to remain active until the motes are released. Additionally, while using this charm, the Infernal loses [X] dice from all social roles except those involving intimidation due to his insectoid appearance.<br /> <br /> <b>If Walls Could Talk Technique</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/770-eldrvarya","name":"Eldrvarya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar770_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T16:50:47-07:00","id":164202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldrvarya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=164099#post164099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>If Walls Could Talk Technique</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Dragon-Blooded Investigation<br /> <br /> Listening carefully to the reverberations left in the stone of a structure , the Exalt can hear faint echos of any conversation that happened in that particular room in the past (Essence) weeks. Threshold successes can be spent to know the number of participants in the conversation, the tone used (whether it was a friendly chat or heated argument, for example), and even a few of the most important words or points made.<br /> <br /> <b>Coward-Rallying Cry</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Playing 3e and miss Anathema? Try my web app, <a href=\"https://www.lotcastingatemi.com\" target=\"_blank\">Lot-Casting Atemi</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/553-hushnowquietnow","name":"hushnowquietnow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar553_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T17:02:45-07:00","id":164210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hushnowquietnow</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=164202#post164202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Coward-Rallying Cry</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Type: Terrestrial<br /> Ability: Presence<br /> With a single word, the Dragon-Blooded reminds his troops that they have strength and power: for the remainder of the scene, the target treats his Valor as the Exalt's Presence (maximum of 5), and treat her Essence as theirs for MDV calculations. The target of this charm may also regain Valor channels up to his current maximum through stunts, as though he possessed the Solar Charm Phoenix Renewal Technique.<br /> <br /> <b>Shedding Skin and Tears</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T19:03:45-07:00","id":164292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=164210#post164210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Shedding Skin and Tears</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Abyssal Occult; cling so tightly to your own sorrow (or that of a ghost, shared with hypothetical prerequisite charms) that you become a dematerialized shade of yourself with a wailing cry that maddens the living or drives them to despair. <br /> <br /> Counting Whispers, Counting Souls","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T20:49:57-07:00","id":164381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=164292#post164292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Abyssal Occult; cling so tightly to your own sorrow (or that of a ghost, shared with hypothetical prerequisite charms) that you become a dematerialized shade of yourself with a wailing cry that maddens the living or drives them to despair.<br /> <br /> Counting Whispers, Counting Souls</div> </div> </div> </div>Abyssal Lore. By liberating several of the living from their prison of flesh, the Abyssal can develop startling insights. This permits a much smoother and more reliable acquisition of knowledge and mysteries from Whispers than is typical.<br /> <br /> Charm Name: Compelling the Specie Atemi","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T21:37:52-07:00","id":164447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=164292#post164292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Counting Whispers, Counting Souls</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Raksha Cup</b><br /> Sometimes when a mortal falls under a raksha's sway, the Prince of Chaos shows mercy (or something like it), and sends him away without a hollow look in his eye, but with sweet whispers in his heart. This Charm supplements an attempt to devour a Creation-born's Virtues or Willpower (via Ravishing the Created Form, Soul-Consuming Hunger, or any other such power), allowing the raksha to forgo reducing the target's traits as well as the usual benefits. Instead, inaudible to all others, alluring half-heard voices become the target's constant companions, urging him to gather fresh recipients for the raksha's tender graces.<br /> <br /> These instill and sustain a Bond in the target toward that end, with a strength determined by the number of Virtue Dots or Willpower the raksha would have consumed or rolled to consume, whichever is greater: Minor for 1, Major for 3, and Defining for 5 or more. If such a Bond already exists, or the target possesses a positive Bond or Tie to the raksha in question, reduce the cost by 1 if Minor or 2 if Major. If the raksha targeted a Virtue, the host cannot channel it while the whispers distract him. If the raksha targeted Willpower, the host experiences no dreams and recovers no Willpower from sleep; the whispers gobble it up, leaving only a vaguely pleasant murmur in their wake. These whispers end only when their host has delivered a number of new Creation-born to the raksha equal to the raksha's Cup Grace. A given raksha cannot place new whispers into a target without removing the old ones.<br /> <br /> On a repurchase, the target must form at least a Minor Bond as described above, but the Prince of Chaos may choose to &quot;spend&quot; some of the foregone traits or original successes on the roll at the above rate to create an additional Intimacy. This may be a Tie to the raksha herself or a Bond that serves and pleases the raksha's aims.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Hunh. ._. Genuinely did not see Saur Ops's post until just now. I'm unsure whether to chalk it up to my general weariness or the forum software being odd. I'll hang onto my name suggestion for later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Cleaning a bit. 06-10-2014, 12:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T21:52:02-07:00","id":164476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=164381#post164381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Charm Name: Compelling the Specie Atemi</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunar Charisma: Merchant prince expose their wealth for all to see, not knowing silver eyes lurking just behind the corner. By rolling (Charisma + Larceny) again a difficulty of the target organization (Size), success allow the Lunar to leech of the group's Wealth, at a rate of one dot per week, the Lunar can freely distribute these stolen dots for any social group that she know of.<br /> <br /> Moon-Swallowing Ancient Worm<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T00:49:57-07:00","id":164587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Moon-Swallowing Ancient Worm </div> </div> </div><b>This is the name the green sun princes have started to call a power of mine. During the night, that annoying moon spirit tries to assist people by providing light. The dark is my domain and it is utter folly of it to even try to resist me. This charm has Witness to Darkness as its prerequisite and allows me to extend my anima to obscure any lightsource that is not sunlight and force anyone opposing me to fight me in the dark - with all the external penalties that implies.<br /> <br /> next up: Dream-Denying Affection</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/537-the-ebon-dragon","name":"The Ebon Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar537_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T07:32:06-07:00","id":164820,"title":"","content":"Dream-Denying Affection <br /> <br /> This charm expands the Quicksliver Dreams Siderial Martial Art. While in this charm is active, the character inflicts aggregated damage against Fae and creatures of the Wyld. Additionally, the character can reflexively engage in a contested Essence roll against anyone crafting illusions or using other charms in this martial arts. On success, the charm which powers the illusion or action is cancelled, and any motes spent are lost. Finally, the character can choose to inflict damage against a character's Virtues (1 dot per wound level), Intimacies (10 wound levels), or Motivation (30 wound levels) instead of their health track. Virtue dots lost in this manner return at a rate of one dot per day. Intimacies and Motivations are lost forever.<br /> <br /> Next up: Infinite Blooming Lotus Perfection","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> This one is for all my Exigents...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/102-lordwyrmsbane","name":"LordWyrmsBane","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T08:26:15-07:00","id":164849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordWyrmsBane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=164820#post164820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Infinite Blooming Lotus Perfection</div> </div> </div> </div>Prerequisites: Essence 6, Martial Arts 6, Mastery of one Sidereal Martial Art. <br /> <br /> Not for nothing are the Viziers acknowledged as the ultimate masters of martial arts. What they master, they can cultivate anew, for their enlightenment is without end. The Sidereal can invent new Charms for Terrestrial and Celestial Martial Arts styles she has mastered as though they were native Hero styles. She may teach these Charms only to those that also know Infinite Blooming Lotus Perfection. <br /> <br /> Next: Salamander Basks In Strife.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T08:56:22-07:00","id":164855,"title":"","content":"<b>Salamander Basks In Strife</b><br /> Type: Terrestrial<br /> Ability: Socialize<br /> The Dragon Blooded knows that only together they can rule- and so, by dividing their enemies, they would fall. This charm allows them just that- by whispering to some people in the same group, they can easily create or awaken disagreements while remaining unknown. A whisper here, a small talk there, and before everyone can notice- the once soil group breaks apart, becoming an easy prey for the united troupes of the Dynasts.<br /> <br /> Next: Soul Bending Shadow Mockery","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T11:06:04-07:00","id":164955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=164855#post164855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b> Soul Bending Shadow Mockery</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Infernal Charm, Socialize, Ebon Dragon,<br /> <br /> The Ebon Dragon is a creature of opposition, of denying a person his victories, his glories, and his passions. This Charm lets you weaken or diminish an intimacy a person has towards something that this person can do, by mocking them for doing it.<br /> <br /> Yes, Ebon Dragon makes you stop doing things by making you ashamed of doing them, because he's a smallminded dick.<br /> <br /> Next Charm: Murder of Crows Assumption","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T11:32:44-07:00","id":164969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=164955#post164955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Murder of Crows Assumption</div> </div> </div> </div>Raksha Assumption Charm<br /> Prerequisite: Assumption of Cerements and Bone, Wonderland Infliction<br /> <br /> This charm upgrades Assumption of the Wyld-Tainted Land and allows the Raksha to appear as a Shadowland in Creation. A second purchase allows for a path to Labyrinth to appear inside the affected land. When used in an Oneironmancy, usually along with Assumption of Cerements and Bone, it usually takes the form of an group of slaughtered animals.<br /> <br /> New Charm: Blurring of Charcoal Lines","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1g_IC644YJoiVAm6ngqcBmsQtff2YYtd3pDbZpaOxx4o\" target=\"_blank\">My Exalted Character Creation Tool may be downloaded here.</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1086797-demac-s-exalted-character-creation-tool\" target=\"_blank\">The thread talking about the tool can be found here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1136654-exalted-seats-of-power\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted: Seats of Power is a homebrewed manse creation system.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1oaq3wk7lJKZ022SUA4iPfGzMpmBTNXlM\" target=\"_blank\">I have a rewrite of the craft system which can be downloaded here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1070312-i-got-my-book-it-s-super-fancy-and-i-can-t-read-the-cover/page2\" target=\"_blank\">I like the Mesoamerican look</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2346-demac","name":"Demac","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T12:09:44-07:00","id":165008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=164849#post164849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sidereal can invent new Charms for Terrestrial and Celestial Martial Arts styles she has mastered as though they were native Hero styles.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bSo because its a sidereal, they still can't make new charms <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> /snark","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1414-pyrosorc","name":"Pyrosorc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T12:19:23-07:00","id":165015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=164969#post164969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Raksha Assumption Charm<br /> Prerequisite: Assumption of Cerements and Bone, Wonderland Infliction<br /> <br /> This charm upgrades Assumption of the Wyld-Tainted Land and allows the Raksha to appear as a Shadowland in Creation. A second purchase allows for a path to Labyrinth to appear inside the affected land. When used in an Oneironmancy, usually along with Assumption of Cerements and Bone, it usually takes the form of an group of slaughtered animals.<br /> <br /> New Charm: Blurring of Charcoal Lines</div> </div> </div> </div>Terrestrial Linguistics Charms:<br /> <br /> The Prince of the Earth's mandate is written into the world, even when the world does not know it. This charm allows the character to use existing laws or literature, any written information commonly accepted or approved of, as grounds for their own argument no matter how inappropriate.<br /> <br /> New Charm: When the Great Dao Declined","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T13:48:37-07:00","id":165111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=165015#post165015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> New Charm: When the Great Dao Declined</div> </div> </div> </div>Getimian Charm - Through a powerful control of self and their own destiny a Getimian becomes capable of miraculous feats. When this Charm is activated out of a Getimian's yang mote pool the Charm may help deflect an incoming attack from close range by establishing that the Getimian's destiny to live through this moment is greater then the attacker's destiny to slay him. When this charm is spent out of the yin mote pool and the Getimian makes a close range attack with a bladed weapon his destiny speeds the blade towards its target greatly increasing the attacks damage. <br /> \u200bNew Charm - Blinded by Rage Vendetta <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/777-bronze-tiger","name":"Bronze Tiger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T18:09:39-07:00","id":165458,"title":"","content":"<b>Blinded By Rage Vendetta</b> is a Malfeas charm that gives the user hyperfocused tunnel-vision on a single entity who has harmed or insulted him in that scene. Upgrades at higher essence can extend the window of use. It gives him significant bonuses in combat against that individual... and equally significant penalties against everyone else.<br /> <br /> Next charm: Mining the Heart of Gold Technique.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T19:19:20-07:00","id":165522,"title":"","content":"<b>Mining the Heart of Gold Technique</b> <br /> Infernal Fiend Charm - This charm enhances a social influence action against a target who has a positive intimacy towards the Infernal. If the influence action would benefit from such an intimacy, the intimacy is treated as one grade higher (Minor - Major - Defining). In addition, if the influence is successful, one of the target's other positive intimacies is downgraded by one level. If the target has no other positive intimacies then the Exalt may choose to upgrade one of their negative intimacies instead. The Fiend may not affect intimacies stronger than the one the target has for the Fiend (however, this is including the tier upgrade granted by the charm). <br /> <br /> New Charm - Shadows Cast in Ash","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/242-mindworm-jim","name":"Mindworm Jim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar242_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T20:33:53-07:00","id":165581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mindworm Jim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=165522#post165522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shadows Cast in Ash</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Infernal Thrown</b> (Ebon Dragon-flavored)<br /> Upon causing the destruction of something or the death of someone, the Infernal may activate this Charm to take the shadow of the thing destroyed into her own. She may save (Thrown) such shadows in this way. At some point in the future, she may pay X motes to shoot her anima through with darkness from such a shadow. Within these shards of murk, most see nothing, but anyone with a positive Intimacy for the shadow's former owner watches the death or destruction play out in excruciating detail. Provided she can perceive them, the Infernal immediately becomes aware of all such individuals, the relevant Intimacies, their contexts, and degrees.<br /> <br /> The Infernal has already pierced the target's heart: the actual attack is just a formality. For the rest of the scene, when the Infernal throws projectiles from her shadow with &lt;prerequisite Charm&gt; at any so affected, her target's (some sort of defense/momentum) is reduced by (progressively more, depending on grade of Intimacy). If the target was previously unaware of the death or destruction of the subject of that Intimacy, treat the Intimacy as being one grade higher than it was for all purposes until the end of the scene. The shadowy projectiles vanish as they typically do, but leave an ashy smear wherever they strike, requiring extensive scrubbing to remove.<br /> <br /> A given shadow may only be used once in a given story.<br /> <br /> New Charm: Firmament-Shattering Roar","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":". 06-10-2014, 11:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T21:00:36-07:00","id":165588,"title":"","content":"<b>Firmament-Shattering Roar</b><b>:</b> Lunar Strength, possibly Elder, or maybe just Ess 5. An upgrade of Lion's Roar Rebuke, it allows the Lunar to roar so loudly that they actually crack the foundations of the world. The area around the Lunar is treated as one step more &quot;Wyld.&quot; It is stackable, though the terrain decays back to its default state at the rate of one step per scene. As a side effect, any creature within the radius has to roll Stamina + Resistance or go deaf (one scene for supernaturals, permanent for mortals).<br /> <br /> New Charm: Riding the Steel Horse","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T01:39:05-07:00","id":165731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WarDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=165588#post165588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[B]New Charm: Riding the Steel Horse</div> </div> </div> </div>Solar Bureaucracy<br /> <br /> The Lawgiver, so sharp is her tongue, convinces a target that the purchase of an otherwise useless item will benefit them in untold useful ways. This was famously used, and thus named, to sell an entire nation matching sets of armor for their horses. They were the only inhabitants of their island.<br /> <br /> Caul-Rending Verse","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Formerly Exodan","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/715-foorish-shamurai","name":"Foorish Shamurai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar715_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T08:19:18-07:00","id":165935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Foorish Shamurai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=165731#post165731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Caul-Rending Verse</div> </div> </div> </div>Abyssal Performance. The deathknight sings out between the boundaries of the living and dead, calling ghosts under the sway of a powerful emotion\u2014sorrow, regret, rage\u2014into Creation as ecstastic phantasms that dance in her anima. <br /> <br /> Grass-Growing Contemplation","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T08:31:42-07:00","id":165956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=165935#post165935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Grass-Growing Contemplation</div> </div> </div> </div>Dragon-Blooded Wood Aspect Investigation. Terrestrials use this Charm to discern the slowest, subtlest patterns at work in the world, aiding in uncovering evidence of not-yet-resolved issues.<br /> <br /> Ten-Thousand Tooth Replenishment","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T15:48:58-07:00","id":166299,"title":"","content":"<b>Ten-Thousand Tooth Replenishment</b><br /> <br /> A submodule for a common Municipal Factory Charm, originally developed by the Orichalcum Caste Metropolis Stalwart Exponent of Industry. It enables the manufacture of many of the gears, cogs, and flywheels that make up so much of the Great Maker's world-body. In times of strife, it can be retooled to also produce gyroscopic chakrams. At least 150 lever-pullers, foundrymen, and line workers are needed to sustain production.<br /> <br /> Valiant Blood-Stone Vajrayana","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Playing 3e and miss Anathema? Try my web app, <a href=\"https://www.lotcastingatemi.com\" target=\"_blank\">Lot-Casting Atemi</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/553-hushnowquietnow","name":"hushnowquietnow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar553_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T16:34:33-07:00","id":166330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hushnowquietnow</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=166299#post166299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Valiant Blood-Stone Vajrayana</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Raksha Sword</b><br /> Though Creation wears down upon all Princes of Chaos in its midst, some have found relief through religion. Specifically, pilfering the religion of others. This Charm may supplement a raksha's efforts to introduce new rites, implements, and other rituals into the existing worship of Creation-born. When these rituals become a prominent feature of their worship, the prayers they issue reach not their intended target, but the raksha, who likewise acquires any appropriate dots in Cult.<br /> <br /> As an additional benefit, should any of the new rituals clearly promote the death of a Creation-born, a stone of blood will appear on the raksha's person. This object will protect the raksha from Creation's ill effects (as a Cyst/Pennant...?), though it will degrade after a number of months equal to the Essence of the deceased, not to exceed the raksha's Heart Grace. The death of an Exalt counts as though that Exalt was 1 higher in Essence and ignores any limit from the Heart Grace. This blood-stone possesses no supernatural protection against being destroyed like an ordinary rock and the raksha cannot reflexively dismiss it from his person. The raksha may willingly crush it to recover a number of health levels equal to the deceased's functional Essence. A raksha may possess only one such blood-stone at a time.<br /> <br /> New Charm: Beasts From Gluttons Revelation","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T18:44:01-07:00","id":166430,"title":"","content":"Beasts From Gluttons Revelation: Is an Ebon Dragon charm that expands on sorcerous activations of Want Becomes Need. During the activation of the former, the Infernal may choose to spend 1ahl to enhance the effect. Every time the victim of this charm indulges in the targeted act they must roll temperance at difficulty 2. Failure earns them a single point of mutation with aesthetics appropriate to their particular addiction. Those who suffer more mutation points this way than their willpower+the sum of their virtues are transformed into strange beasts that no longer resemble or count as human. Their motivation becomes to indulge in the behavior targeted with Want Becomes Need and they have an intimacy of hateful subservience to the infernal. Only removing the effect of Want becomes need may end this charm.<br /> <br /> New Charm: Prana Crafting Prana Methodology Technique","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2944-shadell","name":"Shadell","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T18:54:17-07:00","id":166434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=166430#post166430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New Charm: Prana Crafting Prana Methodology Technique</div> </div> </div> </div>Solar Linguistics. Using his extensive vocabulary and mastery of syntactic structure, the Solar is able to derail a conversation through endless babble that sounds meaningful and smart, leaving all others to ashamed to call him out for his jargon-laden spiel.<br /> <br /> Honey and Vinegar Realty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T19:07:16-07:00","id":166441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=166434#post166434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honey and Vinegar Realty.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wood Aspect, Bureaucracy.<br /> <br /> The administrators of the Realm deftly control the flow of favourable and unfavourable projects, managing their patricians' less sophisticated ideas on running business in their house through applications of Honey and Vinegar Realty. Random accidents, unforseen delays and inconveniences that seem indisputable slow down some projects, while others find fortune in circumstance, a ready hand to speed things along and surplus funds appearing just in time.<br /> <br /> Placating Iron Gesture","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/921-malovich","name":"Malovich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar921_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T19:10:37-07:00","id":166443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=166434#post166434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honey and Vinegar Realty.</div> </div> </div> </div>Raksha charm: Drastically increases the difficulty of disbelieving glamours by weaving petty discomforts and acclimatizing banality to cloak the dreamlike wonder of the true design.<br /> <br /> New Charm: Brotherhood is More Than Blood","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T21:10:37-07:00","id":166516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=166443#post166443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New Charm: Brotherhood is More Than Blood</div> </div> </div> </div>Terrestrial Integrity: The Exalt reinforces the Intimacy between himself and those he cares about; for the cost of a bashing Health Level, he may treat them as related to himself for a scene, in whatever manner might be appropriate to target them with the Dynasty effects of a charm.<br /> <br /> Cloak of Embers and Ash","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T21:45:33-07:00","id":166617,"title":"","content":"Placating Iron Gesture: Spirit Charm, Accept the authority of another to bring their social, physical, or organizational attack to an end.<br /> <br /> Cloak of Embers and Ash: Terrestrial Circle Spell, set yourself on fire and replace your skin and clothing with effigies of ash and charred wood to disguise your appearance and become resistant to extreme heats.<br /> <br /> New Charm: Winter is Coming","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T00:55:31-07:00","id":166701,"title":"","content":"<b>Winter is Coming </b><br /> Abyssal Awareness. Permanent. Can only be learned by a Deathknight who has survived a beheading (through the power of their Charms, at the moment of their Exaltation, by the timeless turns of Fate, etc.). It grants them a great and abiding clarity regarding a single great impending threat that targets one of their Intimacies. Visions of the future etch themselves into their mind while they sleep, allowing them to attempt to witness and investigate events to which they are not party so long as they closely relate to this threat.<br /> <br /> This vision cannot turn inward. If their hearts are cold and forsaken and have no remaining Intimacies to safeguard, or if the deathknight <i>is</i> the single greatest impending threat to their Intimacies, they become listless and unaware of the threat they themselves pose, taking a penalty on actions to notice and investigate the ruin they themselves have brought. People they once cared for may be hanged, betrayed or slaughtered, and lands they once ruled may fall into ruin, but what does that matter? Winter is Coming.<br /> <br /> Solar Rodent Form","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","user":"Guancyto","date":". 06-12-2014, 03:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","name":"Guancyto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T01:23:19-07:00","id":166703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Guancyto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=166701#post166701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solar Rodent Form</div> </div> </div> </div>Solar Rodent Form: Solar Stealth. The Mice of the Sun are the favored animals of the Unconquered Sun himself, and the Rodents of Light have much to teach a champion who would walk unseen. To a student of the Chosen Mice, even the slightest overlooked potential entry point becomes a castle gate thrown wide open. This charm supplements a Lawgivers stealth actions, aiding him in finding small crawlspaces, cracks just wide enough to fit through, and windows left ever so slightly ajar.<br /> <br /> New Charm: Lightning in a Bottle Revelation","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T02:29:12-07:00","id":166752,"title":"","content":"Lightning in a Bottle Revelation: A Solar who uses this charm can instantly and correctly answer any question they choose to contemplate.<br /> <br /> New Charm: Cherry Blossoms Blooming","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2551-lucil","name":"Lucil","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T18:25:02-07:00","id":167414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lucil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=166752#post166752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New Charm: Cherry Blossoms Blooming</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Terrestrial Performance</b> (Wood-focused, but general)<br /> Displaying grace, skill, and self-mastery, the Dragon-Blooded enhances a Performance roll by flaring her anima to its fullest for up to several seconds, before dropping it to its original level. Her anima can inflict no damage to anything during this time, becoming not a weapon for the flesh but a feast for the senses. This may take any pleasing form, such as the blossoming of a magnificently perfumed bouquet or a grand stone statue of Pasiap or the Imperial Mountain, the crack and still life of a lightning strike or bonfire, or a brief, sweet elegy on the wind. All who perceive it find the display breathtaking, granting the Terrestrial &lt;benefit&gt;. Though its greatest beauty is brief, any minor pleasant reminders it produces, such as the scent and sight of flower petals, a sweet smoke of incense or a faint echo, provide the Terrestrial &lt;minor benefit&gt; on social rolls with anyone who witnessed the initial display for the rest of the scene (and the next, if Cherry Blossoms Blooming was used near the end of the scene).<br /> <br /> Some Chosen of the Dragons sacrifice art for more practical ends. While the great display remains just as beautiful, the Terrestrial maximizes the remnants it leaves at the expense of graceful restraint. The great clouds of overbearingly scented blossom petals, dust, or smoke cost the performer any benefit, and may even earn penalties, with those whose tastes favor refinement or with art forms intrinsically dependent on such during and after the display, though those interested in spectacle may appreciate it just as much or more. However, these reminders are now substantial enough to provide &lt;benefit&gt; to Stealth actions in the area against the senses they affect. In particular, if these reminders target a sense of smell, all rolls dependent upon that sense automatically fail (or go to Charm roll off). Wyld Hunts have found this talent to be of particular use against a common advantage among the Lunar Anathema.<br /> <br /> New Charm: Tiger-Hearted Kitten Prana","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":". 06-12-2014, 09:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T18:42:36-07:00","id":167419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=167414#post167414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> New Charm: Tiger-Hearted Kitten Prana</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunar Knack, building out of Tyrant Mouse Dominion. Access the physical traits of one of the larger animals in your Heart's Blood library while in a smaller form, with a certain restrictions on the disparity in size. Who would expect a common city pigeon to swoop down with and fly away with a man clutched in its gross-looking toe talons like the dreaded strix of the wilderness?<br /> <br /> Methaumatic Reactor Core","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T19:10:20-07:00","id":167425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=167419#post167419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunar Knack, building out of Tyrant Mouse Dominion. Access the physical traits of one of the larger animals in your Heart's Blood library while in a smaller form, with a certain restrictions on the disparity in size. Who would expect a common city pigeon to swoop down with and fly away with a man clutched in its gross-looking toe talons like the dreaded strix of the wilderness?</div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> no one ever suspects... the BUTTERFLY mwahahahahaha<br /> <img src=\"http://31.media.tumblr.com/tumblr_l5f5skDuKn1qzh1pao1_400.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=167419#post167419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Methaumatic Reactor Core</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Solar Circle Sorcery</b> - Summons into being a Forge-cauldron that bubbles with a mix of liquid sunlight, ambrosia and a spark of wyld energies. It allows the creation of exceptionally improbable magical beings and artifacts by easing the fusion of anything submerged within it (creating a Tiger with Gossamer-Soulsteel flesh and the mind of a Dragon-blooded General, for example).<br /> \u200bIt also allows the infusion of magical powers.<br /> <br /> Things it creates are absolutely real and come with their own destinies and souls. (or a fusion of those of their constituents if provided)<br /> <br /> All Worlds Are One Hyperbole.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 06-12-2014, 10:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T19:22:27-07:00","id":167428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=167419#post167419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Methaumatic Reactor Core</div> </div> </div> </div>Alchemical Intelligence charm that allows you to inset an Elemental Core to get a mote discount on Protocols.<br /> With a submodule you can drain it for an instant casting.<br /> <br /> New Charm: Never Before, Never Again<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/782-lafing-cat","name":"Lafing Cat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T21:35:57-07:00","id":167553,"title":"","content":"Guess I got a two-fer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=167425#post167425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All Worlds Are One Hyperbole.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Lunar Manipulation</b><br /> The wiles of Luna's Chosen render even the preposterous both credible and obvious. This Charm supplements an attempt to persuade someone of a ridiculous lie, even in the face of direct evidence. So long as the Lunar provides some form of rationale, even one that makes sense only through the logic of metaphor or dream, the lie weaves together a new world for the target to perceive. This may include helping a guard understand that the reason it's a little hot today is that the entire village is actually on fire, or that the ruling lady just needs to look a little closer at her right-hand man to see that the reason for his loyalty is that he's a literal dog.<br /> <br /> The target will be baffled at the inability to see this obvious truth before, but will proceed to treat the world as though what is seen is perceived is the truth. If the guard shouts to people about fire, he may need to strain to hear their confused replies over the crackling blaze, while the ruling lady may note to her man that she never realized he was a dog, she will hear plaintive barks and whines instead of his flustered attempts to point out his humanity. When confronted with evidence of the categorical falsehood -- evidence that the target can perceive, at any rate -- the target may roll again with a bonus to disbelieve it against the original difficulty. The guard may find it odd that the fire does not burn him nor do the people walking through it seem bothered, and the lady may rethink herself if someone else points out the poor man's humanity to her. The target receives a bonus on this roll, which gradually increases as inconsistencies mount.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lafing Cat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=167428#post167428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New Charm: Never Before, Never Again</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Infernal (Abyssal?) Integrity</b><br /> Wrapping a hand around a chosen Tie, the Warlock wrenches it free from his heart and grinds it to nothing in his hand. It disappears like dust on the wind, and takes with it all memory of the Intimacy's subject. All the Green Sun Prince's memories rewrite and reorder themselves to account for this. Mark the Intimacy, as the Infernal no longer possesses it for normal purposes. Still, the hole in his heart remains, and seeks to protect itself from being filled. The Infernal functionally now possesses a Bond, at the same degree of the Tie, to prevent himself from reacquiring or being reminded of the old Intimacy. The Infernal may see or become aware of or be reminded of the subject of the Tie, so long as the original context is not referenced, and may form a new Bond to the subject, so long as the context differs meaningfully from the original context.<br /> <br /> New Charm: Rain of Blue Miracles","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Tweaks, here and there. Also, now unsure about Infernal or Abyssal for the second Charm, but still leaning Infernal. 06-13-2014, 12:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T05:57:59-07:00","id":167795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=167553#post167553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New Charm: Rain of Blue Miracles</div> </div> </div> </div>Exigent of Plentimon charm: When losing any sort of gambit (anything from &quot;guess what number I'm thinking of, between 1 and 3&quot; to a stock market investment that has taken years to come to term ) curse the person or unit most directly responsible for said loss with a streak of minor fortunes and miracles for as long as the motes remain commited; Once the commitment is released, the charm culminates in a tragedy that takes away all given fortunes and makes the target worse off than before.<br /> (if the luck streak makes the target win money and earn the respect of a superior officer, the culmination would be an event that takes all of that away and creates circomstances that cause the target to be forsaken entirely by said superior and potentially the entire organisation.)<br /> <br /> New Charm: Optimizing the Fragmented Narrative (or: Optimizing the Fragmented Script, at your discretion)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 06-13-2014, 09:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T06:38:36-07:00","id":167832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=167419#post167419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunar Knack, building out of Tyrant Mouse Dominion. Access the physical traits of one of the larger animals in your Heart's Blood library while in a smaller form, with a certain restrictions on the disparity in size. Who would expect a common city pigeon to swoop down with and fly away with a man clutched in its gross-looking toe talons like the dreaded strix of the wilderness?<br /> Methaumatic Reactor Core</div> </div> </div> </div>Or having a cat send a grown man to the hospital for 5 days and $16,000 hospital bill. Oh wait, that was in real life, bad example.<br /> <br /> By the way Vance, who is that guy behind you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>while (horse.state == dead)<br /> {<br /> beat();<br /> }","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/830-amdramnar","name":"Amdramnar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T10:16:06-07:00","id":168040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amdramnar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=167832#post167832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way Vance, who is that guy behind you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereal Stealth charm, with Duck Fate as a pre-requisite; Force a scene-change, ending any scne-long effects as you shift the focus of the current event to a new target. Fate itself helps you in this by giving the target of By the Way Vance, Who is That Guy Behind You? a grand entrance that gives a die bonus equal to the Sidereal's Essence to any social roll made for the grand entrace to grab attention.<br /> <br /> (yes, I know this wasn't part of the forum game :P )","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T12:48:13-07:00","id":168209,"title":"","content":"<b>Optimizing the Fragmented Narrative</b><br /> <br /> Sidereal investigation. The Chosen of the Stars, upon hearing incoherent and differing recounts of the same event, chooses the interpretation she deems worthy of being true. Through her will, Fate works to make it so. Events arrange in such a way as to make this version widely accepted and most plausible. Evidence will surface to lend credence to the Sidereal's vision.<br /> <br /> New Charm: Memories of Gross Incandescence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T12:57:33-07:00","id":168218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=168209#post168209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Optimizing the Fragmented Narrative</b><br /> <br /> Sidereal investigation. The Chosen of the Stars, upon hearing incoherent and differing recounts of the same event, chooses the interpretation she deems worthy of being true. Through her will, Fate works to make it so. Events arrange in such a way as to make this version widely accepted and most plausible. Evidence will surface to lend credence to the Sidereal's vision.<br /> <br /> New Charm: Memories of Gross Incandescence.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's one way to solve a Rashomon problem.<br /> <br /> <b>Memories of Gross Incandesence</b><br /> Solar Performance. A Chosen of the Sun knows how to make an impression. The Solar can activate this charm during a scene, and for the duration of the scene afterwards everyone who witnesses the Solar's actions will be able to perfectly remember what they said, what they did, and how they did it, automatically succeeding on any memory tests related to them.<br /> <br /> Next - Thirsty Water Method","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T13:53:32-07:00","id":168242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=168218#post168218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Next - Thirsty Water Method</div> </div> </div> </div>Terrestrial Bureaucracy<br /> The Dragon-Blooded knows that to drink of the sea only deepens the thirst. Using this charm, the Terrestrial picks an intimacy of his target. As long as his social influence plays to that intimacy, the target cannot dull herself to its appeal--she may still resist the influence as normal, but requires the expenditure of extra willpower point toward each social attack to deaden herself to its influence for the rest of the scene.<br /> <br /> Next: Shadows Fall Like Hammers<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T15:36:38-07:00","id":168312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=168242#post168242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Next: Shadows Fall Like Hammers</div> </div> </div> </div>Solar Dodge. The Iron Wolves do not take kindly to being attacked. For the rest of the scene, the Solar gets a Counterattack on any enemy that attacks her. She flares briefly with light, shadows dancing, striking at the enemy with automatic Knockback.<br /> <br /> Next: Exalted Hero Form","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T16:06:25-07:00","id":168346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Limited Reagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=168312#post168312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solar Dodge. The Iron Wolves do not take kindly to being attacked. For the rest of the scene, the Solar gets a Counterattack on any enemy that attacks her. She flares briefly with light, shadows dancing, striking at the enemy with automatic Knockback.<br /> <br /> Next: Exalted Hero Form</div> </div> </div> </div>Raksha Ishvara charm - the Raksha's narrative becomes so strong and compelling that it's essence coagulates into something resembling an exigent exaltation. This allows the Raksha to learn a new set of charms as though it was an exigent. The Raksha loses the ability to shape itself back to life - any demise is permanent outside of shaping combat, however her narrative remains, persisting long enough to endow a suitable host with it's powers (if human, the new host becomes a Fae-Blooded who possesses and owns all for of her own graces). This charm must be learned again if the new host wishes to pass on his powers in a similar fashion.<br /> <br /> \u200bnew charm: Blood of wine, bones of salt","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 06-13-2014, 07:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T21:19:39-07:00","id":168589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=168346#post168346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blood of wine, bones of salt</div> </div> </div> </div>Metagaos consumes everything, there is no reason his dead brothers and sisters should be an exception to this fact. Whenever the Infernal kills a Creature of Dead, all of his actions on the following tick have their Speed reduce by two, as long as the target is another Creature of Dead.<br /> <br /> Five-Hundred Arhats Murderous Pilgrimage<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T13:28:38-07:00","id":169201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=168589#post168589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Five-Hundred Arhats Murderous Pilgrimage</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Raksha Sword</b><br /> Despite their appetites, the Fair Folk can recognize some in greater need of Valor than they. In moments of pity, they may grant this. When feeding on a Creation-born's Valor, the raksha gains no motes, Willpower or gossamer. The Prince of Chaos instead takes this Valor into the kiln of her Sword, alloys it with gossamer, and returns it. In this way can the Creation-born become enlightened beyond the heights of mortal Valor.<br /> <br /> The Creation-born's Valor is treated as though it is 5 dots higher, ignoring the 5-dot limit, for all purposes other than channeling his Valor to enhance an action or any other effects for which it presents a clear benefit (higher mote pools, a Charm granting bonus dice equal to it, etc.), all of which use his original Valor. The first exception is a Valor roll to resist fleeing combat. The second is that the character may use this inflated Valor to retain Willpower when resting, but only in any day the character faces at least one Valor roll and spends no Willpower to resist successes on any such rolls. The character's skill in war and battle become more resilient, and she may reduce any internal penalties to such action by 1, to a minimum of 0.<br /> <br /> All social rolls from others meant to curb violent action are automatically resisted by the afflicted with a bonus of half his inflated Valor, while all social rolls to promote violent action may be resisted only with an equal penalty. No raksha may feed on this tainted Valor. The effect ends only when other effects reduce the target's 5 &quot;artificial&quot; Valor. Many in the threshold have lived in fear of raksha lords with bands of these rage-kissed, mortal warriors with souls drunk empty of all but fey-touched Valor.<br /> <br /> Similar Charms exist for the other Virtues.<br /> <br /> New Charm: Wheels Within Wheels, Worlds Within Worlds","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":". 06-14-2014, 04:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T07:12:33-07:00","id":170685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=169201#post169201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New Charm: Wheels Within Wheels, Worlds Within Worlds</div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereal Bureacracy<br /> <br /> There is no greater trap than the illusion of progress. When any character is interacting with a organization of which the Sidereal is an active member, they can be targeted with this charm. All of their social attacks on members of the organization will be redirected in such a way as to make it appear that they have succeeded, but without actually having any effect. Use cases of this charm include:<br /> * A member of the organization is trying to gain a promotion. Their &quot;successful&quot; performance or socialize checks get them transferred to another position with the same amount of influence and pay.<br /> * An investigator is trying to get information about the organization. Their &quot;successful&quot; investigation checks lead them in a circle, with responsibility for providing information or making decisions constantly being passed from person to person, department to department.<br /> * The leader of the organization wants to restructure it. Their &quot;successful&quot; bureaucracy check changes everyone's titles and positions, but everyone still answers to everyone else in the same hierarchy they had and performs the same duties they had before the shift.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Ignoble </i><i>Varlet's Promise</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T08:05:42-07:00","id":170755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=170685#post170685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Ignoble </i><i>Varlet's Promise</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereal Larceny/Astrology<br /> <br /> The Sidereal, taking the role of a minor functionary or servant of a target, borrows an object from somebody under a vaguely worded oath, such as 'I'll take care of it while you're away' or 'It'll be in the parking lot when you wish to leave,&quot; or even 'Not a scratch.' The target must roll P+Investigation versus the Sidereal's Essence+Larceny, or else willingly part with the object. Note that, while the Sidereal is under no real obligation to keep his word, any attempt to actually adhere to the terms of the promise yield a 3-die bonus to the use of the 'borrowed' object.<br /> <br /> Edit: I like giving people choices.<i> Shadow Strangles Shadow Glare</i> or <i>More Wicked Than Thou.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":306,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","user":"Brasstreader","date":". 06-16-2014, 11:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T10:00:05-07:00","id":170829,"title":"","content":"More Wicked Than Thou<br /> <br /> Infernal Presence<br /> <br /> The servants of the Yozis laugh at your attempts to sway them with pain and fear. The Green Sun Prince doubles his successes on a roll made against an attempt at intimidation, torture or similar acts of violence meant to prey on the infernal's fears. Note that the Infernal's actual fears don't necessarily need to come into play, there simply needs to be an attempt. For instance, an Infernal who is locked in a cage with a swarm of wasps doesn't need to fear wasps to use this charm.<br /> <br /> I also like to give choices:<br /> Absolutely Absurd Warfare Method<br /> or<br /> Harem Master Endurance","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T10:26:05-07:00","id":170863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HalfTangible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=170829#post170829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Absolutely Absurd Warfare Method</div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereal War<br /> <br /> Confusion and deception are the bread and butter of a skilled general. With this charm, a Sidereal can disguise the attack patterns of a battle group he commands as something unbelievable or incomprehensible to observers for one scene. Opposing commanders trying to analyze the battle group's intentions automatically fail, allowing the Sidereal's fighters to take advantage of their flummoxed enemy. The effect ends if Sidereal's battle group fully engages with another battle group or flees.<br /> <br /> Since choices are apparently in vogue now, how about<b></b>:<br /> <i>Total Annihilation Tactics</i><br /> or<br /> <i>Lightning from a Clear Sky </i><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T11:36:36-07:00","id":170929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=170863#post170863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Total Annihilation Tactics</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Abyssal War<br /> <br /> It is one thing to defeat your enemies. It is another thing to kill your enemies. But to go one step beyond and destroy your enemy in every sense of the word, that is the way of the Abyssal, and the path of Oblivion.<br /> <br /> This charm can be activated when your army performs a slaughter. Once the slaughter is completed, all evidence that your battle took place dissapears. Corpses sink into the ground, the injuries of your allied heals and not even their ghosts return, all of it is swallowed by Oblivion. This makes it impossible to track down the location where this battle took place, or who were a part of it, loot their bodies for valuables, or do anything else related to the dead on this battlefield.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I liked the idea of the Slaughter action that is coming up in 3e, and this charm seems like a pretty useful thingy for people who want to go with a figure of dread.<br /> <br /> Anyway, choices are popular, let's give this a spin...<br /> <br /> <b>Cry of the Bloodspattered Raven</b><i>.</i><br /> or<br /> <b>Snake underneath Flower Greeting</b><br /> or<br /> <b>From Tender Sand to HardendStone</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T13:27:06-07:00","id":170994,"title":"","content":"From Tender Sand to Hardend Stone<br /> <br /> Dragon Blood - Resistance<br /> <br /> The armies of the Primordial War were like a wave of iron: implacable and unstoppable. A chosen with this charm active may pay 10 motes and 1 willpower to ignore health level penalties for one scene, and permanently gains 2 -0 health levels. If the player prefers, they may instead distribute these health levels per the Ox-Body Technique, but the willpower and mote cost does not change. A character may purchase this charm once for each dot of stamina or once for each dot of resistance (the player's choice).<br /> <br /> Choose:<br /> <i>The Silver Chair turns Black</i><br /> or<br /> <i>Glory-Eating Shadow</i> <i>Method</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T14:30:43-07:00","id":171046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HalfTangible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=170994#post170994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Silver Chair turns Black</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Lunar Appearance</b><br /> This Charm may only be mastered by a Lunar with a soul that calls out to an Abyssal companion (Defining Bond). A Chosen of Luna may reach into that connection to such a deathknight and draw out a fearsome power. If the moon hangs in the sky, it vanishes when the Lunar activates this Charm for Essence miles around, extinguishing its light and denying even Luna a glimpse of the proceedings.<br /> <br /> For the rest of the scene, the Lunar's anima and tattoos (if any) change to incorporate aspects of Abyssal power, and those of the chosen deathknight in particular. The Lunar may treat her anima banner as though it is an Abyssal one, and may also choose to use one of the Abyssal's Caste anima powers in place of one of her own.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">(EDIT: Eh, this seemed like one Charm trying to do too much, so I've simplified a little. The original text for that last paragraph is below. Its extra effects could be worth splitting up into multiple Charms. Could also help to do something with Necromancy, too, but that would depend on how the broader Sorcery system works out and interacts with Charms.)<br /> <br /> For the rest of the scene, the Lunar's anima and tattoos (if any) change to incorporate aspects of Abyssal power, and the chosen deathknight in particular. The Lunar may freely use such new aesthetics in stunting and may choose to treat it as an Abyssal's anima banner if she chooses. She may also choose to use one of the Abyssal's Caste anima powers in place of one of her own. When learning this Charm, the Lunar may design a variation of her Deadly Beastman Transformation to incorporate Merits and powers appropriate to a creature of death, which may be used only when this Charm is active. She may also select one of these chosen Merits/powers and reflexively apply it to any form she assumes.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Glorious Bandwagon-Hopping Maneuver!</b><br /> New Charm:<br /> <i>Ass in Lion's Skin Deceit</i><br /> or<br /> <i>Moored on Victory's Shoals</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  EDIT: Tweakery and simplification. 06-16-2014, 06:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T16:22:22-07:00","id":171163,"title":"","content":"<i>Ass in Lion's Skin Deceit</i><br /> <br /> Lunar Presence<br /> <br /> Many weaker beasts know the trick of surviving by taking the mien of a stronger animal. The Lunar can use this charm to supplement any social attack used to intimidate. The target of the social attack will become convinced that the Lunar will be able to make good on any threats they make, even if there is evidence suggesting that the Lunar is bluffing. They may still resist the attack, but they will not actually disbelieve it.<br /> <br /> Next round of choices:<br /> <i>Lightning From A Clear Sky<br /> Or<br /> Absolute Balance of Wealth</i><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T16:28:48-07:00","id":171172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=171163#post171163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Ass in Lion's Skin Deceit</i><br /> <b>Lightning From A Clear Sky</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Solar Athletics, requiring Mountain Crossing Leap Technique and Thunderbolt Attack Prana. This Charm allows the Solar to make an attack instead of simply landing from Mountain Crossing Leap Technique, crashing down upon her foes like a lightning bolt from a clear sky. The attack gains bonuses (of which I won't elaborate, since I'm lazy). This Charm also makes it so Mountain Crossing Leap Technique can be used in combat time; depending on the power of the jump, the Solar is in the air for a number of ticks; the more ticks in the air, the more powerful the attack upon landing.<br /> <br /> Next we can continue this weather-themed naming, and one appropriate for what is going on outside my window: <b>Watching the Rain Fall</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":263,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","user":"Limited Reagent","date":". 06-16-2014, 07:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T16:34:57-07:00","id":171176,"title":"","content":"Solar Dodge. Upon being targeted by more than one ranged attack in an action, the Solar flits back to safe cover from the source of the attacks.<br /> <br /> <b>Falling Star Renewal</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Once, there was a maiden... who spent all her time on the internet.<br /> &quot;Someone out there is WRONG,&quot; she said.<br /> So she tossed a noose made of golden light... and strangled her opponent.<br /> Both of them died alone.<br /> &quot;Love is for football players and cheerleaders,&quot; her obituary said.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/261-notthepenguins","name":"notthepenguins","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar261_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"359"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T17:03:27-07:00","id":171204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>notthepenguins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=171176#post171176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solar Dodge. Upon being targeted by more than one ranged attack in an action, the Solar flits back to safe cover from the source of the attacks.<br /> <br /> <b>Falling Star Renewal</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereal Bureaucracy. Nominate the heir to a destiny that would have gone unfulfilled via the death of another. Heaven treats the legend, and the rumor, of the fallen one and the new heir as interchangable.<br /> <br /> <i>Lift the Dragon High</i> or <i>Shattered Gate Assertion.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T17:04:31-07:00","id":171206,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">(Ninjaed)<br /> <br /> Falling Star Renewal - Sidereal Bureaucracy<br /> <br /> Sometimes a Sidereal must execute a god, but still requires a being to fulfill its role temporarily. In such cases, the Sidereal may put a replacement together from the remains. The Sidereal reforms a god that has been struck down in his presence within the last day. The god has 1 Essence for each point of willpower or for each 15 motes put into this charm, plus half of the user's dots in Bureaucracy (rounded down). The god remembers none of its previous existence, and bears a new intimacy for the Sidereal who performs the charm of absolute loyalty and obedience that remains for a year and a day. The god may lose the intimacy after this point, but should they lose the intimacy, the god dies once again.<br /> <br /> ...Bit dark that time. Let's pick a weather themed charm!</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Lift the Dragon High - Solar Occult<br /> <br /> On rare occasion, a Solar in the armies of the Primordials would have to gift a Dragon-Blood, Lunar or Sidereal with his own power to accomplish a task. The Solar gifts another Exalted all of his non-sorcery charms for one scene. The Exalted must pay at least 1 wp per charm used. (charms that already require willpower do not need to spend additional willpower. The Exalted also gains all permanent and reflexive charms, but does not require aforementioned spent willpower to use them. This charm can be extended to a full day, but requires all of the Solar's remaining Willpower and Motes to do so and must pay the minimum cost for a scene. As long as this charm is active, the Solar cannot use any granted charms. The Exalted targeted by this charm is treated like its own Exalt type unless the used charm requires the user to be a Solar.<br /> <br /> Rats on Stormy Tides<br /> or<br /> Lightning Covers the Cloudless Sky","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":879,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","user":"HalfTangible","date":". 06-16-2014, 08:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T17:29:22-07:00","id":171226,"title":"","content":"Lightning Covers the Cloudless Sky<br /> Dragon-Blooded Thrown<br /> <br /> An unexpected storm can sweep away the largest caravan in moments. The Children of Mela are no less dangerous. This charm supplements a Thrown attack, allowing it to strike multiple targets at once. The projectile can strike a number of foes up to the Dragon-Blooded's Essence, but can only target unaware characters.<br /> <br /> Anguished Umbral Echoes<br /> or<br /> Whispering Spirit Technique","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1168,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","user":"HobbitGuy1420","date":". 06-16-2014, 08:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T20:35:58-07:00","id":171342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HobbitGuy1420</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=171226#post171226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anguished Umbral Echoes</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Abyssal Presence</b><br /> The deathknight draws out the voice of one dearly departed to echo in the shadow of her speech. An eligible voice must have an owner the Abyssal knows to be dead and it must be a voice the Abyssal has heard before (whether before or after its owner's death). Any old voice produces an unnerving effect in the deathknight's delivery for &lt;some small bonus&gt; on a roll, but especially relevant voices can move hearts and shake souls. The bonus becomes &lt;something more&gt; if the voice's owner is relevant to the subject matter, one addressed has an Intimacy related to the voice's owner (one bonus per degree of Intimacy), or the Abyssal speaks meaningful words once spoken by the voice's owner. These bonuses stack.<br /> <br /> New Charm:<br /> <i>Sparrow Defies Heaven Meditation</i><br /> or<br /> <i>Silver-Haired Prince Form</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T21:20:33-07:00","id":171378,"title":"","content":"Sparrow Defies Heaven Meditation<br /> <br /> Sidereal - Awareness<br /> <br /> The Sidereal folds a prayer strip into a small paper bird. Written on the prayer strip is the name of the god or elemental this charm will target. Sitting calmly the Sidreals rythmic breathing matches the fluttering of the birds wings as it takes to the air, and seeks out its target passing unoticed into even the most closely guarded divine sanctums. While the Sidereal maintains their meditation they see as if through the eyes of the bird, gaining insight to the spirits movements and action in their most private sanctum.<br /> <br /> New Charm - Illuminated Valet Introduction","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T12:54:21-07:00","id":171925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=171378#post171378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sparrow Defies Heaven Meditation<br /> New Charm - Illuminated Valet Introduction</div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereal Ride Charm<br /> <br /> Convinces any person that the Sidereal is a responsible person to whom they can trust the care of their steed. The Sidereal is not obligated to live up to this expectation.<br /> <br /> New Charm: Song of Maledictions","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1g_IC644YJoiVAm6ngqcBmsQtff2YYtd3pDbZpaOxx4o\" target=\"_blank\">My Exalted Character Creation Tool may be downloaded here.</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1086797-demac-s-exalted-character-creation-tool\" target=\"_blank\">The thread talking about the tool can be found here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1136654-exalted-seats-of-power\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted: Seats of Power is a homebrewed manse creation system.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1oaq3wk7lJKZ022SUA4iPfGzMpmBTNXlM\" target=\"_blank\">I have a rewrite of the craft system which can be downloaded here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1070312-i-got-my-book-it-s-super-fancy-and-i-can-t-read-the-cover/page2\" target=\"_blank\">I like the Mesoamerican look</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2346-demac","name":"Demac","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T13:12:34-07:00","id":171934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=171925#post171925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New Charm: Song of Maledictions</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunar Manipulation Charm.<br /> <br /> You sing a song that twists the world against your target. Your target must hear the Song of Maledictions. For the next lunar month, or until you release the motes committed to the charm, they must spend 2 willpower instead of 1 in order to get an automatic success, and treat any failure in which they rolled no successes as a botch.<br /> <br /> New Charm: Easy Going Style<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T16:17:49-07:00","id":172129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=171934#post171934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New Charm: Easy Going Style</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Easy Going Style - Liminal Resistance<br /> <br /> For the chosen of the Dark Mother attachment to their bodies is at best fleeting, their flesh is a sculpture to be carved and shaped to fit their needs. Upon activating this charm the Liminal focuses upon a limb, or other discreet part of their body and decrees that it is no longer part of them. The body part falls away causing no trauma to the Liminal and leaving a gap receptive to graft and transplantation. The liminal may add (Wits+Resistance) dice to any roll to replace the limb so long as they leave the motes spent on this charm committed.<br /> <br /> New Charm: Infectious Pact Technique","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T16:43:05-07:00","id":172165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=172129#post172129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New Charm: Infectious Pact Technique</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Solar Bureaucracy</b><br /> <br /> Sometimes, a contract is not enough; and sometimes, signing it personally would mean exposing oneself too much. A solar can augment any successful contract, deal or bargain with this charm, such that the other party feels compelled to repeat this bargain again with someone other than the Solar, a number of times equal to the Solar's Bureaucracy. Once the target does so, the effect is copied onto any participants of that bargain, and the process begins anew a number of times equal to the Solar's essence, though the Solar can release commitment at any time and end the charm's cascading effect. When running it's full course, the maximum number of such deals is equal to [Bureaucracy ^ Essence].<br /> <br /> Any and all deals/bargains/contracts sealed this way bear some mark of the Solar (or are known to have been made by the Solar or in the Solar's name in case of verbal contracts) such that the solar can prove without the shadow of a doubt that the deal is officially in his name (any signature or seal made on the contract is exactly the Solar's, for example).<br /> <br /> A little-known feature of this charm is that it allows Eclipse-castes to Seal every such deal as though they had personally made it, though they must spend motes for their Anima Power every time.<br /> <br /> Legends tell of one Eclipse Caste buying up the nigh entirety of Nexus' opium supply using a single piece of gold, and collecting all the merchandise he legally owned a day later.<br /> \u200b<br /> New Charm: <b>Snaring the Sea Maneuver.</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 06-17-2014, 08:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T17:19:13-07:00","id":172195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=172165#post172165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New Charm: Snaring the Sea Maneuver.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dragon Blooded Sail:<br /> <br /> When invoked, the Dragonblood reaches out and plunges her anima into a body of water of sufficient size to qualify as a terrain feature. The water swells and suffuses the area around the dragonblood. As long as the charm is maintained, the Exalt leaves behind a trail of water drawn from the connected body of water with every motion. As he strides forward, he leaves behind a column of water tracing out his every motion, as she strikes a torrent of water slams into the target along with her punches. Mechanically, this adds +2 damage to all of the exalts close combat attacks, or allows an attack to be made with only the water itself out to yard. Treat the latter attack as a thrown attack having accuracy +0 and damage +2.<br /> <br /> An Essence 5 repurchase allows the dragonblood to invoke this charm in a mass combat setting, extending its effects to a unit of Magnitude (Essence/4). Each dragonblooded special character in the mass combat unit adds +1 to the users effective essence, or +2 if they possess the charm themselves, to a maximum total of magnitude Essence. In addition to the damage bonus extending to the entire unit, the Storyteller is well advised to consider the effects of that much water on a battlefield: A high magnitude unit under the effects of this charm could enable ships to sail behind them or to flood lower lying areas. Conversely, the dragonblood is advised to equip his troops to fight in a watery enviornment: While his troops suffer no ill effects from the water they produce on a given tick, water produced in past ticks affects them normally.<br /> <br /> Special: In order to use this charm, the Dragonblood must not suffer a surcharge on Water Aspect charms, either naturally, via mastering Water Dragon Style, or through the appropriate Transcendent Gaian Harmony.<br /> <br /> <br /> New Charm: Eclectic Kinetic Memetics","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/782-lafing-cat","name":"Lafing Cat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T18:49:31-07:00","id":172263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lafing Cat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=172195#post172195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> New Charm: Eclectic Kinetic Memetics</div> </div> </div> </div>Alchemical Enlightenment Charm. An Alchemical can use this Charm to awaken the Essence of a mortal, allowing them to learn Terrestrial Martial Arts.<br /> And Essence 5 upgrade allows them to teach the Celestial Martial Arts initiation charms to Dragonblooded.<br /> <br /> New Charm: One Man with a Dream","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T21:16:52-07:00","id":172349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=172263#post172263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New Charm: One Man with a Dream</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Sidereal Astrological Blessing</b> <b>of the Treasure Trove</b> (associated Ability: Lore)<br /> The Vizier selects a mortal and one of the Major or Defining Principles she knows he possesses. As the stars realign themselves for the coming destiny, the chosen mortal dreams of a world he finds most glorious. His heart is filled with a warm certainty it was made manifest through the pursuit of this Principle. The Sidereal may dictate a number of different features of the dream equal to her dots in the Treasure Trove College and can be sure the dreamer will remember.<br /> <br /> On waking, the mortal is moved to pursue this vision, and his Principle becomes Defining if it was not already. Reducing this Intimacy becomes more difficult for others, even through magic. When supplementing relevant social actions in favor of the relevant Principle with a description of the glorious vision, he becomes unusually artful and articulate, receiving a bonus. If he encounters something that reminds him of a feature the Sidereal placed in his dream, the sight will reignite his resolve. His Principle will increase by one degree if it had fallen, and for the rest of the scene the character may choose to use a one-time benefit on any action he takes in pursuit of the Principle and vision. Each such feature may only receive this benefit once.<br /> <br /> New Charm: King in Collar, Cat in Crown","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":". 06-18-2014, 12:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T21:44:11-07:00","id":172412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=172349#post172349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> New Charm: King in Collar, Cat in Crown</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunar Social Charm<br /> <br /> When a Lunar consumes the heartsblood of a creature more than just the form of the creature becomes part of the Lunar's being, fragments of that creatures intimacies remain as well. The Lunar may call upon one of these intimacies and shed a measure of blood, a potent potion of change. When this potion is given to another being with or without their knowledge it imbues in them the bestial intimacy it was created from. The King is driven by the panthers urge to attack the weak, the Priest feels the greed of the magpie, the General the all consuming fear of a Rabbit.<br /> <br /> New Charm - Image of Elemental Alteration","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T16:16:38-07:00","id":173294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=172412#post172412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> New Charm - Image of Elemental Alteration</div> </div> </div> </div>Dragonblooded Stealth Sometimes it is not enough for the Princes of the Earth to be unseen. Sometimes they must, in fact, be witnessed publicly - as something else. With this Charm, a Dragon-blooded may change their apparent elemental aspect. She may replace stony skin with bark-rippled patterns, her anima may roar with waves instead of the crackle of fires, and even Elemental effects of her Charms are disguised: though an Air Aspect's attack still gives a buffeting penalty, she may portray it as unseating her victim around with waves or pillars of stone.<br /> <br /> New Charm: If Fire Were Water OR Love Is For The Lonely","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T16:46:17-07:00","id":173329,"title":"","content":"edit: oops, I apparently hadn't reloaded in at least a half-hour.<br /> old one:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=172412#post172412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New Charm - Image of Elemental Alteration</div> </div> </div> </div>Raksha Name Charm, in the Assumption of Elemental Shape tree<br /> <br /> <br /> This charm permanently enhances Element Weaving Style such that her works become so poignant and compelling that Creation itself longs to change itself to better appeal to the Raksha. Whenever the Raksha works on a project using Element Weaving Style, including working on Elementals, she may add 5 to her target number and 1 to her difficulty to change that element (or that elemental) into any of the Elements the Raksha currently Assumes.<br /> <br /> For example, the raksha assuming Steel and Fire could craft a flame into a steel rapier, or a hachet into an inferno. Likewise, that raksha could craft an Earth elemental into a Fire elemental for the duration of the charm.<br /> <br /> With the expenditure of Gossamer, the work becomes a small miracle, so radiant that Elements around it want to transform themselves in the same way. Elements that stay within the work's vicinity long enough start going through the same transformations - candle flames might slowly turn to steel, all the swords in the village might spontaneously combust. This also applies to Elementals with an Essence score lower than the Raksha's.<br /> \u200b</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 06-19-2014, 07:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T07:48:59-07:00","id":174129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ellis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=173294#post173294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Fire Were Water</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunar Perception.<br /> <br /> &quot;That's a lake of crystal clear water, I'm sure of it&quot;, the silver eyes girl shout, pointing at the approaching stream of lava. Choosing an element that she can perceive and active this charm, a Nightwitch can treat the that element as another kind of element entirely. This will allow her to ignore any kind of penalties or damage come from the chosen element as blizzard turn into blossom rain under the the Lunar bewitched vision.<br /> <br /> Storm-Gathering Kagura<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T08:00:47-07:00","id":174136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=174129#post174129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Storm-Gathering Kagura</div> </div> </div> </div>Solar Performance. Putting on a play that depicts a political or moral allegory, the Solar subtly sows the seeds of rebellion and uprising in the hearts of her audience, fomenting a dramatic and violent outburst of riotous mass action that cannot be traced back to her thespian performance. <br /> <br /> Hundred Demons Curriculum","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T08:38:13-07:00","id":174164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=174136#post174136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hundred Demons Curriculum</div> </div> </div> </div>Infernal Occult. The Warlock is shown a brief image of the full hierarchy of Hell, and the image is burned into his mind forever. The warlock can now recognize any demon as a demon, even if it has disguised itself in any way, and knows its name, its functions and its customs. In addition, when it speaks, the demon can understand him, even if it's deaf, or doesnt speak the Warlock's tongue.<br /> <br /> Ten Thousand Whispers of the Hungry Maw.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T09:12:26-07:00","id":174186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=174164#post174164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ten Thousand Whispers of the Hungry Maw.</div> </div> </div> </div>Abyssal Performance: The Abyssal's words and music are a horror that drives men and women mad if they bring themselves to observe it; as long as he continues a performance, those who could hear him must either ignore his presence and actions or take on a derangement as his art flays their sanity. <br /> <br /> The Last Long Sunset.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T11:06:44-07:00","id":174290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=174186#post174186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The Last Long Sunset.</div> </div> </div> </div>Solar Resistance<br /> <br /> No matter how hard a hero fights, there will come a day when her sun must set in blood and tears. However, a hero does not leave her business unfinished. When a Solar with this Charm is about to die, her anima suddenly ignites into a blaze of glory, renewing her strength. The Solar gains [obscenely high number] Dying levels, and can act with no regard for wound penalties. However, this charm ends when either someone chips through all her levels or the scene ends, and when it does so the Dying levels disappear and any damage in them is transferred to her normal levels, probably killing her in the process. <br /> <br /> Crying For Corpses OR The Circle Turns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T11:27:38-07:00","id":174364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ellis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=174290#post174290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Circle Turns.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thaumaturgy (Geomancy?)<br /> <br /> Placing a (willing) dying elder and a newborn baby in a room purified with prayer, incense, funeral rites and birthday gifts, the thaumaturge insures the prosperity of both souls. The elder, accepting their passage onto the afterlife, lets go of their remaining lifetime and pass blissfully onto lethe, assured that their soul will rise to new heights with this last sacrifice. The Thaumaturge guides the energy releasd in this manner into the newborn, infusing it's body and fate with wisdom, experience and longevity. (This can take the form of extra experience points, direct attribute/ability dots, mutations, merits (such as Destiny or Lucky) and in some extremely rare cases, the infant rising to god-blooded status)<br /> <br /> New Charm: Belittled, Betrayed and Becoming (may add a noun, e.g. &quot;Spirit&quot;, &quot;Technique&quot;, &quot;Rebuke&quot;, &quot;Meditation&quot;, &quot;Prana&quot;, &quot;Strike&quot;, etc.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 06-19-2014, 03:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T16:14:27-07:00","id":174677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=174364#post174364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New Charm: <b>Belittled, Betrayed and Becoming</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereal Socialize, prereq Cash and Murder Games.<br /> <br /> This Charm is empowered by a moment in which the Sidereal causes one person to be put above another in a social context. This could be by an insult keenly felt, arrogant commands, humiliation, betrayal, or more. Subtle Seers may find ways to make others belittle each other; if the Sidereal had a hand in it, this Charm may still be used. The result is that the Exalt uses the sudden imbalance of fate to her own benefit, wrapping up the strands and swallowing it like a spider would its meal --- she gains a dot of temporary Appearance that lasts as long as the characters involved in the belittlement are still feeling its effects on their emotional states. The Storyteller is encouraged to have the temporary dot last at least a scene. This Charm is Stackable, but each stacked use must be a new form of belittlement.<br /> <br /> Next Charm:<b> Ravens of Thought and Memory</b><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T03:05:40-07:00","id":175104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Limited Reagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=174677#post174677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b> Ravens of Thought and Memory</b></div> </div> </div> </div><b>Lunar Intelligence</b><br /> This Charm physically rips Intimacies out of people, taking attendant memories with them for the Anathema to learn. The stolen passion takes the shape of an animal such as a jackdaw or a centipede, which whispers to the Lunar in a tongue know only to them.<br /> <br /> New Charm: <b>Honey-and-Iron Emanation</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T06:02:40-07:00","id":175173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=175104#post175104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Honey-and-Iron Emanation</b></div> </div> </div> </div><b>Sidereal Socialize</b><br /> The Vizier lays a hand on an individual and makes of him an alluring trap for others. All others who look for something they desire will find it obvious that they see it in the Sidereal's target. Someone seeking a bed partner may find the target especially intriguing, an investigator seeking a clue may believe the target knows something, and a raksha eager to sate his hunger may be certain the target has a most bountiful soul. However, when they make a serious attempt to claim it, the trap is sprung, their attempt fails, and they are struck with a debilitating curse.<br /> <br /> Once triggered, the allure vanishes from the target. At the time of laying the trap, a wise Sidereal may specify a particular sort of desire the target represents, giving appeal only to those in search of it, and preventing the bait from being seized upon by another hunger. Or a Sidereal may simply let loose an alluring target for wont of a distraction.<br /> <br /> New Charm:<br /> <i>Fractal Forest Web</i><br /> or<br /> <i>Brushstrokes on Heartstrings</i> <i>Method</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":". 06-20-2014, 09:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T07:21:54-07:00","id":175227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=175173#post175173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Fractal Forest Web</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Lunar Territory Charm (boundary marking meditation as pre-req)<br /> <br /> The lunar tracks and traces his territory in a web-like pattern, sectionning off parcels of it's area into smaller and smaller pieces with thin lines of essence that only the Lunar can percieve. Whenever a creature enters this web, it is made to believe that it has entered the Bordermarches, Middlemarches or the Deep Wyld, at the Lunar's discretion, as an illusion effect (she acquires illusory mutations and may be targetted by Shaping Combat and Fantasms). As long as the target is within the web, the Lunar has complete control over her perception of the environment, including flora, fauna, weather, distance, the passage of time and percieved position. If the Lunar has any Graces, he may use them for Shaping Combat as long as the illusion holds.<br /> <br /> This can include making a small empty ice-cave seem like an infinite burning desert in the middle of a sand-storm, populated by teleporting scorpions where a day lasts an eternity and cacti grow in mere seconds.<br /> <br /> New Charm: <b>Eight-Legged Stallion Pursuit</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 06-20-2014, 10:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T07:47:03-07:00","id":175247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=175227#post175227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New Charm: <b>Eight-Legged Stallion Pursuit</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Raksha Way Grace Charm. In shaping combat, this Charm allows the Wyld to pursue fleeing opponents from waypoint to waypoint by conjuring up chimerical steeds. In Creation, it allows them to wrap a living steed in strands of gossamer for a hellride that warps space to cross great distances in an eyeblink, incidentally leaving the mount mutated and monstrous.<br /> <br /> Seven Hearts Reliquary","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T09:37:51-07:00","id":175299,"title":"","content":"<b>Seven Hearts Reliquary: </b>Abyssal Integrity Charm, that upgrades Immortal Malevolence Enslavement. It allows the Abyssal to select an alternate &quot;respawn&quot; point by sacrificing six mortals, then cutting out his own heart and placing all six in a soulsteel urn. As long as the urn contains the seven still-beating hearts, he can resurrect either at its location or the Mouth of the Void, and even spirit-killing attacks only delay his return rather than preventing it. It should be noted that the Abyssal has no way of knowing whether the urn is safe without actually going and checking on it.<br /> <br /> New Charm: <b>Fire Upon the Rock of Ages</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T11:50:15-07:00","id":175453,"title":"","content":"<b>Fire Upon the Rock of Ages</b><br /> Sidereal War<br /> <br /> Some things are simply too horrible to allow to spread, even for Fate. And some things must be cleansed by fire. The Sidereal chooses a large area (how large of an area this charm can affect is at the Storyteller's discretion) in which fate has been disrupted. This area becomes isolated, with no one able to enter or leave through any means unless the Sidereal allows it. When the charm is dispelled, the selected area becomes entirely isolated for a full year, and begins burning within.<br /> <br /> Choose:<br /> Crying Tears of Blood<br /> or<br /> Crack the setting Sun","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T12:07:30-07:00","id":175461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HalfTangible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=175453#post175453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Crying Tears of Blood</div> </div> </div> </div>Liminal Resistance<br /> <br /> A Liminal is fully aware of her body, and can remove any impurities if this is required. This charm lets the Liminal know that she is poisoned, it doesn't tell her about the nature of the poison or who poisoned her, just that she is poisoned. In addition, this charm lets the Liminal attempt to purify their own body, by rolling a Resistance+Essence against the poison's toxicity. If this roll succeeds, the poison is excreted through the eyes, effectively making it look like the Liminal is crying. This blood has the same characteristics as the poison it contains.<br /> <br /> Let's do something visceral...<br /> <br /> Dance of the Flayed Twins","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T12:22:17-07:00","id":175468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=175461#post175461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dance of the Flayed Twins</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Liminal Larceny</b><br /> After removing her skin (using a prerequisite Charm) the Flesh Aspect endows it with a shadow of life. The skin-puppet is too weak for battle, but can float on the wind and squeeze through narrow gaps.<br /> This Charm is Indefinite; the Chernozem can't regenerate her skin until she deactivates it.<br /> <br /> New Charm: <b>Four Hundred Heartbeats Curse</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T12:46:02-07:00","id":175480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=175468#post175468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New Charm: <b>Four Hundred Heartbeats Curse</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Labyrinth Circle Necromancy: All men's days are numbered. The target of this spell knows this more acutely than most. The literal four-hundred beats of this spell--roughly a scene's worth of action--are all she has left from the moment the Necromancer afflicts her, and in her skull the countdown echoes. When her time is up, she immediately [insert mechanic here to be likely-to-certain death for a mortal, but not make this a killswitch against any Exalt without an appropriate counterspell]<br /> <br /> Despite this--and despite the name--the spell has its advantages. The target of the spell may slip into a deathlike state at will, freely aware of her surroundings or in a deep slumber. Her body does not naturally degrade, scavengers will leave her be, and she does not require food or water or air. Most importantly, her heart does not beat. In this way, a victim of this curse may in fact outlive the one who cast it upon them. More than one necromancer has thought to cast a messenger into the future with this spell, but only a couple have thought to use it on themselves--it is an unfortunate but useful discovery by these poor souls that the spell cannot be cast and dispelled by and upon the same Necromancer at once.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T13:47:30-07:00","id":175521,"title":"","content":"Since the last post didn't give a Charm name, I'll take the last one in the thread untaken: <b>Crack the Setting Sun</b><br /> <br /> Solar Lore<br /> <br /> The Copper Spider strikes his mind with the Essence of pure thought, cracking it in twain and allowing her to focus her mind on multiple tasks at once. While Essence to this Charm is committed, the Solar may perform two purely mental tasks simultaneously, ignoring any flurry penalties if necessary. She may carefully watch her surroundings while planning for the next day's battle. She may mentally write a speech while drawing up plans for an aqueduct. This Charm is Stackable; each additional activation splits her mind again, allowing an additional task she may focus on without penalty.<br /> <br /> Next Charm: <b>Half-Lidded Thousand-Mile Stare</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":263,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","user":"Limited Reagent","date":". 06-20-2014, 04:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T14:56:50-07:00","id":175554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Limited Reagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=175521#post175521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Half-Lidded Thousand-Mile Stare</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Solar Integrity.<br /> <br /> Activated in response to any effect that would affect her mind (such as illusions, mutations, or a simple conversation), the Solar roots himself in the mundanity of the attempt. Her eyelids lower, her eyes look forward as though beyond the initiator of the effect in an expression of such ultimate apathy that not only negates the attempt, but makes the target lose points of willpower equal to the Solar's Integrity + essence as the vile creature feels it's confidence slip away in the face of such an unimpressionable juggernaught of stoicity. Additionally, this charm adds the Solar's Integrity + Essence to any contested roll to resist mental effects.<br /> <br /> Next Charm: <b>Honey Eyes Shrinking Kinderence</b> or <b>Shrew Summons Thunder</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T12:26:55-07:00","id":176269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=175554#post175554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Shrew Summons Thunder</b></div> </div> </div> </div><b>Infernal Larceny</b><br /> <br /> Though it pains the Infernal to deny the world his full and proper glory, the sweet reveal allows some to weather the burden. When disguised as an individual who is noticed but unremarked upon, such as with &quot;Rainclouds Hide Lightning,&quot; the Warlock may cast off this disguise in an obvious and grandiose fashion. Those who had been taken in by his ruse have their senses dashed by the reveal, as though by a roar of thunder after hours of silence, while those unfooled fare little better. The Infernal affects all witnesses in the area with a free and reflexive use of Sense-Stealing Storm, though those who had not been deceived receive a bonus to resist. If the Warlock spent any motes on the action in which he reveals himself, he may reduce the motes spent by 1, to a minimum cost of 1. If the action was casting a Sorcery spell, unveiling a Shintai, or using any effect directly using storms, lightning or thunder, the reduction becomes 3 motes.<br /> <br /> New Charm:<br /> <i>Brushstrokes on Heartstrings</i><br /> or<br /> <i>Raise High the Black Omen</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T13:21:42-07:00","id":176336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=176269#post176269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <i>Raise High the Black Omen</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Abyssal Performance<br /> <br /> There are some deathknights who view Resonance as a yank on their nooses, chaining them to the will of the Neverborn. Then there are those who embrace any kind of attention from their matters, no matter how painful or deadly. Whenever an Abyssal with this charm experiences a Resonance eruption, her anima immediately explodes to its fullest level and she may enjoy all of its benefits for free, so long as the eruption is in effect.<br /> <br /> Apocalypse Serpent's Embrace OR Love And Hatred Condemnation","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T15:08:51-07:00","id":176455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ellis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=176336#post176336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Apocalypse Serpent's Embrace</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Dragon-Blooded Martial Arts. Prereq of As in the Beginning and Smashing Tidal Wave Technique (yes, requires War and Martial Arts)<br /> <br /> The Dragon-Blooded focuses the apocalyptic forces of As in the Beginning into a single person, filling them with fire and fury and destruction. Roll a martial arts attack against a single target. If successes, the primal forces of the ancient world rise up, strike down, and surround the victim. The Dragon-Blooded needs time to draw such potent elemental energies to herself, dependent on the threshold successes of the roll before the effects described below occur.<br /> <br /> With <b>Air</b>, the sky darkens as clouds roll overhead, and lightning strikes a thousand times in a single spot, dealing bashing damage and stunning the victim. With <b>Earth</b>, the land shutters and splits like a gaping maw, swallowing the victim and crushing them, stranding them hundreds of yards beneath the surface. With <b>Fire</b>, molten fire erupts from the ground like a volcano, engulfing the victim and incinerating them with lethal damage. At sea, <b>Water </b>can be used, a tidal wave reaching up to grasp the victim before pulling them down hundreds of yards into an terrible vortex dealing bashing damage and immediately causing the victim to check for drowning. <b>Wood </b>makes life erupt from all surfaces, growing thick and encasing the victim in thorny vines, dealing bashing damage and poisoning the victim with a venom that never runs out as long as the clinch is maintained.<br /> <br /> If the Dragon-Blooded hasn't taken steps to continue the grapple without physically touching the target (such as using Bonds of Unbreakable Ice), then the Dragon-Blooded is subject to the same effects as the victim. If the Dragon-Blooded manages to maintain the clinch the same time as in the beginning, she may activate this Charm again without paying its Willpower cost. This can be reiterated until the clinch is broken or the Dragon-Blooded can no longer pay the mote cost of this Charm.<br /> <br /> Next Charm:<b> Blood in the Gutter</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":263,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","user":"Limited Reagent","date":". 06-24-2014, 01:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T20:17:01-07:00","id":176662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Limited Reagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=176455#post176455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Next Charm:<b> Blood in the Gutter</b></div> </div> </div> </div> Abyssal Larceny<br /> <br /> When attempting to hide a murder, or a series of murders, instead of getting rid of the evidence, the abyssal makes the grim display seem like a part of everyday occurrences. The scattered blood and guts attract no attention beyond a morbidly stoic &quot;oh, another one&quot;. Incidentally this can be used over a longer term to desensitize a population to any sort of loss of life, creating a district where mass murder is as overlooked as petty bribery.<br /> <br /> New charm : Veteran's Respite Apparition","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 06-21-2014, 11:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-22T10:27:56-07:00","id":177159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=176662#post176662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Abyssal Larceny New charm : Veteran's Respite Apparition</div> </div> </div> </div> Infernal Socialize: Cecelyne Having discovered their victim's deepest desire, the Infernal can cause a tantalizing vision to materialize before their eyes. Travelers in the Endless Desert may see mirages of oases and shelter, while war-ravaged soldiers see images of the people they left behind and at home. Nothing Is Everything OR Dreaming Butterfly Prana","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-22T21:49:57-07:00","id":177673,"title":"","content":"I missed Ellis's one a little earlier, so I guess I'll drop in the effect for Love And Hatred Condemnation here:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ellis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=176336#post176336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Love And Hatred Condemnation</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Solar Presence</b><br /> <br /> The Lawgiver launches a fierce defense of that which she loves, dimming the fires of hate others may hold for such a thing. The Solar may use this Charm to supplement a social action in support of the subject of one of her positive Intimacies. For the rest of the scene, all negative Intimacies others may hold for the subject are treated as though they are one degree lower.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Now! Onto his more recent one:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ellis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=177159#post177159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dreaming Butterfly Prana</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Getimian Intelligence</b><br /> &quot;Never assume what you see and feel is real.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Getimian draws a deep breath, focusing intently on a life that may never -- perhaps could never -- have been. This life need not be human, nor even of human-like intelligence. When she exhales, a new pattern spider takes shape in her mind's eye. If she paid for this Charm with motes from her Yang pool, this spider emerges smoothly and painlessly from her forehead. It proceeds at her mental command to the forehead of someone sleeping, where it descends smoothly and painlessly inside to begin its task. If she paid for this Charm with motes from her Yin pool, the spider instead simply begins its task the next time the Getimian sleeps. The spider weaves for the sleeper a powerful dream, a day in the life of the one the Getimian invented.<br /> <br /> When she wakes, the sleeper is convinced that the dreamed life is her true life, and that her waking life is in fact a dream, albeit one with which she is generally inclined to play along. She receives a number of new Intimacies and Virtues to reflect the dreamed life -- including a Major Bond to her dreamed life being true -- and remains aware of all Intimacies and Virtues of her waking life, but these particular waking traits do not directly affect her. Instead, she gains a Minor Principle to play out her waking life, which is treated as a Major Principle with regard to any of her waking life's Defining Intimacies and any Virtues of 4 dots or more. She receives an extra die on all actions at which the dreamed life would excel, and loses one on all actions at which the dreamed life would be inept.<br /> <br /> If there is any information her dreamed life would know that her waking life would not or could not (or about which her waking life is mistaken), she becomes certain the answer is something her waking life would find plausible. She does receive a two die bonus to any Lore, Occult, or similar rolls to know things her dreamed life would know, if said rolls are reasonable to make at all. Any Charms or other capabilities of her waking life may be used just as easily as ever, though the dreamed life may have certain compunctions against their use (e.g. a Lunar given the dreamed life of a delicate fop is unlikely to drink any heart's blood). The character may obviously not use any powers or capabilities possessed only by the dreamed life, though this may not stop the character from trying (e.g. a Solar with the dreamed life of a voracious raksha may seek to sup on another's Virtues, and then feel quite silly afterward).<br /> <br /> The Charm's effects end on their own after a number of days set by the Getimian, not to exceed her Intelligence. The target wakes as though from a dream, in which she was the dreamed self living out all of those events. She rolls Integrity + Willpower to remember them fully, but otherwise remembers no more details than she would from any dream, though relevant sights or accounts may remind her. If the target's Major Bond to her dreamed life is fully degraded by any means, the Charm's effect ends prematurely. The Getimian may also will it to end early at any time (or at any time she can perceive the target, if paid out of her Yang pool).<br /> <br /> New Charm:<br /> <i>Artisan's Graceful Hooves</i><br /> or<br /> <i>Helix of Unseen Stairs</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":". 06-23-2014, 12:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-22T22:15:38-07:00","id":177683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=177673#post177673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Helix of Unseen Stairs</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Astrology Charm<br /> ------------------------<br /> <br /> Wraps the target with a curse that will cause something to distract their attention whenever a lack of attention paid to their surroundings would be to their particular displeasure or discomfort (or harm).<br /> <br /> New charm-<br /> <br /> Mother of Ten Thousand Dragons<br /> or<br /> Standing in the Full Light of the Heavens","signature":"","edited":{"userid":357,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/357-plotvitalnpc","user":"PlotVitalNPC","date":". 06-23-2014, 01:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/357-plotvitalnpc","name":"PlotVitalNPC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar357_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-22T23:11:04-07:00","id":177707,"title":"","content":"Standing in the Full Light of the Heavens - Solar Presence<br /> To behold a Lawgiver is to know the majesty of the Unconquered Sun. The solar automatically adds 5 successes to any socialize or presence roll made during this scene. In addition, all who attempt to argue with the solar suffer a 2 die penalty to their presence rolls and MDV.<br /> <br /> Fly on Poisoned Wings<br /> or<br /> Grinding Spiral of Eternity","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-23T11:42:55-07:00","id":178098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HalfTangible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=177707#post177707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Grinding Spiral of Eternity</div> </div> </div> </div>Necromancy spell of the Third Circle<br /> <br /> Some speculate that there is an unknown Primordial embodying the concepts of cycles and singularities, who was destroyed or slain and whose only legacy is this spell. Pricking her fingers and ears, the necromancer gestures violently at the ground beneath her feet, which collapses into a sinkhole. This is the beginning of the end.<br /> The sinkhole is a portal straight to Oblivion, with all that that entails. Furthermore, the terrible weight of the Labyrinth sucks at Creation around its wound, pulling it down like a solid whirlpool. Structures in the area take gradual but massive amounts of damage as their frames warp along the lines of a spiral, while living things suffer mutations and insanity without rhyme or reason. The closer anyone approaches to the center of the spiral, the more powerful its effects are. The spell lasts until (unlikely and suitably occult circumstances), at which point the entire area affected by the Grinding Spiral is sucked into the sinkhole and disappears. Yet anyone who sheds Essence-charged blood on the spot where the sinkhole lay may reopen it, and again after it is closed. The spell can only be permanently broken by Third Circle countermagic.<br /> <br /> Sign of Impossible Stars OR First And Final Breath","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-23T12:48:44-07:00","id":178138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ellis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=178098#post178098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First And Final Breath</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Lunar Intelligence (Necromancy Charm)</b><br /> <br /> The Moon-Chosen Necromancer sets a second layer of complexity onto the preparations and materials for a Sorcerous working to create life. This second layer may take any fashion that is appropriate (encircling the circle of glowing runes with a second circle of dark ones, carving harsh sigils into the flesh of anointed offerings, surrounding a pyramid with spires of black crystal, etc.). This complete, the Lunar may begin readying the working. This Necromantic working must be complete before the Sorcerous working is, though it takes a fraction of the time and effort. It is permitted to complete this days in advance, and to conceal the marks of its application.<br /> <br /> If successful, when the Sorcerous working completes, the entity it meant to create takes form just as intended. However, the entity draws one breath and one breath only before the Necromantic energy floods through it. Seizing on the departing Sorcerous energies used to create it, the black spell draws as horrific or beautiful a cry as the creature can produce and then strikes it dead, refashioning it into a creature of death. The Necromancer may add whatever dread enhancements that are within his power to bestow, drawing on all the life the entity was unable to live. It is bound to the Necromancer as a ghost would be, and its living form added to the Lunar's library of forms.<br /> <br /> The Necromancer may affect his own Sorcerous workings with this Charm, but will generally find it more efficient -- and more satisfying -- to taint the efforts of others.<br /> <br /> New Charm:<br /> <i>Beggar with Palace Castigation</i><br /> or<br /> <i>Artisan's Graceful Hooves</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":". 06-23-2014, 04:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-23T13:42:55-07:00","id":178196,"title":"","content":"Artisan's Graceful Hooves<br /> <br /> -Lunar Appearance: The Exalt uses whatever he must to achieve the limits of his craft, blending the form of his outer flesh with the impossible beauty of his innermost soul. Make an Essence+Appearance+Performance roll. Anyone who, watching this performance, begins or continues a Craft Action which, in some way, commemorates or draws inspiration from said performance, gains half your successes, rounded down. Every day a project is not begun, or continued, drains 2 successes, to zero. Said performance can be repeated to further inspire the crafter withiin the alotted Craft session, but no reward from this Charm can ever exceed the initial bonus, unless it is a new project.<br /> <br /> <i>Leeching Vines And Roots </i>or <i>(X), First Of His/Her Name</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-23T14:00:55-07:00","id":178232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brasstreader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=178196#post178196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First Of His/Her Name[/I]</div> </div> </div> </div>First of His/Her Name<br /> Dragonblooded Lore<br /> <br /> This charm almost completely severs the tie between the Dragonblood and their ancestors. The Dragonblood can spend XP to purchase up their breeding as though it were favored charms when they first acquire this charm, cutting away their mortal heritage, but the true effect of the charm is to cut them off from their line of descent- from now on, for all magical purposes they have no ancestors, and any effect which would give them ancestors automatically fails, and they become incapable of answering to any surname they had once inherited. Obviously, this prevents them from using certain Dragonblooded charms which act upon family on any biological kin who are not their children, unless there is some other reason to consider such individuals family.<br /> <br /> Heart for the Heartless<br /> OR<br /> Mother's Manifold Hatchlings","signature":"","edited":{"userid":357,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/357-plotvitalnpc","user":"PlotVitalNPC","date":". 06-23-2014, 09:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/357-plotvitalnpc","name":"PlotVitalNPC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar357_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-23T14:30:12-07:00","id":178254,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ellis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=178098#post178098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sign of Impossible Stars</div> </div> </div> </div> 2nd circle necromancy<br /> <br /> The necromancer spits blood into the sky and forms a blasphemous mudramudra known only to the neverborn. The blood spreads, as though over a glass dome, to form morbid astrological signs and reveal the stars of the underworld. For a month and a day, the area counts as being part of the underworld for the purposes of astrology, and any beings in the area seem to disappear from the loom of fate. For the duration of this spell, the necromancer has access to some effects similar to Sidereal astrology, but that take on a deathly and grim twist and any paradox that would be accrued becomes resonance.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Edit for PlotVitalNPC's Edit:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Heart for the Heartless </div> </div> </div>Lunar Charm - pre-req: Harmony with Reality Technique<br /> <br /> This subtle charm allows a Lunar to imbue a wyld creature (one that can but doesn't have a Heart Grace) with enough volition to <i>want</i> a Heart grace, and enough individuality and Reality to be able to steal Graces as though a Creation-Born. Alternatively, if the creature does have a Heart Grace in it's possession, the lunar can spend an additional [cost] in order to attempt to transplant the grace into the creature with a successful [intelligence + craft(glamour)] roll at a difficulty of the Heart Grace's rating + 2, giving it a sense of self at the cost of the original owner's self-awareness. Failing the roll means instant calcification for the creature as all its potential bleeds out into the world in a display which many commoner raksha would consider horrific.<br /> \u200b<br /> This charm does not function for transplanting the hearts of Noble Raksha with an Essence Rating higher than the Lunar's.<br /> <br /> New charm: Expanding Void Sun","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 06-23-2014, 10:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-23T19:30:26-07:00","id":178535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=178254#post178254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> 2nd circle necromancy<br /> New charm: Expanding Void Sun</div> </div> </div> </div>Solar Stealth, building off of Swallowing the Sun. Drain everyone's anima banners and all ambient magic effects into your own anima before compressing it into a burst of blinding black radiance, letting you make a stealth roll with the benefit of everyone else being momentarily blind. <br /> <br /> New Charm: Gifts Ungiven Prana","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-23T21:26:58-07:00","id":178625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=178535#post178535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gifts Ungiven Prana</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Solar Lore</b> (prerequisites include Power-Awarding Prana)<br /> A wise Lawgiver knows how to gift a mortal a spark of the Sun's own light and thereby light a flame. A still wiser Lawgiver knows how to ignite the fires of heroism by denying it. Setting a hand on a mortal, she wills a flood of Solar Essence to torrent through him, but only for a few brief moments. With a smile, she conveys to him that he does not need that power to be a hero, only his own strength of heart and will, and that he may even someday turn the head of the Most High.<br /> <br /> Filled with certainty in the truth of it and still warm from the afterglow, he acquires a Major Intimacy of self-confidence. So long as it lasts, he receives a point of Willpower when facing adversity, and may channel Willpower for 2 successes in the scene in which he does so.<br /> <br /> New Charm:<br /> <i>King Becomes Princeling Trick</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-23T21:57:33-07:00","id":178647,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Y'know I was working on a full Adamant-Circle spell for Expanding Void Sun, but then it got grabbed by Vance. Oh well! Here's what I had, incomplete, because might as well not waste the effort:<br /> <br /> <b>Expanding Void Sun</b><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 77m, 3wp; <b>Circle</b>: Adamant; <b>Type</b>: Simple (Dramatic Action)<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: Area Effect, Component, Obvious<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Until the orb is consumed<br /> <br /> To begin this spell, the sorcerer first requires a orb of pure tin. Upon this orb he must inscribe the seventy-seven Runes of Eternity, which describe the wheel of ages and the cycle of birth and betrayal that rules all things. Each rune must have one mote imbedded within it, causing it to pulse rythmically with power. Doing so requires a dramatic Stamina + Linguistics action, difficulty 7, that takes seventy-seven straight hours of inscription, one hour for each rune.<br /> <br /> Then the sorcerer raises the orb into the air with his left hand. His anima rises up to a full bonfire, leaping off his body whole and encircling the orb like the corona of a solar eclipse. </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=178625#post178625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>King Becomes Princeling Trick</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereal Larceny, building off of Name-Pilfering Practice<br /> <br /> Threads of fate are intertwined, and by pulling one may another follow. While the Sidereal has stolen someone's name with Name-Pilfering Practice, he may continue to pull on the thread of their fate, dislodging their reputation and social standing. This effect is a gradual shift in the world's perception, a lowering of grade; a king might become a princeling, or a master tradesman a journeyman. A priest seems to become an acolyte, or a farmer becomes a farmhand. Each stacked use of this Charm upon the same person steps them down even further: the princeling becomes a noble, or a journeyman a novice. This Charm doesn't affect their skills, just what everyone perceives the person as.<br /> <br /> New Charm: <b>The Importance of Minutia</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-23T22:19:06-07:00","id":178676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=178535#post178535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solar Stealth, building off of Swallowing the Sun. Drain everyone's anima banners and all ambient magic effects into your own anima before compressing it into a burst of blinding black radiance, letting you make a stealth roll with the benefit of everyone else being momentarily blind.<br /> <br /> New Charm: Gifts Ungiven Prana</div> </div> </div> </div>Please make this a real charm in 3E. You have no idea how much I want this charm. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-24T04:52:36-07:00","id":178797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ellis</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Iron Fire Crucible OR Baleful Meteor Flare</div> </div> </div> </div>I reject the lie of the OR.<br /> <br /> <b>Iron Fire Crucible (Terrestrial Resistance; Fire favoured)</b><br /> Activated in response to a damaging attack, this Charm reforges the user's anima into phantom armour using the force of the blow. This cancels out anima flux for the Charm's duration.<br /> <br /> <b>Baleful Meteor Flare (Terrestrial Thrown; Earth favoured)</b><br /> This Charm ignites a projectile of stone, clay, or jade with a blinding white flame, allowing the Son of Pasiap to use it in one of two ways. It may either be launched at extreme range, resolving as a normal attack, or deal a terrifying crippling blow to a target at close range.<br /> If the Exalted has at least three dots of War, either use of thisCharm has an increased chance of routing battle groups.<br /> <br /> EDIT: There appears to have been a split again. Let's seal it shut.<br /> <br /> New Charm: <b>the Importance of Minutia</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":97,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","user":"The MG","date":". 06-24-2014, 08:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-24T07:03:31-07:00","id":178899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=178797#post178797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New Charm: <b>the Importance of Minutia</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereal Investigation:<br /> The Viziers are well-aware that what seemed insignificant at the time may save one's life later, or end another's.<br /> <br /> This charm gives the Sidereal the ability to store up to her Essence in mundane, non-martial objects she could carry in one hand Elsewhere for one mote each. While so stored, they will not degrade or decay, although particularly &quot;fresh&quot; qualities--such as the aroma of just-baked bread or the heat of steel fresh from a forge--will fade at a natural rate.<br /> <br /> When the Sidereal draws one of these items from storage and uses it, she doubles her stunt dice for whatever action the item supplements.<br /> <br /> New Charm: <b>A Quiver Full of Sorrows</b> OR <b>Outraced Heartbeat Meditation</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":561,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","user":"Mockery","date":".  Somehow I have the feeling that the Sidereals already have a King's Quest style inventory charm--it feels very Sidereal--but I can't remember one. If they don't, they should. If they do, I'll edit t 06-24-2014, 10:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-24T10:34:36-07:00","id":179034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=178254#post178254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New charm: Expanding Void Sun</div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Because, as should be manifestly obvious, I'm a huge Abyssals fanboy, but the fact that they can't establish their own personal Underworlds always bothered me, so:</div></div> </div> </div><br /> Abyssal Bureaucracy<br /> The Unconquered Sun claims to be the king of all Creation. The defeated Yozis make the same claim, and the Neverborn would if they could claim anything. But an Abyssal knows the truth: all things come to he who takes them. With this Charm the Abyssal claims an area in the Underworld as her own personal kingdom. She may add features to her kingdom as if it were a manse, and benefits from the extra motes while in her kingdom. Ghosts will readily accept her command, but they will also expect her to settle their grievances; an Abyssal who persistently fails may be the subject of a ghostly revolt, which may not kill or even unseat them but certainly bodes ill for the kingdom. She may expand it, both by ruling well and by claiming territory through conquest, but she must beware of others who don't like her encroaching on personal space.<br /> <br /> Iron Fire Crucible OR Baleful Meteor Flare","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-24T10:53:17-07:00","id":179044,"title":"","content":"*trying to merge different commits into the main branch*<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=178899#post178899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New Charm: <b>A Quiver Full of Sorrows</b> OR <b>Outraced Heartbeat Meditation</b></div> </div> </div> </div><b>A Quiver Full of Sorrows</b><br /> <br /> CMA, Needles of the 7 Despairs Style (form weapons: Arrows, Javelins, Needles, String*)<br /> <br /> The martial artist strikes his target with a flat palm over the heart and rolls what would otherwise be a normal social Investigation action to reveal intimacies. On a success, he pinpoints his adversary's deepest disappointments in himself and pulls them out, one per extra success, to form them into long thin needles that can be used as any mundane (albeit of exceptional quality) Form weapon for this style, adding a bonus of +2 accuracy and the piercing tag. Alternatively, the martial artist can enhance a weapon in her posession with the provided bonuses by reflexively coating it with the extracted sorrow.<br /> <br /> Each successful attack with such a weapon that dealt at last 1 level of damage creates an inviolable sorcerous intimacy for the rest of the scene that restricts the target's actions unless she spends 1 point of willpower per such intimacy.<br /> (e.g. The target might be reminded of his long-lost brother, whom he failed to rescue from slavery and seems to have a lot in common with the Martial Artist (though this need not actually be the case) and so is restricted from attacking the martial artist while looking at him)<br /> <br /> * a pre-requisite charm allows string and string-like things (such as hair) to be made solid as needles.<br /> ----<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Iron Fire Crucible</b><br /> -----<br /> But Sexually. </div> </div> </div>Terrestrial Fire-Aspected Presence.<br /> <br /> The Dragonblooded are known for their heated passions and larger-than-life desires. This charm rouses such intensity even in the common mortal. By teasing a glimpse of any portion of their body that could be considered sexually inviting and making it appear as the perfect combination of warmth, tenderness and strength, the Dragonblood fans the flames of existing desire into spectacular bonfires. For as long as motes remain commited, any action the target takes in the pursuit of satisfying the Dragonblooded's desires receives a bonus equal to the Exalt's Presence + Relevant Specialty. Every time the target gets a threshold of at least 5 successes on a task, they regain a point of willpower which ignores normal limits. The limit for willpower points gained this way becomes [Target's Willpower Rating + Exalt's chosen Specialty].<br /> <br /> However, this charm may not create desires where none exist, it can only enhance existing emotions.<br /> <br /> Next Charm: <b>Everything Slipping Away</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 06-24-2014, 02:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T07:59:20-07:00","id":179711,"title":"","content":"Sorry about that, everyone. My computer had some issues viewing and posting for a while there.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=179044#post179044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Everything Slipping Away</div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereal Medicine<br /> Sometimes the Sidereal's patient holds on to something instead of accepting it, and she must ease their loss. This Charm allows the Sidereal to erase a memory of up to a scene in length from her patient's memory, undoing any Bonds or Principles formed during that scene. Targeting particularly traumatic memories may even help to heal Derangements (or their 3e equivalents).<br /> <br /> Why We Build The Wall OR Squaring the Circle Technique","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":1797,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","user":"Ellis","date":". 06-28-2014, 01:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T19:45:46-07:00","id":180285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ellis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=179711#post179711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why We Build The Wall</div> </div> </div> </div>Abyssal Bureaucracy. Inspire a workforce to extraordinary labor and near-suicidal dedication by inciting fears of an enemy or antagonistic Other, giving them all Intimacies of hatred towards it as they work. <br /> <br /> Egg and Finger-Bone Trick <i>or</i> Living Bowsprit Prana","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T20:05:20-07:00","id":180294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=180285#post180285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Abyssal Bureaucracy. Inspire a workforce to extraordinary labor and near-suicidal dedication by inciting fears of an enemy or antagonistic Other, giving them all Intimacies of hatred towards it as they work.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was going to write something very similar, where a lunar sets themselves up as the antagonistic beast that is so feared or hated that people build or destroy things irrationally. But then work got in the way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Living Bowsprit Prana </div> </div> </div><i>if you know what I mean</i><br /> <br /> Fairfolk Name Charm.<br /> <br /> This charm enhances Assumption of the Person's Heart, allowing it to be used on the least gods of objects, conveying the same benefits to the object's god or the object's wielder, at the Raksha's discretion upon activating any applicable power. If used with other assumptions, the Raksha can assume the form of pieces of the object while retaining some form of mobility and the ability to communicate, such as becoming a moving, talking Bowsprit, or Singing and Dancing Sword.<br /> <br /> <b>Nexus of five heartbreaks.</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T21:10:33-07:00","id":180372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=180294#post180294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Nexus of Five Heartbreaks</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereal Thrown/Resistance: A super prayer strip Charm that requires two prayer strip Charms from different Abilities as prereqs, this one, building off of Storm's Eye Stance and Unrelenting Torment Technique.<br /> <br /> The Sidereal activates this Charm with a prayer strip which has the Scripture of the Woeful Maiden written upon it. She rips it into five strips, stating a name each time she does; each tear flashes like a yellow lightning bolt. Then the Exalt ties these strips together, binding the fates of these five people into an inexorable knot of woe. Each victim gains an inviolate sorcerous intimacy toward another that will disrupt their life and cause heartbreak and strife, along with a destiny to bring these people into contact. The Storyteller is encouraged to mix up the intimacies so that the most drama and pain will occur by their own doings.<br /> <br /> Trouble brews for the Sidereal's victims, and the Sidereal holds the knot of fate that ties them all together. While she holds the bundle of prayer strips, the victims are treated as bound by Storm's Eye Stance, and may be attacked as if with Unrelenting Torment Technique without requiring the Sidereal to activate either of those Charms.<br /> <br /> Finally, the Sidereal may yank out one of the torn strips from her knot, climatically releasing that victim's woe; in the next scene, that victim suffers a botch relating to the sorcerous intimacy of the Exalt's choosing. At that point, the victim is released from the Charm, and the sorcerous intimacy becomes mundane.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Bonus scripture text!<br /> <br /> <b>The Scripture of the Woeful Maiden</b><br /> Once, there was a maiden\u2026<br /> \u2026who was full of sorrows.<br /> She tried to run away, only to stumble into more trouble.<br /> &quot;Why do you cry?&quot; the trouble asked.<br /> &quot;Running is all I know,&quot; said she.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Next Charm: <b>Last Argument of Kings</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":263,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","user":"Limited Reagent","date":". 06-26-2014, 12:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T00:57:50-07:00","id":180502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Limited Reagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=180372#post180372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Next Charm: <b>Last Argument of Kings</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Abyssal Socialize:<br /> This charm enhances any debate one might have with a local authority. Provided that their arguments are more successful than those of the authority figure, this charm influences those who would have fallen sway to the arguments to instead advocate for a violent purge of the authority figure and those associated with them. Any human who dies as a result of this charm will rise as some manner of ghost, unless slain in a manner which destroys the soul.<br /> <br /> Next Charm:<br /> Building the New Nest<br /> OR<br /> Parent to the Prey's Progeny<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/357-plotvitalnpc","name":"PlotVitalNPC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar357_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T06:18:24-07:00","id":180739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PlotVitalNPC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=180502#post180502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Parent to the Prey's Progeny<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Artifact Headdress (Jade, concealed Gossamer)<br /> <br /> This small and conservatively-designed headdress exudes parental authority that anyone younger than it's wearer picks up on and responds to. After about a scene of interaction the coronet creates a link between the exalt and every valid target the Exalt has interacted with, creating a sorcerous pseudo-parental bond that can be used as an Arcane Link in place of any other, and allows the bearer to use any magic that would target their progeny on the target(s) of the bond.<br /> <br /> If reinforced long enough (e.g. through intimacies or something), this bond might overthrow even the original, effectively becoming permanent and the &quot;official&quot; lineage that any parenthood-related magic regards as completely legitimate.<br /> <br /> Next:<b> Scrolls of Cascading Styles</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T19:21:47-07:00","id":182440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=180739#post180739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Scrolls of Cascading Styles</b></div> </div> </div> </div><b>Solar Linguistics</b><br /> The Lawgiver's prose and brushstrokes flow with gripping elegance and readers find themselves swept along by them, turning page after page. When a Solar supplements a piece of writing with this Charm, she rolls (Linguistics + X). If her successes exceed A, the work instills a Minor Intimacy to read the end of the piece in anyone who reads even a bit of it (a sentence or two suffices). This Intimacy fades at the conclusion of the work.<br /> <br /> If the Solar's successes exceed B, she may instead change the Intimacy's subject upon the complete reading of the piece, to all else in the set or series of which this work is a part. If her successes exceed C, she may change the Intimacy's subject to all works she has ever penned.<br /> <br /> New Charm:<br /> <i>Candle in the Spire Subterfuge</i><br /> or<br /> <i>Wisdoms Freely Whispered</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":". 06-27-2014, 10:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T21:15:47-07:00","id":182536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=182440#post182440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New Charm:<br /> <i>Wisdoms Freely Whispered</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Dragonblooded Lore<br /> <br /> It is the parent's prerogative to choose what their child shall learn and what values will be impressed on them. This charm allows a dragonblood to more easily teach skills to or instill values in their descendants (henceforth referred to as targets). The dragonblood may pay up to one fourth of the XP cost of any ability in which they are training their target from their own experience, may choose to either double or half the number of scenes needed to establish or erode an intimacy (though with willpower expenditure the target may resist this) provided that they are in the presence of the target at the time, and may spend their own XP to raise or lower the virtues of a willing target (lowering a virtue from a certain level has the same cost as raising it to that level).<br /> <br /> New Charm<br /> Pyre-Bed of the Tragic Newlyweds<br /> OR<br /> Mother's Gift to the Unborn","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/357-plotvitalnpc","name":"PlotVitalNPC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar357_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T21:59:08-07:00","id":182607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PlotVitalNPC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=182536#post182536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mother's Gift to the Unborn</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Panoply Charm of the Dowager of the Irreverent Vulgate in Unrent Veils</b><br /> <br /> The Dowager looses a cruel curse that reaches far and wide. One that seizes upon expecting mothers and the children yet to be born. It sits idle while the pregnancy proceeds, but strikes suddenly at birth. It all but assures death in the mother, though almost seems to <i>increase</i> the child's survival. Becoming motherless is not the curse's only cruelty for the newborn.<br /> <br /> Through whispers and dreams, the curse teaches the affected child that his mother loved him, regardless of the truth, in a way distinct, deeper, and dearer than any other ever could. He develops a Defining Intimacy of love for his departed mother, which rebuilds itself if degraded. While many such mothers might rest easier knowing their children understood the depths of their love, this knowledge is but a tool to the Dowager's curse.<br /> <br /> This underscores to the child that this great, boundless love that was his birthright has been denied him, and renders all other affection he may begin to feel hollow and empty. All Intimacies of love or other fond feelings toward others are more difficult to establish and degrade quickly.<br /> <br /> The exceptions are any such Intimacies developed toward the Dowager, who knows upon seeing the child how to assume his mother's shape and effect her mannerisms flawlessly. Should the Dowager build a Defining Intimacy toward herself in the child, it takes the place of the Defining Intimacy of love for the mother, which falls away. All other effects of this Charm remain. The Dowager has made use of this horrendous method for several in her orphanage, and sees great promise in its application for selecting a Deathknight.<br /> <br /> Only if the cursed develops a Defining Intimacy of love or affection toward another can the curse be broken, absent other magic.<br /> <br /> New Charm:<br /> <i>Brushstrokes on Heartstrings</i><br /> or<br /> <i>Candle in the Spire Subterfuge</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T00:31:25-07:00","id":183608,"title":"","content":"<b>Brushstrokes on Heartstrings</b><br /> Solar Socialize<br /> <br /> Anyone who stands in the Solar's presence for longer than two hours straight without direct interaction with this charm active gains a permanent positive intimacy for the Solar. The Solar does not have to know all targets of the charm, the targets simply need to be aware of the Solar's presence in their midst.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Master of Maiden Hearts Method</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T11:03:05-07:00","id":183888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HalfTangible;n183608 [I</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Master of Maiden Hearts Method[/I]</div> </div> </div> </div> Solar Presence The Solar promises adventure to a prospective sidekick, offering them the chance to break free of their humdrum life. This Charm convinces someone to follow the Solar, and if they are mortal they become Heroic Mortals. Apocalypse-Canceling Gesture OR Effortless Violence Technique","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T11:26:49-07:00","id":183895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ellis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=183888#post183888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Effortless Violence Technique</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereal Firearms. Builds off of Wearing Red to a Wedding and Crimson Transient Assurance.<br /> <br /> The Sidereal cloaks herself in a mantle of violent intent. Everyone who beholds her can feel the capacity for harm upon her, no matter the circumstances. Morale rolls for people engaging the Sidereal in combat increase in difficulty be one. The target number of any roll to intimidate decreases by one, or two if violence is implied in the threat. Even if the Sidereal is not armed, everyone will assume she is.<br /> <br /> Finally, those who hold a positive intimacy toward the Sidereal, or who have been instructed by the Seer in the past, are more likely to bring forth their grievances to the Sidereal directly, usually accompanied with the threat of violence. If the Sidereal follows such action up by Joining Battle against these characters, the Sidereal gains one offensive mote per action during the resultant battle.<br /> <br /> New Charm: <b>Mantle of Misplaced Things</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T17:01:45-07:00","id":184209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Limited Reagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=183895#post183895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New Charm: <b>Mantle of Misplaced Things</b></div> </div> </div> </div><b>Fair Folk Cup Charm</b><br /> The raksha dips her fingers into her Cup and spreads about her target a subtle curse. Rolling Cup + Essence against her target's MDV, she fills nearby objects with a playfulness to hide from the target's desire for them. When making an Investigation roll to find something, the target finds its difficulty increased to 1 greater than the threshold successes on the raksha's roll, as objects quietly shuffle themselves around just out of sight and engage in other subterfuge to better confound his efforts.<br /> <br /> The impact is still worse, however, as even searches for which no Investigation roll would normally be called for now demand such a roll, albeit at a difficulty of only 1 fewer than the threshold successes on the raksha's roll. Men have gone mad simply trying to get dressed, as their unworn clothes mysteriously relocate themselves the instant they are out of sight.<br /> <br /> This curse does not afflict another person attempting to find the item, nor does it apply if another person assist in the search or even watches the search unfold. The curse likewise presents others with no difficulty in simply giving it to one so cursed. That said, if normally easily found objects have relocated themselves significantly from the target's failed attempts to find them, anyone else may need an Investigation roll of her own to find them, albeit typically only at difficulty 1 or 2.<br /> <br /> A repurchase at higher Essence allows the raksha to instead (or in addition) name one of the following as the source of the target's addlement:<ul><li>Structures and locations, as small shuffles in terrain (signposts, turns in the road, etc.) disorient him in his search.</li> <li>People, whom the surrounding world subtly contrives to keep the target from finding.</li> </ul><br /> A further repurchase at higher Essence may be used to make the effect permanent, and yet another may even extend its effects down a family's bloodline. Some say the family of a Lunar who wields a massive iron umbrella has suffered from this affliction for generations.<br /> <br /> <u>Glamour (3-9):</u> This Charm may be placed in an outward-facing Oneiromancy, afflicting characters who undertake a certain sort of action specified during the creation of the spell, for a number of days equal to its Lorekeeper's Essence. For every 3 points, the base effect of this Charm or of one of its repurchases may be applied. Each effect may specify its own sort of action, if appropriate.<br /> <br /> New Charm: <b>Thorns Wrapped Round a Crystal Heart</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":". 06-29-2014, 08:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T11:35:12-07:00","id":184969,"title":"","content":"<b>Thorns Wrapped Round a Crystal Heart</b><br /> Terrestrial Craft<br /> Once attuned to a manse, the child of Sextis Jylis may enter a deep meditative state, infusing its structure with the essence of growth and regeneration and repairing damaged systems over time. For every twelve-hour period spent in this state, one damaged system is repaired. The rating of the manse may not exceed (Terrestrial's Essence -1).<br /> <br /> Next charm:<br /> <b>Come with Me if you Want to Live</b><br /> and/or<br /> <b>Get Away from Her, You BITCH!</b> (note, the caps is important)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 06-30-2014, 02:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T20:10:31-07:00","id":185959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=184969#post184969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Come with Me if you Want to Live</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereal Drive, building off of Predestine Escort Coincidence.<br /> <br /> Whenever the Sidereal is driving a vehicle, she can use this Charm to call out to another character, urging them to get into her car if they want to survive. This is a reflexive action and is not a social attack, so it can be ignored without Willpower cost (though this Charm may be comboed with Predestine Escort Coincidence to make it a social attack). If he agrees, however, he comes under a Compulsion to get into the Seer's car by the end of the scene. This can be resisted with two Willpower. Until then (or until the Compulsion is resisted), he gains a +2 non-Charm bonus to his DVs and (the Sidereal's Drive) aggravated, lethal, and bashing soak and Hardness \u2014 by agreeing with the Sidereal's plea, fate conspires to keep him alive until he escapes with the Exalt.<br /> <br /> If the Sidereal did use Predestine Escort Coincidence on the target, then the aforementioned defensive benefits continue to apply until that Charm's chosen destination is reached.<br /> <br /> Next Charm:<b> Silent Bell Ringing Endlessly</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":263,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","user":"Limited Reagent","date":". 07-02-2014, 07:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-02T14:20:49-07:00","id":186517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Limited Reagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=185959#post185959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Next Charm:<b> Silent Bell Ringing Endlessly</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereal Medicine<br /> <br /> Whenever the Sidereal kills something with Smooth Transition or Peaceable Conclusion, a resounding silence rings throughout her anima. She may use either Charm once for free per dot of killed beings' Essence. If she kills something with Invocation of the Storm-Following Silence, she may use it again for free. These free Charms can be chained indefinitely, though they must be used within the scene.<br /> <br /> Ten-Ton Enlightenment OR Cold Star Burning","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-02T16:28:44-07:00","id":186615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ellis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=186517#post186517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ten-Ton Enlightenment</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunar Knack-<br /> <br /> With this knack, the lunar may multiply or divide the weight of any form assumed by a factor of their essence. This knack does not have to affect the lunar, and can be used on other beings transformed by the lunar.<br /> <br /> True Essence of Courage OR Weaving the Bloodline","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/357-plotvitalnpc","name":"PlotVitalNPC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar357_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-02T18:17:37-07:00","id":186684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PlotVitalNPC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=186615#post186615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weaving the Bloodline</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Lunar Knack (Intelligence)</b><br /> <br /> The Lunar dips into her treasure trove of stolen shapes, and fashions freshly alloyed marvels of the flesh. The Lunar may select a number of shapes equal to her Intelligence, pay a number of motes equal to the shapes chosen (on top of any for a shapeshifting action), and create a facsimile form between them. She may select traits between them as she pleases, so long as there is an obvious visible similarity to all component shapes, as though through parentage (however impossible). Anyone who would recognize any of the component shapes receives a bonus or penalty related to the relative number of component shapes recognized or unrecognized.<br /> <br /> A higher Essence repurchase allows the Lunar to weave the bloodlines of one or more others. Paying the cost of using this Knack herself, the Lunar may affect a number of nearby targets equal to her (Intelligence - 1) who have an open wound. The Lunar may include forms from her Heart's Blood library in the donations, and may include either one such form or herself without counting against the maximum number of targets. If successful on a (roll) against each target's (roll/defense), blood flies from whichever donors and recipients she chooses, mingling their blood. A recipient character is unharmed (if donated blood is poisonous or acidic, it loses these properties), but the character's blood and bloodline thereafter become a facsimile of its original owner's and any donors for all relevant effects. The Lunar may freely decide the traits of this facsimile as normal. Any child born of an affected character treats this facsimile as one of its parents, in place of the character. The Moon-Chosen who mingled the blood may at any time return an affected character's blood to normal, if the affected character possesses an open wound through which the tainted blood may escape.<br /> <br /> Some Dynasts return with their lives from a Wyld Hunt, only to live in dread that their next child may be born a twisted bestial mockery.<br /> <br /> New Charm:<br /> <i>Moon Counsels Stars</i><br /> or<br /> <i>Breaking the Gates of Sundraprisha</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T09:12:37-07:00","id":187143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=186684#post186684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Moon Counsels Stars</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Lunar Intelligence Knack, requiring that one knack where you take someone's destiny as well as their shape.<br /> <br /> Studying the rapport between the moon and the stars, a lunar internalizes their celestial relations enough to give purpose to the faces she takes. During any valid Sacred Hunt, the Lunar may declare a purpose for the shape he is about to earn, associating it to a constellation and giving it similar properties to an Ascendent Destiny.<br /> In any scene where willpower has been spent to take or maintain that shape, the lunar recieves a target number reduction on actions related to the shape's assigned purpose as an astrological effect.<br /> <br /> Additionally, the Lunar may sacrifice a dot of willpower during that Sacred Hunt to create a resplendent destiny for the taken shape, spending points of willpower and limit to activate effects similar to Resplendencies.<br /> <br /> Next: <b>Irreverent Onslaught of Ideas</b> or <b>Magnanimous Onslaught of Principles</b><br /> (I'm not big on the &quot;choice&quot; subsystem)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T10:21:53-07:00","id":187232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=187143#post187143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Next: <b>Magnanimous Onslaught of Principles</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Raksha Cup. The raksha plays muse to a mortal, unstopping the inner wells of their creativity and unlocking great creative potential within them...delicious, delicious creative potential. For best flavor, wait until victim has fulfilled a Motivation based on great artistic achievement before consuming their soul. <br /> <br /> Next: <i>Hounds of Baying Midnight</i> or <i>Spinning the Murder Bone</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T11:17:07-07:00","id":187273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=187232#post187232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Hounds of Baying Midnight</i></div> </div> </div> </div><b>Abyssal Survival</b><br /> <br /> The deathknight reshapes a ghostly familiar into a terrible beast of the hunt and puts them on the scent of a quarry. The beast immediately seeks to track down and tear its quarry apart, and the quarry feels an intense fear when it hears the monster's baying or detects any other sign of its coming. Wrapped in protective midnight, the beast can even survive for a number of days in the sun's light equal to the Abyssal's Survival, though it loses a lethal health level for each such day in the sun; such health levels cannot be restored by any means until the transformation's end. The transformation lasts until the hunt is successful or the Abyssal calls off the hunt (which may only be done when the beast is subdued).<br /> <br /> A repurchase of this Charm allows an Abyssal to apply this transformation to any ghost, though unwilling spirits offer resistance. Other than the enhancements from this Charm and a new Defining Bond to track down and kill the quarry, the ghost retains its other traits. The Abyssal may treat it as a Familiar when it is on the hunt. Regardless of the hunt's conclusion, this Charm's effects end after a number of days equal to the Abyssal's Survival. When this transformation ends, the ghost may voluntarily take on a bestial shape, evocative of both its original form and this Charm's transformation, and may choose to become the deathknight's Familiar. At higher Essence, the Abyssal may attempt to force this last effect.<br /> <br /> New Charm:<br /> <i>Breaking the Gates of Sundraprisha</i><br /> or<br /> <i>Boars Between Bookcovers</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":". 07-03-2014, 02:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T02:01:20-07:00","id":187778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=187273#post187273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>Breaking the Gates of Sundraprisha</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Fair Folk Heart Charm<br /> <br /> With a final push of chaos against the pressure of order, the Noble breaks the duality of shaped and unshaped existence. This state cannot last, however, as the forces of order shuffle the altered Raksha towards a mechanism their kind should never touch. This mechanism is Lethe, for the Raksha has come to resemble a higher soul. When the 'soul' is again incarnated. the being born will be both Mortal and Noble as it benefits them. They will continue to incarnate in this way until they are devoured by a Han'ya or killed with a force that destroys the soul.<br /> It is to the benefit of creation that this apex is beyond the ken of any ordinary Rakshasthani.Noble, and moreso that they can never grasp the power of Exaltation.<br /> <br /> The Softest Agreement<br /> OR<br /> The Ripple In That Blood","signature":"","edited":{"userid":357,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/357-plotvitalnpc","user":"PlotVitalNPC","date":". 07-04-2014, 05:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/357-plotvitalnpc","name":"PlotVitalNPC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar357_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T20:24:32-07:00","id":191058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PlotVitalNPC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=187778#post187778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Softest Agreement</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Solar Bureaucracy</b><br /> <br /> The Quills of Heaven understand well the power of a contract. What's more, they understand the power of the <i>appearance</i> of a contract, no matter how toothless. With this Charm, the Solar may negotiate a one-sided contract with another party, offering concessions to this party's benefit in exchange for nothing or near to nothing. These &quot;concessions&quot; need not go beyond what the Solar or his party intended to do anyway and need contain no effective mechanisms for control or sanction, so long as the terms are still favorable to the other party. For instance, a Solar ruler may vow to encourage his people not to encroach on a Lunar's territory (never mind that he and his people hold no interest in the land and it is unfit for cultivation) or a Solar merchant may assure a Guild functionary that he will not pursue a city's prime export (even if the Solar is actively positioning himself for just that).<br /> <br /> Once struck, this agreement may be leveraged as though its terms are far more burdensome to the Solar or the Solar's party than they actually are, granting (bonus) to do so. Likewise, should the Lawgiver or his party fail to uphold the agreement, blame for doing so shifts seems to fall obviously on the other party's negotiation. If leveraging this fact, this reduces any appropriate penalties the Lawgiver or his party would face by (Bureaucracy - 1) not to extend beyond 0 and increases those faced by the other party by (Solar's Bureaucracy - 2).<br /> <br /> New Charm:<br /> <i>Boars Between Bookcovers</i><br /> or<br /> <i>One Beloved by Silver Sands</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T22:29:36-07:00","id":191125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=191058#post191058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Boars Between Bookcovers</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereal Stealth. Untethering the thread of his destiny from the bounds of space, the Sidereal may compress it infinitely to find concealment within the most unlikely of places\u2014the space between a teacup's bottom and the warm liquid that fills it, between the pages of a book, or behind a blinking eye. Unfolding to reveal one's self from this stealth is generally too wonky to make a sneak attack, but it delivers a substantial advantage Joining Battle upon ambushing an enemy. <br /> <br /> <b>New Charms</b>: Black Star Zodiac (can't be a Underworld Sidereal thing) <i>or</i> The Beginning is the End","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T23:15:13-07:00","id":191142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=191125#post191125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Black Star Zodiac</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunar Knack<br /> <br /> The noble beasts contained inside of the lunar have fallen to dead stars. From now on, while in one of their true shapes the lunar may elect to turn into a ghostly version of the same. While in such a state they are naturally material but may dematerialize and may respire essence as a ghost would, but are subject to any non-summoning non-banishment effects which target ghosts. Making use of this knack gives the lunar an automatic point of limit for each such transformation.<br /> <br /> New Charm: Detours are Shortcuts Cartography<br /> <br /> (Well, you said not an underworld SIDEREAL thing. I'm going to sit out for awhile now.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/357-plotvitalnpc","name":"PlotVitalNPC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar357_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-08T06:07:21-07:00","id":191326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PlotVitalNPC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=191142#post191142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Detours are Shortcuts Cartography</div> </div> </div> </div>Solar Survival<br /> <br /> Using his superior knowledge of his environment, the solar can take paths that would otherwise be seen as illogical or unpredictable detours without losing any time.<br /> <br /> When moving through familiar terrain such as a city or a forest, the solar can take a longer route, and arrive at his destination as though he took the fastest possible path that he could. This can be useful for foraging for food on the way back to the camp, taking a smith's sword on the way to a fight, or getting some coin from home while crossing the street to the pub.<br /> <br /> When using this charm to plan a trip, chart a course or set up a migration, the solar can include a number of detours into his path as long as they are within [some distance] of any point on the original course, without incurring extra travel time on the road (e.g. resupplying still takes it's normal time, but the travel time to get to and from those supplies isn't counted).<br /> <br /> (This charm can explicitly be placed in a combo with charms of other abilities, such as Athletics, Sail and Ride)<br /> <br /> <b>Searing White Emptiness</b><br /> <br /> or<br /> <br /> <b>Dreams in Answers Contemplation</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":".  Tried to balance it. Failed. 07-08-2014, 03:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-08T13:25:11-07:00","id":191653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=191326#post191326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Searing White Emptiness</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Shadowlands Circle Necromancy<br /> <br /> The Necromancer whispers into his cupped hands the terrible knowledge of Life, and bites back the shuddering terror that tries to drive him away from it. A burning numbness sets in along his fingertips, which ignite in white flame. He may discharge this spell by touching another entity, inflicting (his Charisma + Occult) in dice of damage, ignoring all non-natural soak. <br /> <br /> He has one action after his casting to discharge this spell freely--each one after that requires another willpower point to be spent to resist the effects of the spell on himself.<br /> <br /> If the target fills in a single one of their dying levels from this spell, they are instantly slain--the Necromancer grabs their soul and plunges it entirely into the solvent clarity of Lethe, and then tears it back through into the land of the living, into their own body to be reborn...after a fashion. Their body is consumed in white fire, but left unscathed and featureless, without any internal or external identifying features.<br /> <br /> Over the course of the next season, these develop along with its personality, although any similarities of passion or physiognomy are coincidental, and for a brief time the reborn entity learns at a staggering rate: at the end of this time, they possess all the traits of a normal mortal in the prime of their life.<br /> <br /> Non-human entities are generally likewise forced into a human existence for a lifetime; while many are reduced into permanent human reincarnation afterwards, some more puissant creatures (including all entities who exist as part of a hierarchy of souls) recover themselves--and ironically, their proper immortality--in death.<br /> <br /> <b>Sky-Shattering Apocalypse Prayer</b><br /> <br /> or<br /> <br /> <b>Songs-from-Stones</b> <b>Ear</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-08T21:57:46-07:00","id":191984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=191653#post191653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Songs-from-Stones Ear</b></div> </div> </div> </div><b>Lunar Perception</b><br /> <br /> There are rhythms in all things, though these hang beyond the perception of most creatures. Luna's Chosen pity ones so deaf. With this Charm, a Lunar may hear the internal cadence of an object or closely related group of objects. The Lunar may choose to roll Perception with Performance or another relevant Ability to harmonize the object's song with her actions, granting (bonus) in its use so long as the natural performance continues, with (lesser bonus) for those who witness the Lunar's display. Those who successfully copy the rhythm of the Lunar's performance may receive the full benefit. When using such a harmonized object to perform its song, the object is treated as a tool one grade superior for the purpose (including being treated as an appropriate tool at all). Alternatively, the Lunar may make the same roll at a greater difficulty to determine a perfectly discordant rhythm. She -- and any who duplicate this rhythm -- receives (bonus) to damage the object and (penalty) in its use so long as the disharmonious performance continues, with (lesser bonus/penalty) for those who bear witness.<br /> <br /> Objects minimally reshaped by directed effort, such as stone, bone, or unhardened leather, receive (benefit/discount) from this Charm, as their core songs ring through with little interference.<br /> <br /> New Charm:<br /> <i>Beloved by Silver Sands</i><br /> or<br /> <i>Where Angels Dare Not Tread</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-08T22:24:56-07:00","id":192011,"title":"","content":"<i>Beloved by Silver Sands</i><br /> <br /> <b>Dragonblooded Resistance: Earth-Aspected</b><br /> <br /> While this charm is in effect, the Terrestrial heals one lethal or bashing health level per combat action so long as they are in contact with soil, sand, clay, or some other natural equivalent. This charm ceases to function if the user is suspended in the air, in the water, or standing on metal, wood, pavement or some other artificial surface. Even crippling wounds are healed at the end of the scene, so long as earth is used to bind the flesh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1595-scatters-the-ashes","name":"Scatters-the-Ashes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1595_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-08T23:01:30-07:00","id":192051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scatters-the-Ashes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=192011#post192011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Beloved by Silver Sands</i><br /> <br /> <b>Dragonblooded Resistance: Earth-Aspected</b><br /> <br /> While this charm is in effect, the Terrestrial heals one lethal or bashing health level per combat action so long as they are in contact with soil, sand, clay, or some other natural equivalent. This charm ceases to function if the user is suspended in the air, in the water, or standing on metal, wood, pavement or some other artificial surface. Even crippling wounds are healed at the end of the scene, so long as earth is used to bind the flesh.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you suggest a name for the next charm?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-08T23:20:58-07:00","id":192092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=192051#post192051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you suggest a name for the next charm?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah! It is late at night and I forgot. <br /> How about <i>Pillar of Immutable Ivory</i><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1595-scatters-the-ashes","name":"Scatters-the-Ashes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1595_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-08T23:33:07-07:00","id":192103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scatters-the-Ashes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=192092#post192092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Pillar of Immutable Ivory</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Liminal Resistance<br /> <br /> The Chernozem takes a deep breath and forces his life-essence deep into his body, into his spine.<br /> The Liminal can ignore any wound penalties, including incapacitated and can not die, until his spine is damaged. At this point, their essence flows back into the rest of their body and the penalties are inflicted as normal.<br /> <br /> It was said that Liminals are durable figures, so this seemed appropriate.<br /> <br /> For our next Charm:<br /> Tomb-sundering Waltz.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-09T06:16:58-07:00","id":192312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=192103#post192103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tomb-sundering Waltz.</div> </div> </div> </div>Abyssal Performance<br /> <br /> The Abyssal is worse than any at conjuring life into dead, dry bones, but perhaps the best at faking it. With this Performance charm, all corpses within (Undefined Radius) spontaneously animate, and attempt to make their way to her--this charm aids them in this pursuit, adding the successes on the Abyssal's [Charisma + Performance] roll as successes of their own for the purposes of breaking through physical or supernatural barriers. These non-sapient undead join in the performance as best they can as they arrive (Adding their Magnitude to her successes), but unless acting under other bindings or compulsions, they will not attack the Deathknight or anyone in her vicinity.<br /> When the Abyssal terminates this charm, the corpses remain vaguely animate--standing, but unresponsive--until the end of the scene, at which point they resume their previous inert state. During this time, if the Deathknight wishes, she may use any suitable charms or necromancy at her disposal to animate them on a longer-term basis.<br /> <br /> Next up!<br /> Storm Mother's Sorrow<br /> or<br /> The Brilliance of Falling Stars","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-09T07:07:43-07:00","id":192377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=192312#post192312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Abyssal Performance</div> </div> </div> </div>Because this is Thriller?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-09T07:22:51-07:00","id":192384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=192377#post192377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because this is Thriller?</div> </div> </div> </div>Curiously enough, the first thing that leapt to mind was actually a flash animation called El Despertar--it wasn't until I was mostly done that I realized that the Thriller video was a potential application of it and actually much lot closer to what I'd written in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-09T08:33:38-07:00","id":192443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>The Brilliance of Falling Stars </b> </div> </div> </div><b>Cecelyne Occult:</b> The sky of hell hosts countless ancient wisdom, each individual is someone who has manage to piece together the Yozi's incomprehensible plan. By mediating at the stroke of midnight, the Infernal can gain a small glimpse of this source forbidden knowledge, she gain [Essence] points of Specialties that she can spend on any of her Abilities. These Specialties still obey the normal rule for Specialties and count as dice add by charm.<br /> <br /> Ghost-Calming Jizo Mantra or Screaming Garrote Execution<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-09T09:58:30-07:00","id":192490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=192443#post192443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghost-Calming Jizo Mantra</div> </div> </div> </div>Liminal Manipulation:<br /> The Chernozem speaks peaceful, calming words in a cool and droning voice. As long as she continues, ghosts and plasmic entities of lower Essence than her must ignore her presence, as well as up to her Manipulation in others she keeps at close range. Those under her protection lose this protection if they deliberately interact with one of the charmed dead.<br /> <br /> Next:<br /> Thousand-Boar Moka Largesse<br /> Or<br /> Dancing in Scarlet Rains","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-09T10:26:48-07:00","id":192504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=192490#post192490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thousand-Boar Moka Largesse</div> </div> </div> </div>Getimian Socialize<br /> <br /> Offering a gift to a local patron, the Getimian tunes himself to the balances of social and economic power in a region and sets himself up as a local dignitary from whom the locals wish to gain favor. As long as the Getimian is able to match or exceed the gifts or bribes she is given, she gains a daily increase in one relevant social background for the duration of the charm (Backing, Contacts, Influence, Fame, Resources, etc; the only exception is Allies), to a maximum of 5 or the Getimian's Essence, whichever is higher.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, when the Getimian's Yin pool exceeds her Yang pool, anyone plotting against her recieves a die penalty equal to half (rounded up) and a target number increase equal to half (rounded down) of the highest rating in a background affected by this charm. Conversely, when her Yang pool exceed her Yin pool during the charm's duration, the Getimian gains a die bonus equal to half (rounded up), and a target-number reduction equal to half(rounded down) of the same background in all social interactions on top of any other bonuses already afforded by said background.<br /> <br /> Next:<br /> <br /> <b>Dreams in Answers Contemplation</b><br /> or<br /> <b>Step of Manifold Ideologies</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 07-09-2014, 01:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-09T10:48:34-07:00","id":192519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=192504#post192504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Dreams in Answers Contemplation</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereal Investigation<br /> <br /> The Sidereal prays to the heavens for guidance, and finds that the cosmos will answer him with visions of the past or premonitions of the future. The next time the Sidereal sleeps, he will have a vivid dream that either suggests an answer to a problem currently plagues him, or directly shows him events that happened in the past as though he were present. The Sidereal can use this charm on another character, with or without their knowledge. That character will have visions as described above, which the Sidereal will not be privy to.<br /> <br /> Next:<br /> <b>Journey of a Thousand Miles Step</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-09T11:42:24-07:00","id":192551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=192519#post192519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Journey of a Thousand Miles Step</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Ceceline Charm<br /> <br /> With a touch, the infernal releases a fraction of ceceline onto a being, cursing them to feel a lifetime of travel with every step. While this charm doesn't affect it's victims physically, psychologically it wreaks havoc as the target feels the effects of traveling a barren wasteland in complete isolation.<br /> <br /> Every time she moves a yard, the target must roll Willpower contested by the Infernal's own. Every time the target fails, she forgets what she was doing as though a lifetime had passed and loses intimacies, background and ability dots and might change her Motivation (e.g. to &quot;Just survive&quot;) as though they simply faded through disuse or avoidance, or gains derangements that could be caused by prolonged isolation and depravation - in reality, the target simply forgets that she once had friends, or was capable of shooting a bow, as the ravages of time make the journey the only persistent memory.<br /> <br /> This charm lasts until the target has taken a number of steps equal to the infernal's essence, or until the infernal chooses to release the committed motes.<br /> <br /> The decision to remain completely motionless staves off this charm's effects, but unless the target dies cowering in the corner, they will have to move <i>some</i> time.<br /> <br /> Next:<br /> <br /> <b>Penitent Forgiveness Rain</b>.<br /> or<br /> <b>Dance of a million genocides.</b> (caveat: not abyssal performance)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 07-09-2014, 02:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-09T12:29:51-07:00","id":192619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=192551#post192551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Penitent Forgiveness Rain</b>.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Celestial Circle Sorcery<br /> <br /> Making the sign of Mercury with his left hand and the sign of Venus with his right, the Sorcerer casts a cry for mercy to Heaven so sharp that it tears open the sky, scattering clouds toward all four outer poles, and makes it weep a cleansing, shimmering rain all the same.<br /> <br /> There is no lightning to illuminate the sky, although a distant sussurus of thunder is a near constant.<br /> <br /> For five hours, those caught in the rain treat each scene they partake in as eroding a single negative intimacy. If the intimacy is wholly eroded, they regain willpower as though from a restful night's sleep, and further scenes erode a new intimacy. They may remember the intimacy with effort, but it seems vague and dreamlike, and often silly; any scene spent rebuilding it requires a point of willpower until it is fully re-established.<br /> <br /> Those who avoid the rain entirely merely treat the entire storm as a scene of erosion, while those who remain wholly exposed more than a scene treat every subsequent minute as a new scene of erosion.<br /> <br /> Next:<br /> <b>Indelible Horror Stain</b><br /> or<br /> <b>Unthorned Rose Technique</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-09T20:56:03-07:00","id":193092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=192619#post192619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Unthorned Rose Technique</b></div> </div> </div> </div><b>Liminal Appearance</b><br /> <br /> The Chernozem breathes a sweet breath upon his body. So long as this Charm is active, the Liminal's body becomes both more attractive and less threatening, extending appropriate bonuses and penalties when perceived. This Charm's effects also aid attempts to conceal scars, sutures, and other signs of his true nature.<br /> <br /> If the Liminal uses this Charm to treat a body part as he attaches it, it permanently bestows these effects upon it without demanding a commitment. These effects apply only if others perceive only body parts the Liminal has treated in this way. For instance, a single treated arm extending a come-hither gesture from an otherwise shrouded Liminal grants these effects, but they will not apply if his untreated other arm is visible.<br /> <br /> New Charm:<br /> <i>Where Angels Dare Not Tread</i><br /> or<br /> <i>Parting a Sea of Pearls</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T11:58:33-07:00","id":194862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=193092#post193092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Parting a Sea of Pearls</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Liminal Sail<br /> <br /> Pouring a waxy white ectoplasm out of it's mouth to coat the sea around itself or it's ship, the Liminal creates a wound in the ocean, a long-toothed maw whose teeth of corpus-infused water serve as cover, protecting everything inside from attacks (both long- and short-ranged such as arrows and ramming maneuvers).<br /> <br /> Additionally, the maw can raise and lower the ship, making it appear lighter or heavier, or even making it appear to sink.<br /> <br /> Next:<br /> <br /> <b>Black Earth Salted Thrice</b><br /> <br /> or <br /> <br /> <b>Incubation of Horrors and Prayers</b><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T12:39:20-07:00","id":194910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=194862#post194862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Black Earth Salted Thrice</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Abyssal War<br /> <br /> Where the Armies of Oblivion march all things die. An Abyssal with this Charm is not interested in conquering kingdoms, all he cares for is the blissful nothing that can only be found on the other side of the Final War. Whenever the Death Knight partakes in a battle during which both sides lose enough men to count as devastated he may activate this Charm. Blood seems to seep into the earth faster as plants wither and animals flee. Nothing will grow upon this blighted land and now animals will come and forage from it for 1 year and 1 day. No living creature can find anything to sustain itself for 1 mile around the battle sight and not even the wind dares to disturb the beautiful nothing the Abyssal has created with more then a soft, stale breeze. Any dead cannot be taken and refuse to burn during this time as well, the bodies seemingly waiting to be called to war once more. <br /> <br /> Next:<br /> <br /> Obscured by Starlight","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/777-bronze-tiger","name":"Bronze Tiger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T13:17:53-07:00","id":194934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bronze Tiger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=194910#post194910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Obscured by Starlight</div> </div> </div> </div>Greater Astrology/Sidereal Charm<br /> <br /> Grabbing at the strands of arcane fate, the Sidereal weaves this destiny around the something in the area. When those present for the scene next role to remember the Sidereal, their roll also applies to their ability to recall the relevance of the things or beings enveloped by the astrological effect to the scene, while obscuring memory of affected objects introduced during the scene. This charm cannot be used by a sidereal with an active resplendent destiny, as to share the Sidereal fate to be forgotten requires that that fate be expressed. If anything would cause the subjects thus concealed to gain paradox, it is instead taken on by the being who has symbolically made the subject a part of their own fate.<br /> <br /> Next:<br /> <br /> Auspicious Progeneration Gift","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/357-plotvitalnpc","name":"PlotVitalNPC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar357_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T06:29:43-07:00","id":196733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PlotVitalNPC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=194934#post194934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Auspicious Progeneration Gift</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunar Stamina<br /> <br /> Giving some of their blood to a creature, the Lunar is able to impart some of its fortean nature.<br /> <br /> In conjunction with this charm and a sacrifice of 1Lhl, the lunar may activate any charms or knacks that would affect her physical form (such as healing or regeneration charms, mutation charms, knacks such as Twin-faced Hero or Changing Plumage Mastery, etc.) at their normal cost [+surcharge maybe], imbuing the sacrificed blood with their effects. The receiving creature then benefits from the effects of those charms as though she had just activated them, for their normal duration (maximum 1 day).<br /> <br /> Releasing commitment to this charm ends all gifted effects over the course of 7 ticks.<br /> The blood cannot be stored, it must be consumed within a few minutes of this charm's activation, otherwise its effects and cost are wasted.<br /> <br /> Next:<br /> <b>Obsidian-Toothed Cavern Invitation</b><br /> or<br /> <b>Sands of flaying comforts</b> (Caveat, though not outright ban: avoid Cecelyne)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T07:01:55-07:00","id":196750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=196733#post196733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Obsidian-Toothed Cavern Invitation</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Abyssal Presence<br /> <br /> Subtly stripping her target of every shred of fear, the Abyssal renders her foes gentle lambs for slaughter. While under the effects of this charm, the target can react to clear and present threats to their well-being with perfect clarity of mind, but the Abyssal reduces the target's MDV by her Essence for any attempts the Deathknight makes to gloss over or conceal eerie surroundings, strange noises, an excess of martial or mordbid decor, or other such trappings. She also adds an external penalty of the same amount for any other rolls the target makes to notice the same. For the duration of this charm, the target's Valor is treated as the higher of either its natural value or the Abyssal's Performance solely for the purpose of resisting or overcoming fear.<br /> <br /> NEXT:<br /> <br /> <b>White Walls and Scarlet Blood</b><br /> <br /> OR<br /> <br /> <b>Three Crowns for Four Kings</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T22:09:03-07:00","id":197522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=196750#post196750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Three Crowns for Four Kings</b></div> </div> </div> </div><b>Sidereal Larceny</b><br /> <br /> Even the loftiest rewards can fall within the reach of ones united toward a common cause. Alas, it sometimes serves destiny's ends to purloin that unity, and turn its prior owners against one another. When engaging in social influence with a group that shares a common goal, this Charm may supplement a Sidereal's attempt to instill a belief that the rewards of achieving the goal will not be enough to go around. The Charm does not function if it is unclear how this could be so for the goal in question (for instance, if the goal is only to see that a village has food enough to eat and none of the group care for fame, the Sidereal may have his work cut out for him).<br /> <br /> If successful, group members who hear his words automatically develop a Minor tie of mistrust toward other group members and a Minor tie of selfish desire for the fruits of the venture's labor. If similar Intimacies already exist, their respective grades increase by one and change their contexts to the ones described. These Intimacies may not be degraded by mundane means without compelling evidence that the reward is enough to go around, such as proof that this is so or by a sufficient reduction in the number who stand to be rewarded (by whatever means this takes).<br /> <br /> New Charm:<br /> <i>Where Angels Dare Not Tread</i><br /> or<br /> <i>Hungry Eyes and Empty Hearts</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":". 07-15-2014, 01:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-15T07:35:50-07:00","id":197914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=197522#post197522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Hungry Eyes and Empty Hearts</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Raksha feeding charm, requiring Banquet of Crumbs and Gaping Virtue Mouth.<br /> <br /> A raksha's hunger knows no bounds, not even ownership or shape can stave off it's own gluttony. Using this charm during feeding, a Raksha can imbue an Enchanted creation-born with the Raksha's own hunger. The target gains the ability to feed on virtues as a Raksha would (using a virtue of the Raksha's choosing as though she posessed a Feeding Grace), and feels an endless hunger that compells them to do so. However, such feeding can only be used to create gossamer, and yields no other possible (mechanical) rewards.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, if and when the target posesses Gossamer, she is compelled to hoard it in a hiding place of the Raksha's choosing.<br /> <br /> Lastly, the Raksha has a general idea of the status of each such creation-born.<br /> <br /> This charm can be warded off or dispelled by prolonged contact with Iron (i.e. at least a couple of actions so that attacks don't automatically negate it, but grapples could).<br /> <br /> Next:<br /> <br /> <b>Fractal Cultures Defence</b><br /> or<br /> <b>Recursive Shaping Methodology</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-15T20:38:22-07:00","id":198529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=197914#post197914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Recursive Shaping Methodology</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Pyrian Charm, requires Sorcerous Enlightement of She Who Lives In Her Name.<br /> As she shapes the world, the Infernal does not tie off her sorcery but instead forces the world to remain malleable to her will, turning the end of one spell into the beginning of another.<br /> When the Infernal has cast a spell of any circle of Sorcery, she may immediately begin a new Shape Sorcery action for a new spell of the same or of a lesser circle. There is no limit on the number of spells she may theoretically cast outside of the limits of her Willpower and Essence pools, but she cannot invoke this charm to continue after the invocation of a spell or ability that reduces casting time, such as any Countermagic spell.<br /> <br /> Next:<br /> <b>Fire-in-the-Blood Style</b><br /> OR<br /> <b>Unblinking Sungazer Soul</b><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T11:45:33-07:00","id":199134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=198529#post198529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Unblinking Sungazer Soul</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Solar Awareness. Honing his vision to pierce the skies, the Solar's visual range when scanning the skies is extended to an extreme degree, unhindered by harsh sunlight or stormclouds alike. Provides hefty bonuses when combating aerial enemies from the ground, or a lower vantage point, and is probably useful in piloting a skyship. <br /> <br /> Next: <b>Wolves Among Sheep Guardianship</b> or <b>Anchor-Shattering Launch</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T16:45:37-07:00","id":199405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kukla</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <b>Trinity Collapsar Fist</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Theion Charm, supplementing an unarmed melee attack so that Fate bows to the whims of the Empyreal Chaos and collapses in on the target, Crippling them and inflicting punishments similar to Paradox.<br /> <br /> Next: <b>Battle-Demon Dueling Trance</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/2480852/chapters/5503997\" target=\"_blank\">Glorious Echeladder Ascension Technique</a> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/287292-glorious-echeladder-ascension-technique-a-homestuck-exalted-crossover\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Topic</a><br /> <br /> &quot;Look, sometimes you just are in the mood to play the divinely empowered champion of the God of Farts. Mechanically optimized play is not the only way to enjoy playing your character.&quot; -Wise Old Guru","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1048-ryumaru","name":"Ryumaru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1048_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T17:35:11-07:00","id":199461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryumaru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=199405#post199405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Next: <b>Battle-Demon Dueling Trance</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Solar Integrity, Permanent.<br /> <br /> The warriors of the sun never stray from righteous violence. When in battle, the Exalt's mind is so focused that she is counted as having a Major intimacy against stopping the fight when anybody tries to influence her socially.<br /> <br /> Now... either :<b> Emerald Blood Atemi</b><br /> or<br /> <b>Twisting Towers of Madness</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ultimate Jade-Screened Exalted Scholar, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304239-my-next-campaign-tdhr-peach\" target=\"_blank\">THDR : Future Dragon-Blooded campaign</a>, and other links.<br /> If you like Ex3, you can support <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/holdenshearer\" target=\"_blank\">Holden</a> on Patreon!","edited":{"userid":541,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/541-letipex","user":"LeTipex","date":". 07-16-2014, 08:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/541-letipex","name":"LeTipex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"902"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T18:24:56-07:00","id":199489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LeTipex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=199461#post199461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Twisting Towers of Madness</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Solar Sorcery<br /> <br /> The sorcerer speaks from the Incomprehensible Verse, as many phrases as she is able or desires. She captures each impossibile stanza in the palm of her hand and throws it into the ground, where it erupts into a twisting tower. These towers each hold a terrible mental trial that can rend sanity from those who attempt to scale it. Those who do, however, find great truths and information they seek. Each time the a tower is fully scaled, it becomes more comprehensible, thus its integrity weakens. Eventually, the tower crumbles, and falls.<br /> <br /> There are still towers standing in the Time of Tumult, left from ages long past. Some are tall and strong, holding many secrets, while others are ruins with but one truth remaining. Any who dare scale one of these towers may find great revelations of ages long since forgotten, but may also suffer so great a madness they cannot act upon it.<br /> <br /> Next Charm: <b>Thousand Eyes Watching</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T20:20:28-07:00","id":199577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Limited Reagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=199489#post199489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Thousand Eyes Watching</b></div> </div> </div> </div>(Lunar Appearance, has Observed Predator Instinct as a prerequisite)<br /> This charm creates an Illusion that the target is seen. No matter where they go, the certainty that <i>something</i> is watching them--which stubbornly refuses to make its presence known--follows them.This charm may enhance its prerequisite; rather than specifying a target, the Lunar piggybacks this effect onto the knowledge that the Lunar does see them. Regardless, this effect inflicts an internal penalty to the target's rolls to become or remain hidden by the Lunar's Essence, to a maximum of five.<br /> <br /> This charm requires 1 willpower to resist a scene; when the target has spent three willpower they may feel assured that nothing is <i>actually </i>watching them. <br /> <br /> Unless they are.<br /> <br /> NEXT: <b>Wet Ink on Ancient Scriptures</b><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T02:11:42-07:00","id":199841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=199134#post199134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Anchor-Shattering Launch</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Infernal Malfeas. Taking a deep breath, Infernal focuses his strength and lifts a ship (or any other big transportation device) off the ground. He then throws it into the sky, blazing ribbons of essence spreading from the ship like wings. With a reflexive (Dexterity + Athletics) roll Infernal can cling on to the ship as it is launched. The ship lands safely within (Essence) * 10 miles from the launch point. Any non-magical devices that prevent the vehicle from moving (like anchors) are shattered by the Infernal's mighty throw. At Essence 5 the ship can be thrown anywhere the Infernal has previously been.<br /> <br /> Next: <b>Exiled Knight Obfuscation</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","name":"Mahasamatman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2347_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T02:27:25-07:00","id":199855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=199577#post199577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">NEXT: <b>Wet Ink on Ancient Scriptures</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Infernal, Ebon Dragon. In his infinite deviousness, the Ebon Dragon twists future, past and present alike. With but a simple gesture, warlock changes the text on a written source. At Essence 5, application of this charm changes all existing copies of the document.<br /> Keyword: Shaping.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","name":"Mahasamatman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2347_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T07:43:29-07:00","id":200026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahasamatman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=199841#post199841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Next: <b>Exiled Knight Obfuscation</b></div> </div> </div> </div>First Evocation of Walks-Like-Kings, a cloak-and-rapier artifact of Starmetal and pitch-black silk that seems to glitter with the light of the stars when seen at night.<br /> <br /> No matter his outward appearance, one protected by this cloak will always find respite. For as long as it is worn, this pair of artifacts makes its bearer look like an unjustly exiled hero and suppresses any connection the wearer might have to criminals or infamy in the minds of people he meets. It doesn't so much erase the knowledge as make the logical connection any such criminals or infamy might have to the character extremely hard to make (but not impossible). Mecahnically, it suppresses Fame, Wanted, Influence, Cult and other such merits whenever it would be disadvantageous for the character to have such traits.<br /> <br /> Next: <b>Compassion Walks No Roads Proclamation</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T08:08:20-07:00","id":200039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=200026#post200026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <b>Compassion Walks No Roads Proclamation</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Infernal Charm, Ebon Dragon<br /> Charity begins at home; until the Shadow of All Things gets around to taking care of <i>that</i> little cosmic defect, it can stay there.<br /> The Infernal may use this charm on any target within his eyesight. As an Emotion effect, that target becomes exempt from mercy or care to the world: unless they have an extant intimacy toward her, even the gentlest saint is uncompelled by his compassion to help her in her hour of need, nor may they channel that virtue to aid her. <br /> Those around the target may spend a willpower point to resist the effects of this charm for a scene.<br /> This charm is a sorcerous effect which can be countered by Emerald Countermagic.<br /> <br /> Next: <b>Storm-Swollen Flood Onslaught</b><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T08:43:31-07:00","id":200058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=200039#post200039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Next: <b>Storm-Swollen Flood Onslaught</b></div> </div> </div> </div><b>Hegra Throw Charm</b><br /> <br /> Foul vapour constantly risen from the Demon City into hellish sky, and the Prismatic Monsoon answer back with a torrent of her own. The Infernal make an attack roll and applies it again everyone in a 45-degree arc with a range equal to his Essence. By paying a Bashing Heath Level, he can also purge any disease and poison currently in his system and combine them into his attack as needles leave corrosive trail while charkams fill the air with horrid stench, making it so that anyone who is wound from the onslaught also be affect by maladies reject by the Infernal. Note that this charm can only negate actual poisons and disease, not effects stemming from the Sickness or Poison keyword.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Iron River in Sleeve Strike</b><br /> <br /> or<br /> <br /> <b>Steel Rain from Sky Assault</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T10:31:12-07:00","id":200216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=200058#post200058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Steel Rain from Sky Assault</b></div> </div> </div> </div>A cluster of Alchemical charms, one for each element (although without access to Creation, the Big Five elements are probably not accessible, or are extremely rare designs)<br /> <br /> This charm installs a series of small cannons inside the Alchemical's back. Upon activation, the weapons fire bolts imbued with concentrated Elemental Essence into the air that rain from the sky for the remainder of the Alchemical's action, creating an area with [some hazard rating] within [shortbow-ish range] customizable by the Exalt upon purchase. (Examples include firing molten mercury for a fire hazard, miniature smoke grenades for a Smoke hazard, etc.) Each &quot;customized&quot; version is it's own separate charm.<br /> <br /> The mote cost for this charm can be paid again at the beginning of the alchemical's every action to continue the effect. Once the charm is deactivated, the fired projectiles dissolve into oil and steel shavings, and eventually back into Elemental Essence.<br /> <br /> Next: <b>The Most Comforting of Lies</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 07-17-2014, 03:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-18T08:19:22-07:00","id":201152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=200216#post200216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The Most Comforting of Lies</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereal Medicine:<br /> The Vizier arranges for Saturn to take her due at a slightly later date, holding a dying mortal in escrow for a brief time.<br /> <br /> The target of this charm rises up unharmed, and constructs memories that elide whatever brought him to an untimely end. As long as the Sidereal commits Essence to this charm, the mortal retains all the trappings and appearances of life; while the target can be targeted by effects that play upon his technically-undead status, this charm opposes them.<br /> <br /> If the target of this charm learns the truth of his death, the Sidereal must immediately re-invoke this charm (which causes the target to forget what he has just immediately learned) or it terminates.<br /> <br /> Next: <b>Flame-Shod Cavalry Style</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-18T08:30:42-07:00","id":201182,"title":"","content":"Dragon-Blooded War Charm.<br /> <br /> The Dragon-Blooded pushes her troops relentlessly, allowing to arrive at their destination far faster than would normally be expected.<br /> <br /> Next: <b>King-at-Leisure Rulership Method</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-18T09:05:58-07:00","id":201193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=201182#post201182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>King-at-Leisure Rulership Method</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Solar Bureaucracy<br /> <br /> Imbue a mortal that (or your familiar, to have e.g. an Eagle rule a nation) with your bureaucratic skill (and Merits) and be aware of all their decisions, with an upgrade that allows you to communicate or maybe impose compulsions/obsessions on said mortal. Basically allowing you to rule a kingdom while you're out adventuring, and letting someone else do the extended actions of figuring out and writing policies and treaties.<br /> <br /> Next: <b>Parasitic Diplomacy Sutra</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-18T09:26:36-07:00","id":201197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=201193#post201193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Parasitic Diplomacy Sutra</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Abyssal Bureaucracy:<br /> There must always be a winner, and there must always be a loser. Really, reasons the deathknight, in the end there are only losers, and then nothing at all...but at least there are those who lose <i>first.</i><br /> This charm targets an Organization, allowing the Deathknight to use an Organization which she has authority in--or of which she is a special asset--to make secret attempts to reduce the traits of the target organization. She must roll Manipulation + Bureaucracy against [a relevant difficulty or die pool] to succeed in making her attempt secret; while the target organization is likely well aware of the damages taken, they come across as the result of happenstance, or the malice of Organizations with which they are already in conflict.<br /> This charm requires that the target Organization and the Deathknight's organization be in contact, but not conflict.<br /> <br /> Next: <b>Evanescent Firefly Dance</b><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-18T10:59:06-07:00","id":201280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=201197#post201197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Evanescent Firefly Dance</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Dragon-Blooded Socialize:<br /> The children of Hesiesh knows that a good distraction is sometimes key. This charm may be invoked in a social event where at least 20 persons are present. The Dragon-Blooded skips from guest to guest, always seemingly demanded elsewhere, before suddenly leaving the party without anyone noticing. This charm imposes a supernatural mental influence on all guests that forces them to believe the Terrestrial is too busy with someone else to be disturbed. As such no one will come looking for him. This Charm lasts until the end of the party or a number of [Essence Scenes], whichever comes first. If the Dragon-Blooded is not back by then, people will start noticing that he left.<br /> <br /> Next:<br /> <b>Order-is-Chaos Meditation</b><br /> <br /> OR<br /> <br /> <b>Butterfly-Effect Annihilation</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-18T11:20:34-07:00","id":201292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=201280#post201280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Butterfly-Effect Annihilation</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereal Brawl:<br /> The Sidereal meditates upon the web of fate and gains insight in how it will destroy her opposition. The Sidereal performs a small, at a glance pointless action, thereby altering fate slightly to her advantage. At any point after using this charm, the Sidereal can declare that its effect takes place at that moment. This causes an enviromental hazard that has to be specified by the Sidereal. A tree falls over, a pillar collapses, a bull charges into the opponent. This hazard counts as a surprise attack and it's properties are dependent on the nature of the hazard. Because this Charm is very intimately tied to fate, no more than [Essence] Butterfly-Effect Annihilations can be stacked.<br /> <br /> Yes, the Sidereals are very, very well prepared.<br /> <br /> <b>Slay one to Slay a Thousand Tactic.</b><br /> <br /> OR<br /> <br /> <b>Snake Beneath Flower Inflection</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-18T12:28:44-07:00","id":201343,"title":"","content":"<b>Snake Beneath Flower Inflection (Terrestrial Socialise; Wood favoured)</b><br /> This Charm allows the Dragon-Blooded to seduce a target covertly, using nothing but glances and secret harmonies of the voice. It also impresses the need for secrecy on the intended target.<br /> If the attempt at seduction succeeds, the target suffers a penalty to their soak and Stamina rolls.<br /> <br /> Next:<br /> <b>Dancing Devil Paracosm</b> OR <b>Left-Handed Hummingbird Strike</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":97,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","user":"The MG","date":". 07-18-2014, 03:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-18T13:26:51-07:00","id":201413,"title":"","content":"Wrote it out, missed my chance, I'll post it anyway:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=201292#post201292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Slay one to Slay a Thousand Tactic.</b></div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Getimian War<br /> <br /> The bonds of Fate weigh heaviest on groups, stemming from followers and coiling around leaders.<br /> <br /> An attack supplemented by this charm exploits these shackles, targeting the leader of a unit, group or organisation.<br /> <br /> Reducing the Raw Damage of her attack by 1 die, the Getimian spreads the Fate of Endings throughout the chains of command, doubling the amount of targets affected by the attack - these new targets need not be within any range, the only requirement is that they are ranked lower than the highest ranking target affected by this charm.<br /> <br /> This charm can be invoked any amount of times, as long as the Getimian has Essence to spend and the raw damage of the attack is above 0.<br /> <br /> 20 raw damage could be reduced by 10 dice (for around 3 motes per die + 1wp ) to deal 10 raw damage to 1024 targets.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Moving on:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=201343#post201343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Dancing Devil Paracosm</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Solar Performance rquiring Phantom Conjuring Performance<br /> <br /> Through a stirring performance, the solar rouses the imaginations of his audience into taking over their senses.<br /> <br /> As long as the Solar performs, all targets of his performance believe themselves to be in a world described by the Solar - for better or for worse - and those that <i>want</i> to believe can keep the effects of this charm going for themselves.<br /> The solar overwrites any and potentially all senses with his descriptions, and can make friends and family seem like hellspawn or trees, or simply seem to disappear. He can make himself seem like a specific Emperor or the Silent Wind of Malfeas for example. During the performance, all these changes seem absolutely real to their targets, but once the charm expires are considered to be all part of a particularly compelling show that got everyone too carried away, and not actual events that transpired (unless other efforts are made to that effect).<br /> <br /> Next: <b>Self Dissolving Truth</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T13:51:12-07:00","id":202351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=201413#post201413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Self Dissolving Truth</b></div> </div> </div> </div><b>Raksha Heart</b><br /> <br /> The Fair Folk understand that there is sometimes value in not being themselves, and may use this Charm to create deep-cover identities. When using this Charm, the raksha loses all memory of the life he has led and all of a his Intimacies cease to affect them, and are recorded separately. In their place, he acquires a new personal history and new set of appropriate Intimacies equal in number to his Heart Grace, as well as a minor Tie to the idea that he is the false life. A raksha with a Heart Grace of 3 may make this Tie Major, while one with a Heart Grace of 4+ may make this Defining. If this Intimacy is stripped away, the raksha's false life dissipates and the original one returns.<br /> <br /> He may also select (Heart Grace - 1) conditions for the end of the false life. Each condition may either end the false life once it is met, or must be met in addition to the raksha's Tie to its false life. These conditions often involve the erosion or change in context of the false life's Intimacies, sometimes called &quot;pivotal&quot; Intimacies by the Fair Folk.<br /> <br /> At the false life's end, the raksha remembers the original and false lives just as well (and by default knows which is which), while his Intimacies mostly return to what they were. The exceptions include any new Intimacies or contexts to old Intimacies the Creation-born caused the fey to develop during its false life However, the raksha's player and Storyteller may feel the false identity left an impression, particularly if the raksha spent a considerable length of time with it. If they agree, the Fair Folk's present set of Intimacies generally skew toward the original's, but may become a blend of the false life's and the original's, as seems appropriate to them. For instance, if a cataphract with a Major Tie of hatred for a character adopts a false life in which he has a Major or Defining Tie of love instead, he may after a long time return to find that his Tie of hatred has been degraded (perhaps completely) and/or changed its context; he may also or instead find that it has been joined by a Minor, Major, or Defining Tie of love for the character.<br /> <br /> A repurchase of this Charm allows the raksha to use this Charm on behalf of any character whose Heart Grace he owns.<br /> <br /> New Charm:<br /> <i>Pearls Before Swine Invitation</i><br /> or<br /> <i>Water Follows Wind Kata</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T09:08:26-07:00","id":203888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=202351#post202351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Pearls Before Swine Invitation</i></div> </div> </div> </div><b>Lunar Manipulation</b><br /> <br /> Using something the target would want as a distraction, the Lunar offers something potentially dangerous as a minor stepping stone to it.<br /> <br /> The Lunar rolls a [contested roll], modified by the Distraction's Resources or Appearance rating and the target's Intimacy level to it (if applicable). If the Lunar succeeds, he innocuously slips a potentially lethal suggestion as a requirement for attaining the Distraction, that the target accepts without really thinking about it.<br /> <br /> Examples include &quot;You can have this Swine, but you have to eat these [poison-coated] pearls first&quot;; &quot;You can take me as a lover, but you must alter your will to include me first&quot;; &quot;You can have all my gold, but you must first rip out your own heart and present it to me.&quot;.<br /> <br /> the target proceeds to fulfill the requirement a though it was no big deal. However, anyone attempting to point out the lethality or recklessness of the target's actions (such as &quot;you're killing yourself!&quot; or &quot;he's trying to take everything you own!&quot;) allows a re-roll against the Lunar's original successes, and may allow the target to spend a point of willpower to augment his chances at success, or spend [the Lunar's Essence] willpower all at once to shake off the effect completely.<br /> <br /> Next: <b>Mirrored Mores Mansion</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T11:35:29-07:00","id":204022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=203888#post203888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Next: <b>Mirrored Mores Mansion</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Lunar Manipulation.<br /> <br /> The Chosen of Luna sometimes invite madness into their homes. For what reasons, only the Moonchildren can truly know.<br /> <br /> This Charm alters the minds of any character that sets foot in the Lunar's territory, though this may be limited to (Essence) select areas within the territory, at the Lunar's option. For example, an Essence 3 Lunar could choose to have her entire territory affected by this Charm, or she could choose to only have its effects apply within her home, in the forests bordering her territory, and the area of the sacred spring where she practices Sorcery. Regardless of this choice, this Charm alters the social perceptions and understandings of any character within the boundaries of its effects, causing them to believe the opposite of what they normally would; what was considered polite is now considered rude, and customs of sacred hospitality may exist where none did before. This is an Illusion effect.<br /> <br /> For any character (besides the Lunar herself and other Essence-users) that remains within the boundaries of this Charm's effects for more than a week, this ceases to be an Illusion effect and they believe that this is and has been their cultural practice the entire time, or at least that such beliefs are those of the region. The cost of this Charm must remain committed, however, for this to continue. Once the commitment lapses, the original customs and practices begin to return to public memory, though the Lunar may begin using social attacks to actually alter the beliefs of those subject to this Charm, with a +3 bonus to any relevant rolls - it's very easy to convince someone of something they already believe, after all. This bonus is reduced to +2 after three days, and only +1 after a week, as the original memories begin to return to the populace. After (10 + Lunar's Essence) days, this effect fades entirely, as the memories will have returned completely.<br /> <br /> Let me see... <b>Sword and Rose Champion Training</b> or <b>Badge of the Law Righteousness</b><br /> <br /> Bonus points if you name the book series (serii?) these names refer to!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/2480852/chapters/5503997\" target=\"_blank\">Glorious Echeladder Ascension Technique</a> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/287292-glorious-echeladder-ascension-technique-a-homestuck-exalted-crossover\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Topic</a><br /> <br /> &quot;Look, sometimes you just are in the mood to play the divinely empowered champion of the God of Farts. Mechanically optimized play is not the only way to enjoy playing your character.&quot; -Wise Old Guru","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1048-ryumaru","name":"Ryumaru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1048_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T23:14:13-07:00","id":204697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryumaru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=204022#post204022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bonus points if you name the book series (serii?) these names refer to!</div> </div> </div> </div>Alas, outside an outrageous stroke of luck, the Charm is unlikely to suit the series I don't know. ^_^o Cool idea to theme them, though! Think I'll borrow that...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Sword and Rose Champion Training</b> </div> </div> </div><b>Infernal Lore</b> (Szoreny)<br /> <br /> When a warlock seeks to cultivate a paragon, true devotion is the only proper soil. On activating this Charm, the Green Sun Prince names an ideal for her chosen pupil and plants an appropriate silver seed in his heart with a touch. The silver sands around it will preserve it, but only for (Lore) days, during which time the Infernal may change a Minor Intimacy's context to relate to the named ideal. For instance, a warlock seeking to make a great swordsman might convince the man he can win the town's respect by doing so. If successful, the seed's life is no longer on the clock, and it provides the pupil with &lt;benefit&gt; when he acts toward becoming the ideal in question. However, while the Intimacy is still ostensibly about its original subject, the pupil now cares for it only where it overlaps the ideal. Further, &lt;relevant social influence effect&gt; works to likewise change the context of another Minor Intimacy whenever he enjoys the &lt;benefit&gt;.<br /> <br /> This proceeds through the pupil's other Minor Intimacies, with the warlock's personal attempts to convert them having identical effects. With a total of three converted (or as many as the pupil possesses, if fewer), work may begin on the Major Intimacies. With the first Major Intimacy, the demon plant in the pupil's heart begins to bud and &lt;the benefit&gt; increases. With a total of two converted (or as many as the pupil possesses, if fewer), the seed may at last begin to seize a Defining Intimacy. With success, the pupil receives &lt;additional benefit&gt;, as the Infernal's efforts yield a blossoming silver rose of roots in the paragon's heart. The pupil becomes an automaton, able to live the ideal and do little else.<br /> <br /> Should anyone successfully change the context of the pupil's highest-converted Intimacy away from the ideal's -- a task with difficulty increased by 2 -- the demon plant withers and dies, and all effects end, all other affected Intimacies returning to their original contexts.<br /> <br /> New Charm:<br /> <i>Ill Met by Moonlight</i><br /> or<br /> <i>Full of Sound and Fury</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T23:30:25-07:00","id":209131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=204697#post204697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Full of Sound and Fury</b></div> </div> </div> </div><b>Infernal Presence </b>(Malfeas)<br /> <br /> Malfeas is a creature of great, all-encompassing rage, if any lesser creature were to experience his anger, they would run in fear. With the help of a Warlock, this event can happen.<br /> The Warlock takes a deep breath and shouts of a command, carrying the presence of Malfeas in their voice, encompassing only a fraction of his fury. Anyone within a mile of the Warlock can hear it. Upon hearing it, the listener must roll (Integrity+Stamina) against the Warlock's (Presence+Charisma+Essence). If the listener fails, he will instantly try to accomplish the task the Infernal commanded, in addition, he instantly develops an intimacy of intense fear towards both the Warlock and Malfeas.<br /> <br /> I just realized you could use this charm to convince everyone within a mile to bring you cookies... Malfaes isn't really a subtle guy I guess.<br /> <br /> So next:<br /> <br /> <b>Strung like Iron Wire Stance</b><br /> <br /> Or<br /> <br /> <b>Six-fingered Handshake Greeting</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T05:12:29-07:00","id":209273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=209131#post209131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Strung like Iron Wire Stance</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Celestial Martial Arts (Wire-Strung Temple Style?)<br /> <br /> The Martial Artist takes a precarious stance, seeming still; but every muscle in his body is tense and ready to unleash a multitude of lashings. When activating this charm, the Martial artist rolls Dexterity + Martial Arts + Essece. Each success on this roll provides a +1 PDV bonus and one full-dicepool counterattack until the Martial Artist's next action (with the exception of Defend and Defend Other actions, which prolong this effect). Dodging or Moving (or being moved) cancels this effect.<br /> <br /> A later charm would allow the use of several such counterattacks against a single attack, like a multitude of wires snapping and recoiling against one blow.<br /> <br /> Next: <b>Coruscant Mandalas of the Sun</b> or <b>Space-Severing Scripture</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T10:21:57-07:00","id":209385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=209273#post209273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Space-Severing Scripture</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereal Linguistics. After spending hours, days, or weeks writing the story of a voyage from one locale to another, the Sidereal may cast her writing into the fire, reweaving reality such that the journey has already been undertaken (and perhaps some events described along the way, as well). While this can be used for personal transport, it can also be used to write third parties into different locations, making the arrangement of proper love matches or encounters much easier. Using this against an unwilling Exalt is difficult, if not impossible. <br /> <br /> Next: <b>Ten-Ton Talisman Blessing</b> or <b>Necklace Turns The Head</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T11:01:15-07:00","id":209421,"title":"","content":"<b>Necklace Turns The Head</b><br /> <br /> Sidereal Craft. The right gift at the right time can make a great difference - and the Sidereal can make sure her gift is the right one, and at the right time. By weaving strands of Fate into a small trinket he crafts, the Star-Chosen can then offer it as a gift to a person she is already familiar with, which will be well-received. That person will subsequently become even more favourable towards the Sidereal and pliable to his suggestions.<br /> <br /> Next:<b> Delight in the Unbidden.</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T08:18:49-07:00","id":213604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=209421#post209421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Next:<b> Delight in the Unbidden.</b></div> </div> </div> </div><b>Adorjan Thrown</b><br /> <br /> Uninvited guests are fun, more thing to murder are always welcome ! Everytime the Infernal witness another make a Join Battle action after the fight has began, all her attacks enjoy a Speed reduction of (the enemy's Magnitude) for one scene, however if this would reduce her attack speed to 3 then she immediately enter a killing frenzy as if she just suffers from an uncontrolled Berserk Anger Limit Break as an Emotion effect, the excitement to kill overdrive all of her though process.<br /> <br /> <b>Hostility-Killing Confession </b><br /> <br /> or<br /> <br /> <b>Hanuman's Wild Dance</b><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 07-30-2014, 11:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T09:00:46-07:00","id":213631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=213604#post213604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Hostility-Killing Confession </b></div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereal Socialize<br /> <br /> By verifying a target's Intimacy, giving it truth and grounding, the Vizier gives them a rush of catharsis and sets them free. The Sidereal invokes this charm when making a revelation germane to one of his target's intimacies. This must be a genuine revelation--both true as far as the Sidereal knows and unknown to his target--but placing it on the table fulfills the relevant intimacy so fully that she can no longer contain it. The Sidereal rolls [a relevant roll] versus his target's MDV, Success means that the target loses the Intimacy until they take the time to rebuild it, but instantly roll to gain willpower as though they had enjoyed a restful night's sleep. Further, they cannot take actions that would support the intimacy for the rest of the scene.<br /> Even if they fail, the scene is still treated as though the target had spent that time eroding the intimacy unless she spends a point of willpower.<br /> <br /> <b>A Study in Soulsteel</b><br /> or<br /> <b>Five Fathoms Sea-Change</b> <b>Style</b><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T09:46:35-07:00","id":213676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=204697#post204697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alas, outside an outrageous stroke of luck, the Charm is unlikely to suit the series I don't know. ^_^o Cool idea to theme them, though! Think I'll borrow that...</div> </div> </div> </div>The first is a reference to the Redwall novels, with it's constant use of swords and roses as motifs. The second is Discworld, because Sam Vimes is &quot;the LAW you sons of bitches!&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=213631#post213631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Five Fathoms Sea-Change</b> <b>Style</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Dragon-Blood Sail. By diving into the depths and reading the currents of both the ocean and the Essence of the ocean, the Terrestrial can determine how to change their course and guide her ship to its destination quickly and safely. This also allows the Terrestrial to alter the currents with a successful Intelligence + Sail roll, with a Difficulty dependent on the effect she desires. Calming the seas is only Difficulty 1, or 2 if they are rough. Making the seas rough is Difficulty 2. This scale ends at Difficulty 5 to create a massive tidal wave in the direction of the Terrestrial's choice.<br /> <br /> <b>Shattered Dreams Route</b> or <b>Promise to Forever Haunt</b><br /> <br /> Once again, themed! This time it's music.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/2480852/chapters/5503997\" target=\"_blank\">Glorious Echeladder Ascension Technique</a> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/287292-glorious-echeladder-ascension-technique-a-homestuck-exalted-crossover\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Topic</a><br /> <br /> &quot;Look, sometimes you just are in the mood to play the divinely empowered champion of the God of Farts. Mechanically optimized play is not the only way to enjoy playing your character.&quot; -Wise Old Guru","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1048-ryumaru","name":"Ryumaru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1048_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T12:01:39-07:00","id":213811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryumaru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=213676#post213676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Shattered Dreams Route</b> or <b>Promise to Forever Haunt</b><br /> <br /> Once again, themed! This time it's music.</div> </div> </div> </div>Boulevard of Broken Dreams?<br /> and... I'm not sure I know that second one, but it sounds like something I might know...<br /> the one that goes &quot;Every move you make, every step you take I'll be watching you&quot;?<br /> <br /> Choice is an illusion, and so are pants. I choose both!<br /> <br /> <b>Shattered Dreams Route</b><br /> <br /> Fairfolk Cup<br /> <br /> The Raksha more than anyone know the lures of passions - afterall, mortals willingly come to see their magnificent performances and allow their souls to be devoured just to touch the spark of beauty and grace that is the the Raksha. Employing this powerful yearning, the Raksha may use the Dreams of a subject that is addicted to her as a [demesne or manse, can't remember the appropriate one] when attempting to create a permanent breakthrough. In Essence, the longing of the subject becomes so powerful that it pulls the Raksha (and a portion of the Wyld) into the subject's soul.<br /> <br /> Once there however, the Raksha must employ other magic to get out.<br /> <br /> -------------------------------<br /> <br /> <b>Promise to Forever Haunt</b><br /> <br /> Fairfolk Name, Assumption of Cerements and Bone tree.<br /> <br /> This charm allows a Raksha to exploit the rules of creation for its own survival. Activated in response to an attack that would destroy her, the Raksha weaves a narrative of death and persistence. Unless the Raksha already has Assumption of Cerements and Bone active, she may activate it and instantly dematerialize, taking no damage. <br /> <br /> However, any ancillary effects the charm would have (such as dismemberment or calcification) cannot be avoided, as the narrative of the attack dictates that it has hit; only damage is avoided. <br /> <br /> Lastly, the raksha must take on an appropriate Fetter for the remainder of the Story when activating this charm, most likely the attacker.<br /> <br /> <br /> Theming it is, but I can't give a hint because it'll narrow it down <i>too</i> much :<br /> <b>Rejection of Observation Scripture</b><br /> or<br /> <b>Rats and Tourists Attitude</b><br /> or<br /> <b>Clean Streets, Clean Governments</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T14:50:48-07:00","id":213969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=213811#post213811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Boulevard of Broken Dreams?<br /> and... I'm not sure I know that second one, but it sounds like something I might know...<br /> the one that goes &quot;Every move you make, every step you take I'll be watching you&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Right on the first, wrong on the second. It's &quot;Say You'll Haunt Me&quot; by Stone Sour.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/2480852/chapters/5503997\" target=\"_blank\">Glorious Echeladder Ascension Technique</a> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/287292-glorious-echeladder-ascension-technique-a-homestuck-exalted-crossover\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Topic</a><br /> <br /> &quot;Look, sometimes you just are in the mood to play the divinely empowered champion of the God of Farts. Mechanically optimized play is not the only way to enjoy playing your character.&quot; -Wise Old Guru","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1048-ryumaru","name":"Ryumaru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1048_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T16:58:16-07:00","id":214026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=213811#post213811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Promise to Forever Haunt</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh. Reflexive and conditional activation of an Assumption to avoid a negative consequence (while gaining a different negative consequence) is a very cool idea. ^__^ I could see similar notions finding their ways into the other Assumption Charms. Maybe one for slipping into Assumption of Dreams and Passion to mimic being a different person could negate an attempt to reveal a disguise and uncover the raksha's true identity (with some comparable penalty when trying to act counter to the false identity). Or another to activate Assumption of Bestial Form to basically pull off a Lunar's Labyrinth of the Beast, ignoring the impact of a social roll (with some comparable penalty to resisting instincts/tendencies the animal would have).<br /> <br /> Aaaaand I'm afraid I've got nothing on the theme here, either. :/ Oh well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Clean Streets, Clean Governments</b> </div> </div> </div><b>Infernal Bureaucracy</b> (Principle of Hierarchy)<br /> The Warlock understands that all things must know their proper place, and enlightens those without his perspective of the merits. Upon activating this Charm, the Infernal personally or legislatively begins a public work, service, or other campaign to improve well-being for a community by removing something perceived as negative from it, with bonuses toward carrying it out. This may be as large as removing crime from the streets or as minor as an anti-littering campaign. Any who assist or carry it out on his behalf receive a lesser bonus. Those who observe or participate in the work in progress or observe the fruits of these labors begin to develop a Principle that &quot;We must help to make society orderly.&quot; Those who know the Infernal is responsible also develop a Principle that &quot;&lt;The Warlock&gt; can create an orderly society.&quot;<br /> <br /> The grades of these Principles may be no greater than Minor if the campaign is not one of especially great perceived benefit to an individual (an anti-littering campaign where the streets are not seen as especially filthy), but may be elevated to Major or Defining if the perceived benefit is more significant (working to eliminate bureaucratic corruption, a den of thieves, or a distrusted ethnic minority). No such Intimacies form if one does not perceive them as beneficial. If the campaign is given particular difficulties such that one begins to lose confidence in it, the results of such a campaign are significantly undone, or one no longer sees it as beneficial, the associated Principles fade -- unless they are sustained by another campaign enhanced by a different use of this Charm.<br /> <br /> New Charm: (No theme, I'm afraid)<br /> <i>Ill Met by Moonlight</i><br /> or<br /> <i>Wedding and Funeral Crasis</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T19:38:48-07:00","id":214208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=214026#post214026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ooh. Reflexive and conditional activation of an Assumption to avoid a negative consequence (while gaining a different negative consequence) is a very cool idea. ^__^ I could see similar notions finding their ways into the other Assumption Charms. Maybe one for slipping into Assumption of Dreams and Passion to mimic being a different person could negate an attempt to reveal a disguise and uncover the raksha's true identity (with some comparable penalty when trying to act counter to the false identity). Or another to activate Assumption of Bestial Form to basically pull off a Lunar's Labyrinth of the Beast, ignoring the impact of a social roll (with some comparable penalty to resisting instincts/tendencies the animal would have).</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad you like it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Also, the Assumption of Bestial Form would totally be the Fairfolk version of this:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://i3.kym-cdn.com/photos/images/original/000/002/763/invalid.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=214026#post214026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aaaaand I'm afraid I've got nothing on the theme here, either. :/ Oh well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Banksy, a UK graffiti artist, the first one being <a href=\"http://d1eucpngoftcha.cloudfront.net/304/wp-content/uploads/2008/04/banksy-one-nation-under-cctv.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">One Nation Under CCTV</a>, the second being his various <a href=\"http://3.bp.blogspot.com/-HlWW5cHjcLw/TViSeHgFtFI/AAAAAAAAAAU/koBGiXO6rtA/s1600/2913665334_d139e5485d_o.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Rats</a>, and the third being <a href=\"http://www.artofthestate.co.uk/photos/banksy_maid_passer_by.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">the maid</a>.<br /> <br /> I really want to do something for <i>Ill Met by Moonlight</i>, but really have to go to bed. Hope it's not taken by the time I get back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-31T07:31:14-07:00","id":214645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=214026#post214026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Ill Met by Moonlight</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Celestial Circle Sorcery<br /> <br /> Standing upright with the moon to his back and a mirror to his front, the sorcerer observes the moon looming over the area he wishes to blight.<br /> <br /> This ritual begins when the moon is highest in the sky, and takes roughly an hour to perform, as the Sorcerer intones blessings to the moon and curses to the area.<br /> <br /> The Sorcerer may target specific individuals within that area as long as he can either see them in the reflection or has an Arcane Link to them in the form of tears, blood, or other bodily liquids; saying the name of each and naming the reasons for their suffering.<br /> <br /> Once the spell is cast (with a roll of Charisma + Occult + essence) the light of the moon is a blight upon the land until next Calibration :<br /> <br /> - Dreams depict the deaths of their dreamers through betrayal or suicide. Anyone sleeping in the area counts as having the Nightmares flaw unless they sleep in a pitch-black room into which no outside light can possibly penetrate.<br /> <br /> - Direct contact with moolight causes a persistent rash and similar damage and effects to [some hallucinogenic venom] and applies an additional dose every [hour?] of direct contact. Animals in the area usually go ferile after the first night, as they are just as prone to the nightmares and hallucinations.<br /> <br /> - The area is considered to be 1 level closer to Pure Chaos for the purposes of madness and mutation - this increases to 2 levels if the spell was cast with an exceptional success.<br /> <br /> - [seems appropriate but might be too much] The spell can only be Counterspelled during its initial ritual, afterwards its effects become a permanent part of Creation untill Calibration.<br /> <br /> Next: <b>Horn of Wood and Hooves of Cloud</b><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-31T12:07:06-07:00","id":214939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=214645#post214645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Horn of Wood and Hooves of Cloud</b></div> </div> </div> </div><b>Getimian Ride</b><br /> Mounting her steed, the Exalted rides far from the world. The horse moves as though unencumbered, ad may cross any surface without leaving a mark. In this way, they may ride across water, thin rice paper, and other surfaces that should not carry them.<br /> Activated using only peripheral Essence, the horse and rider become indistinguishable among the living things of the world, and move through trees, yeddim, and other living obstacles as though they were mist.<br /> Using only personal Essence, this Charm turns the Getimian and her steed into things like ghosts. Fire and mist and the like become firm as rock beneath the two of them.<br /> <br /> New Charm: <b>Scorpions-and-Wine Libation</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-31T21:40:28-07:00","id":215527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=214939#post214939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New Charm: <b>Scorpions-and-Wine Libation</b></div> </div> </div> </div><b>Infernal Resistance</b><br /> Lesser creatures must fear the work of poisoners and assassins, employing tasters (willingly or no) to verify the safety of their foodstuffs. Not so the chosen of Hell. The character gains a bonus equal to his permanent Essence to all rolls to resist imbibed drugs, toxins, or poisons. In addition, he may spend 8 points of Essence to render himself completely immune to a single poison for a scene. However, from now on he suffers something like an addiction, craving the strange, sweet taste of danger. He must consume a number of drugs or poisons with a combined toxicity equal to his Essence every day or suffer a -1 penalty to all mental rolls from the distracting cravings.<br /> <br /> Next: <b>Cast Upon the Walls of Truth</b><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-05T10:17:48-07:00","id":219245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HobbitGuy1420</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=215527#post215527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Next: <b>Cast Upon the Walls of Truth</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Solar Investigation.<br /> <br /> Blazing her Anima, the Solar illuminates an area equal to [her Essence x 10 yards] with a piercing light that pierces obstacles and leaves no shadows (in case of supernatural darkness, supernatural stealth or obstacles made of Magical Materials, this charm adds the Solar's Essence to the roll-off. Unattuned Magical Materials (such as walls of Jade) and Magical Materials the character is attuned to (such as the walls of a manse) offer no resistence.). Everywhere and everything this light hits is considered to be within the Solar's senses for the purposes of all other effects (such as Unsurpassed [Sense] Discipline) including touch and smell. This includes items stored under floor-boards, inside vaults, swallowed by other characters for safe-keeping and simply resting under 20 yards of cooled lava. While this does not pierce closed Portals, if one were to open even for a second, the Solar could get a very detailed idea of its insides.<br /> <br /> All the shadows that <i>would</i> be cast appear to the solar as arcane scriptures that reveal mood, nature, intent, purpose, history and other such characteristics. Traits (such as Attributes, Abilities and Charms) are not revealed by this charm, though things that would modify or stand out from the target's Pattern with physical manifestations ( such as Graces, Mutations, Prosthetics, Demon-Ink Tattoos and Tattoo Artifacts ) are made Obvious unless magically concealed (in which case roll-off).<br /> <br /> Activating this charm in tandem with the Night Caste Anima Power yields an invisble light that nevertheless allows the Solar to benefit from the charm's effects.<br /> <br /> (basically it's a giant solar X-Ray machine... Might be better off as a Sorcery now that I think about it...)<br /> <br /> Next: <b>Pyrotechnic Artistry Method</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-06T11:57:02-07:00","id":220376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=219245#post219245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Pyrotechnic Artistry Method</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Terrestrial Presence:<br /> <br /> The Dragon-Blood's anima swirls into multi-hued light as she states her points and makes her claim. Her anima billows about her and lances out with terrifying glory. Those present treat this scene as building an intimacy of fear, wonder, awe, or another appropriate emotion. This power is not easily contained, though; every (Integrity) actions while she maintains this charm, she must make a ranged attack, using her successes on a Charisma + Presence Roll to target. While she may pull her blows, dealing only bashing damage, failure to designate a target causes instead the streamer of fiery essence to strike a part of the scenery with its full incendiary force.<br /> <br /> Next:<br /> <br /> <b>Between Here and Heaven</b><br /> <br /> or<br /> <br /> <b>Scattered Sunbeam Strike</b><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-07T08:28:42-07:00","id":221036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=220376#post220376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Between Here and Heaven</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Celestial Circle sorcery<br /> <br /> This spell creates a floating sanctum (though not a Sanctum) high in the sky, shrouded in clouds and appearing as whatever structure the Sorcerer wishes (from a perfectly flat platform to a floating castle with any amenities the sorcerer wishes to design for it during the preparation of this spell). The sactum's size and structure depend on how much time the Sorcerer is willing to spend preparing, designing and casting this spell. Without any preparation or design, this spell produces a large irregular slab of earth, similar to a forest clearing, that might contain a cave for shelter, a small pond with drinking water and enough wood for a campfire.<br /> <br /> Additionally, once complete, the Sorcerer can spend [x] motes when within [some distance] to summon a bolt of lightning that would transport himself and anyone touching him (along with their belongings) to the sanctum's entrance.<br /> <br /> The sanctum's position is fixed by default - it can't be used as a transport to fly from one point in creation to an other. However, it can ascend and descend to a limited degree - it cannot land or go beyond the dome of Creation. The Sorcerer may design some form of propultion for it however (giant sails, wind-mills or wind-oars) or incorporate magical means of transportation during the design process.<br /> <br /> Lastly, while Magical Materials can be brought to it to reinforce its structure, this spell cannot create Magical Materials, so by default sanctums are made of natural materials such as stone, iron, glass and earth. However, if the Sorcerer has Magical Materials on hand, they can be incorporated into the design, and will position themselves in their assigned places upon the completion of this spell.<br /> <br /> Next: <b> Edge of the sword, edge of the world [meditation/technique/kata etc.] </b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-07T11:45:36-07:00","id":221152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=221036#post221036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b> Edge of the sword, Edge of the world Kata </b></div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereal Melee<br /> <br /> At the edge of Creation, the laws start to break down. Concepts like up, down, front, back, life and death fail to accurately describe the conditions of the Wyld. While it is considered cruel, a Sidereal can apply these conditions to his adversaries.<br /> By attacking their opponent's fate through a complex series of strikes, the inside of their opponent's body is treated as being part of the wyld. This attack counts as a regular attack for the purpose of dodging and blocking, though it can't be soaked through natural defenses, armor can still soak it. During this time, anything underneath his skin starts acting unnaturally, moving, twisting, growing, shrinking, changing consistency and changing color are all things that regularly happen. This effect inflicts [Essence] points of unsoakable, undodgeable lethal damage every turn, though it can never kill them, or get them unconscious. In addition, the pain of this technique gives the Sidereal a bonus when gathering information from the victim. The aftereffects of this Charm can be undone by medicine charms, though it is beyond mortal surgery.<br /> <br /> Yes, the Sidereals have an interrogation technique in their Melee tree.<br /> <br /> <b>Divided we Stand</b><br /> <br /> Or...<br /> <br /> <b>United we Fall</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-07T13:25:40-07:00","id":221244,"title":"","content":"<b>Divided we Stand</b><br /> Solar War<br /> <br /> Against the armies of the Unconquered Sun, none shall stand. This Charm adds Essence dice to all rolls made by any force of the Solar's choice. In addition, all rolls receive a bonus equal to the War + Intelligence of the commanding officer for the force. These die may not be rerolled by any means (other than caulking the die*). This applies for only one particular battle, and cannot be used again until the next sunrise.<br /> <br /> *Just in case this isn't used outside my circle of friends: it's when a die roll is unclear due to the way it lands, and you reroll it to get a better landing.<br /> <br /> <b>There is Only War</b><br /> <br /> or<br /> <br /> <b>You can fight Fate</b><br /> <br /> or<br /> <br /> <b>None shall stand</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-07T14:29:10-07:00","id":221268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HalfTangible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=221244#post221244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>None Shall Stand</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereal Bureaucracy, after End Debate.<br /> <br /> With a sharp word or a strict glance, the Sidereal grabs the fates of everyone in the scene and yanks them downward. She takes control of a heated argument, causing everyone to sit down, be quiet, and listen to what the obviously wiser Exalt has to say. The more heated the arguments had been (based on how many Intimacies had been invoked or whatever), the more strongly the Sidereal takes control, and the more susceptible everyone else is to her next words.<br /> <br /> Next Charm:<b> Lighting the Labyrinthine Path</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T13:19:10-07:00","id":222413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Limited Reagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=221268#post221268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Next Charm:<b> Lighting the Labyrinthine Path</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Terrestrial ... awareness I think.<br /> <br /> The terrestrial touches a surface and saturates it with an element, sending forth one of his senses along that surface in a line that glows with elemental color. This line moves forward along the surface at roughly double the exalt's normal movement speed. (and potentially costs motes per unit of distance )<br /> <br /> If the character knows more than one version of this charm, [cost] can be paid to activate those effects, endowing the trail with the combined properties of each activated element.<br /> <br /> <b>Fire</b>: Sight. The Exalt can see (but not hear or smell) out of any point along the blazing crimson trail. Additionally, the trail can create a blaze of light to illuminate out to [the range of an anima banner].<br /> <br /> <b>Water</b>: Taste. The Exalt can pick up tastes (such as spilled blood, food, sweat, salt, poison). Additionally, the trail can move through water in any direction (it can float, and isn't bound to a surface as long as it remains in water). This includes Ice, though not vapour.<br /> <br /> <b>Earth</b>: Touch. The exalt can feel the trail and everything with [essence x 10 yards] of it as though it was his own skin. Additionally, the trail can move through solid earth-aspected surfaces such as stone, gravel and earth, but not wood or ice.<br /> <br /> <b>Air</b>: Sound. The Exalt can hear everything along the trail as through he was present there himself. Additionally the trail can move through air in any direction like a flying ribbon, no longer bound to a surface.<br /> <br /> <b>Wood</b>: Smell. the exalt can pick up and follow smells, pinpointing their location and direction.<br /> (his sence of smell isn't more powerful however, simply more accurate).<br /> <br /> <br /> The expenditure of [cost, maybe no cost] upon activation or any time during the charm's duration allows the exalt to extend his anima power and effect to the trail (e.g. for a fire aspect, both the glowing and the 4L burning of anyone that touches it)<br /> <br /> <br /> Next: <b>Alliterative Allies-and-Admonishers Charm</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T18:41:14-07:00","id":222664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=222413#post222413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Next: <b>Alliterative Allies-and-Admonishers Charm</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Elloge Charm. Based on someone's current social &quot;role&quot; in relation to you, you then assign them a new role that starts with the same letter, with mind-warping Emotion backing up that change. Turn foes to friends, paramours to pets, assassins to assistants, minions to mothers, or betrayers to betrothed!<br /> <br /> Next: <b>One With Nothing Satori</b> or <b>Your Mother's Sword</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T20:09:15-07:00","id":222729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=222664#post222664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Next: <b>One With Nothing Satori</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Abyssal Integrity. Wards off Illusion, Compulsion and Emotion effects, but will activate whether or not the Abyssal wants it to. Her heart is permanently emptied.<br /> <br /> Next: Born to Kill Approach OR Tattoo-Inscribing Diatribe","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T21:46:46-07:00","id":222786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ellis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=222729#post222729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tattoo-Inscribing Diatribe</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Infernal Presence</b> (Malfeas)<br /> Those whom the Warlock decries shall wear the marks of his displeasure for all to behold. When the Infernal denounces or otherwise harshly criticizes an individual, he may activate this Charm. The subject of this abuse feels a brief burning sensation as a relevant mark sears itself prominently into his flesh. Each time anyone beholds it in a given scene, the viewer is affected as though she had heard the Warlock's original rebuke exactly as it was delivered. This mark may be concealed as easily as any tattoo, though this may become difficult if the Infernal uses this Charm for multiple criticisms, or employs other magic.<br /> <br /> New Charm:<br /> <i>Pauper in Palace Castigation</i><br /> or<br /> <i>Wishes Are Horses Understanding</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Slight Cleanup 08-09-2014, 12:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T10:14:45-07:00","id":225139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=222786#post222786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <b>Pauper in Palace Castigation</b></div> </div> </div> </div><b>Solar Presence</b><br /> <br /> A Solar taps deeply into his own conscious, reminding herself of her own greatness, and, with a few words, can show others how pitiful they are, and how worthless and temporal the materials are that they use to hide this.<br /> The Solar speaks down upon whoever he is speaking with, creating a minor intimacy within the person they are speaking to of self-doubt, annoyance or frustration with any type material goods this person has in his possession. This type is specified by the Solar who uses this charm. If the person has a positive intimacy with these goods, this gets eroded instead.<br /> <br /> <b><i>King between Rats Camouflage</i></b><br /> or<br /> <i><b>Meat is Meat realization</b></i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","user":"While My Guitar","date":". 08-11-2014, 01:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T11:26:55-07:00","id":225179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=225139#post225139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><i>King between Rats Camouflage</i></b></div> </div> </div> </div>Lunar Charisma<br /> <br /> The Lunar spendsa majority of the scene among several people (in a bar, in a theater, in a crowd) and subtely infuses them with mercurial essence that resonates with the Lunar's personality. This adds an internal environmental penalty equal to the group's magnitude to anyone trying to pick the Lunar out of the crowd.<br /> <br /> If discovered (either as an impostor, as a thief, through a failed Stealth roll, etc.), this charm allows the Lunar to treat the crowd as having a Major or Defining intimacy of loyalty towards him. They will do whatever they can to help the Lunar make an escape or a stand. For example they could help by distracting his accusors, blocking their paths, throwing tomatoes at them or helping the Lunar hide; though this charm cannot force anyone to knowingly put themselves in mortal danger.<br /> <br /> Though the crowd doesn't actually develop a hive-mind, they are more prone to act in unison, such as everyone turning simultaneously to stare down the accusor, or arranging their clothes in a manner similar to the Lunar to create red-herrings.<br /> <br /> Commitment to this charm lapses as soon as the crowd disperses or the scene in which the Lunar was discovered ends (whichever comes first), but is otherwise indefinite.<br /> <br /> Next: <b>Warming the Frozen Hearth</b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">if you know what I mean.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T16:26:45-07:00","id":225388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=225179#post225179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <b>Warming the Frozen Hearth</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Dragon-Blooded Socialize<br /> <br /> The soul-heat of Hesiesh alone is enough to spark the passions of many like a wildfire. This charm supplements a sexual intercourse with a character having a major positive intimacy towards your character. The flames of your passions ablaze all participants's sexual pleasure, and the scene counts as two scenes reinforcing the intimacy. It ensures that a child will be born from such intercourse and keeps the bloodline intact (no breeding loss if cross-breeding with a mortal). As a side effect, the character affected by this charm will start propagating rumors about the Dragon-Blooded bed-prowess, slowly developing a minor intimacy of lust in a group of [Essence Magnitude] characters in his vicinity.<br /> <br /> At Essence 4 or higher, this Charm now goes beyond mortals and affect all local spirits of lower essence than the Dragon-Blooded, allowing him to give birth in a much quicker way. <br /> <br /> <br /> Next up: <b>Wheat-as-Gold Craftmanship</b> OR <b>Time-Narrative Meditation</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T12:04:31-07:00","id":236772,"title":"","content":"<b>Wheat-as-Gold Craftsmanship</b><br /> <br /> Solar Craft<br /> <br /> The true craftsman knows that 'spinning wheat into gold' is just a metaphor - every masterpiece of art or craft is in truth a labour of many hands, who provide the materials and tools for the craftsman to create it, in a chain that might have dozens of links. No master's work or no man's wealth can ever come to pass without this, sometimes vast, network. One can only create true beauty and peerless function, and obtain true wealth, by recognizing it.<br /> <br /> The Charm allows the Solar to meditate upon the task before him and picture the most efficient ways of obtaining materials, resources, tools and labour required for it. He gains a supernatural insight into obtaining the best possible components of the project and all the efforts to obtain them. She cannot be fooled by shoddy materials or unskilled labour being passed as high-quality, and will be granted an intuition as to obstacles that may appear. However, this Charm does not prevent random, unforeseen events from interfering.<br /> <br /> Next up: <b>Pronouncement of Two Skies</b> or <b>The Riddle of Steel</b>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T05:45:32-07:00","id":240171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=236772#post236772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The Riddle of Steel</b></div> </div> </div> </div>This artifact buckler has a scripture engraved on it in an unknown language. <br /> The scripture is a riddle addressed to the Titans and to Creation itself. When activated (as a simple action, or reflexively during a Defend or Defend Other action), its writing glows and creates an area of effect within which objects harden and slowly, over the course of [some time], gain the properties of iron or steel (weilder's choice).<br /> Generally this increases those items' hardness and soak. In the case of iron, the bonuses are smaller, but it has the useful property of keeping the fairie folk at bay.<br /> <br /> With [extra cost] the weilder can also target individuals, increasing their soak (if he does so, his own soak increases in the same way for no cost).<br /> <br /> The effect's AoE, speed and Soak/Hardness bonus scale with the weilder's essece, and works on items already made of steel or iron when its bonus would surpass their normal stats.<br /> <br /> Next: <b>Endless Butterfly Parade</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T14:22:20-07:00","id":244319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=240171#post240171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Next: <b>Endless Butterfly Parade</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Resplendent Destiny of the Haywain<br /> <i>Once, there was a maiden...<br /> whose father took her to the city.</i><br /> (i know there are only sutras for actual charms i just couldn't resist)<br /> The Sidereal attempts to anchor someone and prevent them from traveling. Each time they try to travel (as defined by Journeys astrology and/or Charms), they suffer botches and other unfortunate accidents that stymie them. Each botch costs the Sidereal some Endurance, though she cannot control it.<br /> Next: The Greatest Lie OR Knight-And-Dragon Exchange","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T01:57:07-07:00","id":244683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ellis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=244319#post244319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Greatest Lie</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Infernal Socialize, Ebon Dragon</b><br /> <br /> The Ebon Dragon speaks in nothing but lies, except when revealing horrible truths. A Warlock can use this same power to tear down what a person's faith.<br /> <br /> To use this charm, the Warlock needs to be familiar with the intimacy it wants to target. By carefully choosing his words, the Infernal twists one of their target's intimacies, making them realize that, what they thought it stood for was a lie.<br /> This Charm destroys any positive intimacy a person had and replaces it with a negative intimacy of the same level. This effect lasts until this negative intimacy is destroyed, at which point it becomes a positive intimacy again at the same level it once was.<br /> The Greatest Lie can be used to deceive person multiple times, but each intimacy can only be targeted once.<br /> <br /> Shaking a person's worldview by making them realize that their beliefs are wrong seems very ED-like<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'd like to see some more Lunar Charms, so....<br /> <br /> Wearing the Lion's Mane<br /> Or<br /> Hunting Nightstalker Presence","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T13:20:43-07:00","id":244956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=244683#post244683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, I'd like to see some more L*kshhhcrackle* Charms, so....</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, what's that? Couldn't quite make it out. Oh well, I'm sure this can't be too far off the mark:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wearing the Lion's Mane </div> </div> </div><b>Liminal Charisma</b><br /> With this permanent Charm, one of the Chernozem may derive further benefit from pieces of any animals she has added to herself. She may enhance her social actions, if she treats any cultural or personal attitudes others hold toward any such animals as though they applied to her. If others can observe these animal parts, they may likewise benefit from this enhancement when applying such attitudes toward her. If an animal part is meaningfully incorporated as part of the Liminal's stunt, this enhancement improves.<br /> <br /> ... Kidding. <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hunting Nightstalker Presence </div> </div> </div><b>Lunar Awareness</b><br /> The Lunar opens his eyes and ears to the nightmares that prowl like hungry predatory beasts, and may interact with them as such. They are simple entities, viewing dreams and a good night's rest as their prey. The Lunar may attempt to engage in social actions with them or attack them as though they were physical. If he destroys or dissuades them from affecting himself or anyone else, such sleepers receive a bonus toward a good night's rest (for the purposes of Willpower and mote recovery, etc.). On the contrary, some Lunars find it a great advantage to drive the hunters toward less favored sleepers, giving their enemies penalties to the same.<br /> <br /> Under most cases, nightmares are relatively few and trivial opponents, simple to drive off for easier prey. However, circumstance plays a heavy role. Such creatures are more numerous and fiercer in dangerous places, and sleepers experiencing fear, depression, or other mental anguish prove more alluring to them. They likewise become more dangerous if the Lunar himself is currently frightened. This Charm also allows the Lunar to perceive and interact with dream-influencing magic effects as though they were physical. This may include interrupting another dreamer's dealings with Makarios (and even harming the demon) or fending off some strange raksha oneirochorous disease.<br /> <br /> New Charm:<br /> Roses in a Sea of Thorns<br /> OR<br /> Martyr of Small Cause","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":"08-30-2014, 04:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T21:55:41-07:00","id":245186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=244956#post244956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Roses in a Sea of Thorns</div> </div> </div> </div>Dragon-Blooded Awareness. Honing his sense of smell a thousandfold, the Dragon-Blood is able to read people through their pheromones, allowing him to find those he can truly trust among the endless ranks of those who would use or abuse him.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Martyr of Small Cause </div> </div> </div>Sidereal Performance. Binds you to a small god (Essence 1) as its prophet and first believer, giving you persuasive power that declines as your god's cult grows, and letting the god develop rapidly into a regional spiritual force. <br /> <br /> Next: <b>World's Shell Hatchery</b> or <b>Teaching Manners to the Bear</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T07:26:00-07:00","id":246130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=245186#post245186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Teaching Manners to the Bear</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Throne Shadow Style<br /> <br /> The Seer demand polite behavior from beast and savage alike. Allowing the Sidereal to make animal into shadow finger, granting them human-level sapience in the process.<br /> <br /> <b>Desert Princess</b> <b>Tantrum Toss</b><br /> <br /> or<br /> <br /> <b>Soul-Wrecking Higanbana Field</b><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T21:16:25-07:00","id":246612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=246130#post246130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Soul-Wrecking Higanbana Field</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Abyssal Socialize<br /> <br /> It is said flowers that bloom near grave sites guide the dearly departed to their next incarnations. The deathknight's blossoms have somewhat different aims. Near a corpse or in a graveyard, the seeds of a flower associated with death begin to sprout shortly after the Abyssal sows them. All souls nearby that have not yet passed on have a significantly increased chance of lingering as ghosts. This chance increases if the Abyssal takes plains to plant them carefully and tend to them for at least a day. Onlookers who hold personal or cultural associations of death for the flower may find themselves moved by its beauty. Such onlookers lose some aversion and unease typically felt toward the dead and deathly things, and have an increased likelihood of leaving a ghost upon death. These effects fade after a number of days equal to the Abyssal's Essence, or linger as long as the individual possesses a positive Intimacy for the blossoms.<br /> <br /> New Charm: (canine theme!)<br /> <i>Silver Sand Coyote Tricks</i><br /> or<br /> <i>Fox's Artful Logomancy</i><br /> or<br /> <i>Wolf Den Hospitality</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T00:00:51-07:00","id":246681,"title":"","content":"Wolf Den Hospitality<br /> <br /> Lunar Socialize<br /> <br /> While it lacks the comforts of the city, there is a cozy warmth to the den of a mother wolf. For any matter in which the Lunar does not need to engage in social combat, she is looked on favorably by those she interacts with within her territory. During social combat with any guest within her lands, the Lunar may choose to add her essence to any roll that does not already incorporate it. She may also pay 1wp in order to create an intimacy of her choice in those she speaks with for one scene. This intimacy must be related to the territory the target is currently within. If the Lunar's territory is a forest, for example, the intimacy must be related to the forest. Its wildlife, a river within it, even the Lunar herself, but it must relate to the territory.<br /> <br /> <i>Chains of Silken Terror</i><br /> or<br /> <i>Stained by Hero's Blood</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-27T23:11:52-07:00","id":267227,"title":"","content":"Well, this thread's sat idle for rather a long time. I wonder why... Oh well.<br /> *primes the defibrillator*<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HalfTangible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=246681#post246681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Chains of Silken Terror</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Raksha Cup<br /> <br /> The Prince of Chaos breathes a profound luxuriance into a possession as it is gifted to another, causing it to appear slightly more valuable than it actually is. If the recipient fails an opposed roll, the recipient develops a Minor Principle to enjoy this gift to its fullest as well as a Major Tie to abject terror at the thought of losing it. If another individual claims the gifted possession, failing the same opposed roll will bestow the same Intimacies to this new owner. More than a few raksha have created these footholds to turn mortals into easily directed paranoid wrecks. At least one land is subject to endless wars after one of the Fair Folk claimed it centuries ago and then freely gave it to a mortal family. The only sure end to this curse is if one of its owners willingly gives it to another.<br /> <br /> New Charm:<br /> <i>Silver Sand Coyote Tricks</i><br /> or<br /> <i>Logomancy of the Artful Fox</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-01T09:06:44-07:00","id":270159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Silver Sand Coyote Tricks</i> </div> </div> </div>Physical hazard are not the only danger lurking in Hell's endless waster. An Infernal using this charm release Cecelynian essence into a place of desolation, space and time bend in strange way to traveler. Character that attempt to navigate out of the affect area suffers as though they are trying to track a character using the Solar charm Trackless Passage as mirage and illusion plague the Infernal's victim.<br /> <br /> If using this charm on a Holy Land made by the Infernal, then she can give it the Sorcerous tag. Adamant Countermagic make a character immune until she leave an area under the effect of Silver Sand Coyote Tricks.<br /> <br /> <i>Rotting Yomi Paradise</i> / <i>Genocide Guillotine Gale</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-01T09:21:38-07:00","id":270163,"title":"","content":"Genocide guillotine Gale<br /> <br /> This charm directly upgrades glorious carnage typhoon. For a surcharge the Abyssal doubles the effective magnitude of troops he slays (triple if in close formation) sending the minced corpses of his victims flying all over battlefield. The difficulty to route is increased by essence as long as with an intimacy of fear to those who do route.<br /> <br /> New charm:<br /> Snatching defeat from victory method/ask not from which the thunder comes","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T16:29:48-07:00","id":290844,"title":"","content":"*blows off surprising layer of dust*<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=270163#post270163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ask Not From Which The Thunder Comes</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Evocation</b> (Harmonious Storm - paired short daiklaves, each is one part Starmetal alloyed with two parts Blue Jade)<br /> <br /> Previous Evocations:<br /> - clashing the blades brings a mist and resonant song to the area, obscuring others' views and subtly cuing the wielder on when to best move and act.<br /> - rolls of mist periodically form into convincing replicas of the wielder, more the longer and better the wielder dances; they confuse opponents and aid in stealthy movements through the mist, but any attack that overcomes the wielder's DDV automatically dissolves them.<br /> - lightning crackles along the blade edges (including misty doppelgangers'), to be released in separate bolts or twined together into a great one.<br /> <br /> When unleashing a great bolt of lightning on tempo, all misty replicas become indistinguishable from the wielder and loose their attacks at the same time, with the same crack of thunder. The doppelgangers' bolts of lightning are less harmful, but may aim for separate targets, or make it very difficult for a single target to evade them all. Any participating doppelganger diffuses afterward, regardless of its attack's success.<br /> <br /> <b>New Charm: </b><br /> <i>Awe-Inspiring World Cauldron</i><br /> OR<br /> <i>Puppets Without Strings Revelation</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Elaboration. 10-23-2014, 07:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T13:43:43-07:00","id":291544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=290844#post290844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*blows off surprising layer of dust*<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Puppets Without Strings Revelation</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereal Presence<br /> Having carefully mentored her students, the sifu knows they are ready to be weaned of her tutelage. She abandons all connection to someone, rendering them Outside Fate so far as she is concerned; she cannot lay astrology on them, fool them with her Fate-derived illusions, etc. In return, she ensures that she has truly made them in her image, with one last parting gict: the Sidereal's subject gains a secondary magical Motivation which matches the Sidereal's own. This cannot change, even if the Sidereal changes her own; only something capable of breaking the Sidereal's magic can remove it (which excludes the Sidereal, who obviously cannot affect her student any longer).<br /> <br /> Next up: Tearing the Veil OR Shape of the Soul","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T14:20:04-07:00","id":291568,"title":"","content":"<b>Shape of the Soul</b><br /> <br /> Requires: Wyld Cauldron Technology, Essence 5<br /> <br /> Solars do not simply bring order to chaos - they give it purpose. This charm allows Wyld Shaping Technique successes to used to create customized heroic mortals, at the cost of 4 successess per heroic mortal. The mortal's statline is that of a default heroic mortal, but the solar has complete control of how those stats are distributed. For one additional success the solar can conjure a copy of the original mortal. All mortals created this way appear with the motivation &quot;Obey my maker&quot; In the first age a lot of Solars used this to create legions of quite dimwitted but exceedingly beautiful courtesans, or strong and fiercly loyal bodyguards when not even dragon blooded could be trusted... or test subjects for anything from combat charms to new necromantic spells.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T19:55:25-07:00","id":291758,"title":"","content":"webkilla passed on giving a new name, so:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ellis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=291544#post291544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tearing the Veil</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Fair Folk Heart</b><br /> <br /> The raksha may sheathe themselves in beautiful forms of perfection to travel Creation, but the truth -- hungry maws and unformed will -- always lurks beneath. And nearer the surface than most might guess. Though it happens seldom, the Princes of Chaos sometimes allow their true madness to break through a crack in their sublime masks. Though they expose themselves to Creation's deadly pressure, some (short-lived) fey deem the brief power it grants them the only appropriate response to marring such a perfect face.<br /> <br /> Upon receiving at least 1L in damage (this may be self-inflicted as a reflexive action), a Fair Folk with an active but non-Permanent Assumption Charm may reflexively dismiss it, and becomes unable to apply a new one any earlier than the next scene. She immediately receives however many motes she had committed to it. For the rest of the scene, the local area is treated as the Wyld for all purposes, with a strength dependent on the raksha's Heart Grace (2 for Bordermarches, 3 for Middlemarches, 4 for Deep Wyld, and 5+ for Pure Chaos; if used in the Wyld, this Charm cannot reduce the local strength). The new Waypoint acquires some superficial properties reflective of the Assumption Charm (iconography relevant to the particular animal, element, or emotion; small apparent changes to environment, local creatures, etc.), which cannot be altered for the duration. A raksha may also choose to include a number of Fantasies somehow resonant with that Assumption, equal to (Heart - 2), rolled as normal using the raksha's traits.<br /> <br /> At the end of the scene, the area returns to normal, though a few subtle changes may linger, particularly if exposed to more potent raksha. Now without an active Assumption, the raksha begins suffering all associated damage if in Creation, and will no doubt take whatever means necessary to avoid calcifying.<br /> <br /> <b>New Charm:</b><br /> <i>A New Face in Rippled Water</i><br /> OR<br /> <i>Awe-Inspiring World Cauldron</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T04:06:18-07:00","id":291948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>A New Face in Rippled Water</i> </div> </div> </div><b>Getimian Larceny</b><br /> By shattering her opponent's reflection, the Unbound shatters their identity.<br /> The <i>Peripheral</i> version of this Charm allows the Getimian to make a reflexive disguise attempt on behalf of her target, cursing them with the face of one lost to the world. The <i>Personal</i> variant, meanwhile, simply deprives the victim of self and memory, temporarily removing all but their Defining intimacies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Awe-Inspiring World Cauldron</i> </div> </div> </div><b>Infernal Craft</b><br /> The warlock stomps his foot, and the earth shatters, and the air, and the boundary between them. Chaos seeps from the cracks.<br /> This Charm creates a space of almost-Wyld around the user. Within, the Green Sun Prince is considered to have the tools for any Craft roll she performs, allowing him to chisel rocks into statues with his gaze or smelt metal in his cupped hands. Furthermore, he may perform reflexive, Craft-based Intimidate actions against anyone who tries to attack him or enter his cauldron, even if he isnt aware of them.<br /> <br /> <i>Next up, </i><b>Blind Star Demon Fist</b><i> (or </i><b>Blade</b><i>, </i><b>Bolt</b><i>, et cetera) or </i><b>Horse Conquers Leopard Mantra</b><i>.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T10:17:45-07:00","id":292170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Horse Conquers Leopard Mantra</b> </div> </div> </div><b>Sidereal Socialize</b><br /> <br /> By reciting the Scripture of the Whore, one can easily subvert the relationship between two individuals with a flick of finger. One of the target must has an Intimacy created by Cash and Murder Games, activating this charm will transfer the Intimacy from the victim to the beneficiary as an unblockable, undodgeable Shaping attack that travel across all distance save for when the beneficiary is in another realm of existence like the Underworld or Malfeas.<br /> <br /> <b>Fata Morgana's Mirage</b> or <b>Optical Light Flection Defense</b><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T10:49:27-07:00","id":292222,"title":"","content":"<b>Optical Light Flection Defense</b><br /> Cost: variable; Mins: Strength 4, Essence 3;<br /> Type: Reflexive (Step 2)<br /> Keywords: Combo-OK, Obvious, Counterattack<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Requirements: Light-Etched Interceptor Barrior<br /> <br /> The champions of the Great Maker reject the offense of their foes. This charm's appearance depends on its prereisite's appearance. If the LEIB is based on external armor, then the OLFD is a white jade and orichalcum circular assembly fitted on the gauntlet, for internal LEIBs the OLFD appears as additional circular patterns seared into the champion's arm.<br /> <br /> The charm functions by briefly empowering the LEIB on successful parries, pulsing the barrier to thrust the attack back upon the attacker. This costs a number of motes equal to the essence rating of the attacker. This functions as a counterattack, as if the attacker attacked herself, with an identical attack as used on the champion. For close combat attack these cannot be defended with the same weapon being thrust back on the attacker, while ranged attacked reflected back on attackers do not carry this added penalty. This charm cannot be used if the LEIB perfectly parries an attack, as that solidifies the barrier and locks the emiitter nodes, preventing a counter-pulse.<br /> <br /> Submodules:<br /> <br /> Enhanced Emitter Stabilizers<br /> By strengthening the OLFD's connections and essence circuitry with jade coatings and more refined copper wires, the OLFD can now also function when the LEIB is used to perfectly parry an attack.<br /> <br /> <br /> Next charm on the list: <b>Resplendent Buttflow Technique</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":588,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","user":"webkilla","date":". 10-25-2014, 01:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-29T10:07:47-07:00","id":295972,"title":"","content":"<b>Resplendent Buttflow Technique<br /> <br /> Terrestrial MA/Brawl Charm, Water</b><br /> <br /> As water from the back of a river pushes that in front of it to the sea, this charm allows the dragon-blooded to knock lesser enemies aside with ease.<br /> <br /> Upgrade charm: <b>River Meets Sea Impact</b>; For a surcharge the dragon-blooded causes the victim to land with such force that a small spring or lake forms in the resulting crater.<br /> <br /> Next charm, <b>One Stone, Many Birds</b> or <b>Self Found, Others Lost</b>, you decide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Currently Playing:</b> <i>A large, mixed splat game of <b>CofD</b>.</i> <b>As:</b> Seraph du Salomon, Voice on the concordance. Unsubtle man reluctantly participating in the business of Magi. Awakening 2E homebrew <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1338514-house-du-salomon-a-proximus-dynasty?_=1569864567692\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...=1569864567692</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","name":"Gryphon's Feather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2598_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"215"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-29T10:35:12-07:00","id":295997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>One Stone, Many Birds</b> </div> </div> </div><b>Solar Thrown</b><br /> <br /> The Night Wolf concentrate for just a moment before making a perfect shot that can slay even the horde selves of Adorjan. The Solar active this charm and in his next action make an attack roll and compare the successes to every enemy in the base range of his thrown weapon as boulder ricochet between demon and knife bouncing from ghost to ghost.<br /> <br /> <b>Remembering </b><b>Embryo's Dream</b> / <b>Eight Millions Kami Dance</b> / <b>Philosophy of a Hated Person</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T10:14:38-08:00","id":300142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=295997#post295997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Philosophy of a Hated Person</b></div> </div> </div> </div><b>Lunar Manipulation</b><br /> <br /> Luna's Chosen often lead others to more favorable impressions of themselves, but there can be value in inspiring disdain or hatred. Particularly if these negative feelings become tied to ideals and principles the Lunar cannot abide. This Charm supplements a Lunar's attempt to build or strengthen in others a negative Intimacy toward himself (or whomever he appears to be), subtly turning his every look, word, and gesture in an unpalatable direction. If the Lunar is espousing a philosophy or idea and convinces others he holds it, then his targets will find great ease in painting that thought with the same brush as the Lunar, as this Charm supplements an attempt to build or strengthen a negative Intimacy toward it. If the Lunar is wearing the shape of someone who actually holds (or held) a positive Intimacy toward the idea, this borrowed sincerity only magnifies the inspired contempt, reducing the difficulty and strengthening the effect even further.<br /> <br /> New Charm:<br /> Jade Rabbit Descends<br /> OR<br /> Verdant Kirin Blessing<br /> OR<br /> Elated Romp of the Pooka","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T18:30:46-08:00","id":346281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=300142#post300142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Verdant Kirin Blessing</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Celestial Circle Sorcery<br /> <br /> Through a lengthy ritual the sorcerer rolls Intelligence + Occult as an extended action. This imbues a steed with the elemental Essence of wood - life, health and plentiness.<br /> For a number of days equal to the ritualist's Essence, the mount and its surroundings (1 yard per accumulated success) grow ever-fresh fruit, herbs and spices appropriate to the region at an accelerated rate - enough to keep [successes] people sated and quenched for the duration; though this food must still be foraged - the rider is exempt from this, as most necessities grow directly on his steed.<br /> The mount itself becomes tireless for the duration of the enchantment, and can move through difficult terrain without hindrance and without disturbing the flora.<br /> <br /> Next:<br /> <b>Thousand-Spires Conflagration</b><br /> or<br /> <b>Mask of iron whispers</b><br /> or<br /> <b>Duplicitous Beloved Filigree</b><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T12:32:26-08:00","id":346887,"title":"","content":"I like this game, so I'll do more.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=300142#post300142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Jade Rabbit Descends</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Terrestrial Athletics, Reflexive<br /> <br /> After gaining aerial advantage in some manner (through flight or terrain advantage for example), the Terrestrial leaps down and activates this charm at the beginning of their descent. This charm converts up to the Terrestrial's Athletics + Relevant Specialty score of raw falling damage into a die bonus to the damage of any attacks made this tick, as the Exalt plummets like a comet from the sky, surrounded by elemental energy. This effect is calculated before any effect reduces falling damage to 0.<br /> <br /> This charm has an additional effect based on its aspect:<br /> <br /> <b>Fire:</b> The terrestrial leaves a burning trail in his wake, bright enough to temporarily blind opponents and set surroungs on fire.<br /> <b>Water: </b>Heavy rain falls like lead beads in the Exalt's wake, making it hard to breathe, see or stand for a few turns.<br /> <b>Air:</b> Snowflakes and sharp shards of ice are formed in the Exalt's wake. The shards fall like knives, dealing [some] damage.<br /> <b>Earth: </b>Upon landing, the Exalt causes an earthquake that shakes the ground and raises sharp stalagmites.<br /> <b>Wood:</b> Thorns and flower petals follow and encircle the exalt, imparing visibility and inducing a slow and sluggish sleepiness in enemies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=346281#post346281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Next:<br /> <b>Thousand-Spires Conflagration</b><br /> or<br /> <b>Mask of iron whispers</b><br /> or<br /> <b>Duplicitous Beloved Filigree</b></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":".  clearer formulation. 12-21-2014, 03:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T13:06:22-08:00","id":346902,"title":"","content":"<b>Mask of Iron Whispers:</b><br /> Abyssal Presence<br /> <br /> The Abyssal's face twists, hardening into a slate grey, emotionless mask, with a voice as cold and distant as Death itself. As long as this Charm is active, the Abyssal's face does not move, he doesn't blink, move his lips or twitch his eyes. As long as the mask is worn, it gives the following effects.<br /> <br /> -His cold, distant voice gives people a penalty in gaining information on his Intimacies directly from him.<br /> -The unmoving face and the quiet, inhuman voice uneases even the most brave men, giving a minor intimacy of fear to anyone within earshot of the Abyssal.<br /> -The voice of the mask seems to pierce every other sound, even if it itself is a barely hearable whisper. The voice of the Abyssal is always hearable and understandable and can not be overpowered by louder sound. The voice does not carry any further than his normal voice does.<br /> -His face has hardened into this mask and is considered medium armor for as long as the mask is active. This only applies to his face and does not give him any penalties associated with wearing medium armor.<br /> <br /> Maybe a bit obvious, but Abyssals kind of need a creepy face type-Charm.<br /> <br /> <b>Isle-Shattering Strike<br /> <br /> Whispers of Ink and Salt<br /> <br /> Truths Written in Scars</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T14:09:38-08:00","id":346983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=346902#post346902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Truths Written in Scars</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Lunar Perception (or intelligence maybe) - indefinite (committed).<br /> <br /> The Lunar's eyes take on a silvery sheen - a layer of essence shows them the meaning behind markings carved in flesh and wood and stone.<br /> <br /> For the duration of this charm, markings such as scars, bruises, tattoos, claw marks and the like, appear to be exhaling glowing mists that form patterns of meaning, revealing the marking's purpose or reason for being. This often manifests as claw-speak, but is ultimately unique to each Lunar.<br /> <br /> Each success on a Perception (or Intelligence) + [Appropriate ability]* roll reveals pertinent information, such as:<br /> - what message the marking is supposed to send (e.g. &quot;stay away&quot;, &quot;remember your duty&quot;, &quot;You have no chance to survive, make your time&quot; etc.)<br /> - why it is there (&quot;to mark him as a traitor&quot;, &quot;to prevent him from walking ever again&quot;, &quot;so that no one will ever find him attractive&quot;, etc.)<br /> - how it was made (&quot;By a white-hot blade&quot;, &quot;by a Tiger of Larjin's claws&quot;, etc.)<br /> - what context it happened in (&quot;protecting own home&quot;, &quot;dueling for honor&quot;, &quot;begging for mercy&quot; etc.)<br /> etc.<br /> <br /> A tattoo can be revealed as being there to remind a warrior of a particular battle, scars can be revealed as coming from defending one's home from invaders, a tiger's missing eye can be revealed as being caused by a particularly callous poacher during a hunt.<br /> <br /> This charm can reveal such information about writing as well, though it doesn't automatically defeat attempts at misdirection - it can reveal the intended meaning of the piece and the context in which it was written, but it doesn't make lies any more obvious than they would usually be. If the writing (or tattoo) is coded, it might appear as devoid of meaning unless the Lunar knows the code. Likewise, this charm isn't affected by most common languages unless one is deliberately being used to obscure the message's meaning, and as such can offer rough translations - wording meant to be specific (such as loop-holes, plays on words, deliberate misspellings and technicalities) does not survive this translation.<br /> <br /> *Appropriate abilities include Craft for tattoos, medicine, survival for scars caused by &quot;natural&quot; means (animals and environments), Martial Arts, Thrown, Archery, War or Melee for markings caused by weapons or intended for troops, Linguistics for writing.<br /> <br /> Next: any of the previous unused ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T14:19:29-08:00","id":346993,"title":"","content":"Many thanks to Fata-Ku* for the Revive!<br /> <br /> In an attempt to forestall another 1.667 month hibernation, I'mma institute a new rule, soon to be added to the opening post:<br /> - If a full week has passed without any response to the current name(s), a new poster may respond to any unused prior name. Try to aim for something recent, though no biggie.<br /> <br /> * Who, incidentally, elicited a reaction of &quot;Oh, son of a--!&quot; for the Charm I just wrote up, until I saw the words &quot;any of the previous unused ones.&quot; ^_^<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=346902#post346902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Whispers of Ink and Salt</b></div> </div> </div> </div><b>Infernal</b> (Cecelyne; building off Penitents Like Scattered Grains)<br /> <br /> The Warlock has learned to hear prayers from places of desolation, but it sometimes serves her needs to receive petitions from more vibrant locales. An act of reducing the local vibrancy will do.<br /> <br /> Upon learning this Charm, the Green Sun Prince becomes able to receive prayers from even a lush location, so long as they are accompanied by an act that makes it more a place of desolation. Examples of appropriate acts include salting fertile land or drinking water, setting fire to local plant life, and releasing locusts. In order to qualify, the act must be difficult to reverse, but need not be large enough to create a new place of desolation by itself -- with enough local petitioners, this will surely happen soon enough.<br /> <br /> Should the Warlock also know Withered Soul Wastes or other Charms that expand the scope for a &quot;place of desolation,&quot; acts that use this expanded scope also qualify.<br /> <br /> <u>New Charm:</u><br /> <i>All Roads Meet</i><br /> OR<br /> <i>Yearning Heart Penance</i><br /> OR<br /> <i>Spark in the Depths Exhalation</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Broke up the text a bit. 04-19-2015, 08:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T10:38:04-08:00","id":347521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=346993#post346993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>All Roads Meet</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Raksha Way.<br /> <br /> Allows the Fairfolk to treat any 2 waypoints that are connected by up to [Way + Essence?] waypoints/journeys as being adjacent.<br /> <br /> In creation, the Raksha embarks on a scene of travel. Her surroundings gradually become indistinct and blur into a tedium of travel, such that she could be anywhere. The Fairfolk can change her location almost instantly to any location with a similar description within [some limit]. For example, the Raksha and her caravan might journey along a long road through the forest towards Nexus, only to appear on any other long road through the forest, this time leading to Larjin. Likewise, a Raksha might sail to sea, and the indistinct horizon allows her to shift her journey to anywhere on the vast ocean within [limit] that can be generally described the same way.<br /> This is a teleport effect and can be blocked by the usual wards etc.<br /> <br /> Next:<br /> <br /> <i>Ballad of Torn Beliefs</i><br /> OR<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Yearning Heart Penance</i><br /> OR<br /> <i>Spark in the Depths Exhalation</i> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T22:27:26-08:00","id":348821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=347521#post347521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Ballad of Torn Beliefs</i></div> </div> </div> </div><b>Solar Performance</b><br /> <br /> The song of the Lawgiver stirs its listeners to remember old convictions since abandoned. This Charm supplements any social influence through Performance that appeals to an Intimacy the Solar is aware of, at a former intensity, so long as the social influence is intended to make any subjects act in line with or further an ideology or personal conviction the subjects once held. For example, the Solar could attempt to lead in prayer people who have lost faith in their once-favored god. The Lawgiver's song could seek to move a corrupt magistrate to remember the idealism of her younger days and release prisoners from trumped up charges. A call to arms might inspire even a pacifist of many years to once again take up the sword. This Charm would not aid a ballad aiming to reconcile two estranged lovers, unless either or both once held strong beliefs that love never truly dies.<br /> <br /> ha ha ha i totally ripped off <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-exalted-3rd-edition/posts/853702\" target=\"_blank\">Subject-Hailing Ideology</a><br /> <br /> <u>New Charm:</u><br /> <i>Spark in the Depths Exhalation</i><br /> OR<br /> <i>Summit as Foothills Instruction </i><br /> OR<br /> <i>Iron-Graced Dreamer Form</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T11:56:00-08:00","id":349185,"title":"","content":"<b>Iron-Graced Dreamer Form</b><br /> <br /> Executing a stiff and languid kata, the Martial Artist takes on an otherworldly appearance as her Anima coalesces into flecks of iridescent metal covering her body in elaborate patterns. For the rest of the scene, her body takes on the properties of cold iron, gaining (minor soak/hardness bonus). Her natural attacks gain (accuracy/damage bonus) and can deal Lethal damage if she chooses, but always deal Aggravated damage to the Fair Folk and other denizens of the Wyld. She can also parry lethal and ranged attacks without a stunt. Finally, the unyielding nature of cold iron increases the difficulty of any rolled Shaping effect targeting the her by (Martial Arts/2).<br /> <br /> Iron-Graced Dreamer Form is incompatible with other effects that add the properties of other materials to natural attacks, such as Invulnerable Skin of Bronze, Wood Dragon's Claw, Blade of the Battle Maiden, Deadly Starmetal Offensive, and others. One notable exception is the spell Incomparable Body Arsenal. The ST is the final arbiter of which other effects can stack.<br /> <br /> [I wish I had the chops to write full martial arts styles, because a martial art that emulates an iron-striped fae would be super cool]<br /> <br /> Next: <br /> <br /> <i>Spark in the Depths Exhalation</i><br /> or<br /> <i>Lambent Tongue Atemi</i><br /> or<br /> <i>Champions-As-Chattel Pronouncement</i><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Playing 3e and miss Anathema? Try my web app, <a href=\"https://www.lotcastingatemi.com\" target=\"_blank\">Lot-Casting Atemi</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/553-hushnowquietnow","name":"hushnowquietnow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar553_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T13:20:55-08:00","id":349240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hushnowquietnow</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=349185#post349185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Lambent Tongue Atemi</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Solar Presence, building off Enemy Castignating Solar Judgement<br /> <br /> Keywords: Holy, Obvious, Combo-Ok or Combo-Basic (and probably others, I'm bad at keywords)<br /> Cost: Enough to balance it. Something like the attunement cost of chosen weapon + 3.<br /> <br /> The lawgiver's words carry supernal weight and truth enough to smite those that would go against his holy edicts. The solar pours holy burning light into his words, overloading them with the majesty of the searing noon. This energy leaves the solar's mouth and collides with the target, exploding in visual essence effects appropriate to the Exalt's anima - such as bursts of light, arcane sigils or holy chains that assault the target. Intense sunlight shines from the character's mouth as he speaks.<br /> <br /> The solar rolls a social attack as normal against a single target, save that it is made against the lowest of DV or MDV, and its speed is in ticks instead of long ticks. If an effect would make this attack Unnatural Mental Influence, attempts to block or dodge this attack cost the requisite amount of willpower no more than once per action (in the case of flurries, only the highest cost of any one attack needs to be paid for that action's defense).<br /> <br /> This attack has the weapon statistics and tags of an orichalcum weapon of the player's choosing (including long-ranged weapons). This choice is made when purchasing this charm and is permanent, save that it is always Reaching (for melee and martial arts weapons) and never requires more than 0 hands, and may never hit more than one target per attack. [an upgrade could conceivably attack groups though] In the case of long-ranged weapons, the words are carried to the target and are heard clearly - though anyone else outside of earshot hears nothing at all. Choosing a melee weapon means the target must be within this weapon's normal range to work (barring other charms).<br /> <br /> This charm deals aggravated damage to creatures of darkness, lethal damage to those that have betrayed the Solar or one of his intimacies, and bashing otherwise.<br /> At ST's discretion, particularly pure or innocent characters can be immune to this charm.<br /> <br /> This charm can be placed in a combo with charms of other abilities, such as Archery, Martial Arts, Bureaucracy or Melee.<br /> [insert solar merchant lashing a 1st-circle demon for trying to screw him in a trade deal].<br /> <br /> [Mouth Lasers!]<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://img3.wikia.nocookie.net/__cb20130106060135/onepiece/images/9/9e/Kuma_Fires_A_Laser_Beam.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> Next:<br /> <b>[Retracted in favor of While My Guitar's post]</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 12-24-2014, 04:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T13:42:13-08:00","id":349271,"title":"","content":"[Hopefully, 3e will make it easier to write a Martial Art like that, because it sounds pretty awesome]<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hushnowquietnow</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=349185#post349185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Lambent Tongue Atemi</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Infernal Brawl<br /> <br /> This Charm only works on those that have been previously wounded by Green Sun Nimbus Flare or any of its expansions and has survived it. The Infernal can, with a glance, recognize those that have survived the might of Malfeas, and punish those that dare to stand up after their weakness has been proven.<br /> Simply by speaking, the Solar can cause the scars created by the Malfean Fire to reopen, letting its victim feel the heat and the pain again. This inflicts [Essence] Unsoakable Lethal damage per turn upon it's targets, but can never kill them.<br /> <br /> At Essence 4, this Charm no longer requires it's spoken component, the old wounds opening by the presence of the Warlock alone.<br /> <br /> [Because nothing says Malfeas like reminding your opponent how they ended up last time they fought him, showing superiority through brutality]<br /> <br /> Next:<br /> <br /> <b>Spark in the Depths Exhalation<br /> <br /> Torn Hide Prophecy<br /> <br /> Sevenpronged Refabrication Apparatus</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-25T10:13:37-08:00","id":349932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Torn Hide Prophecy</b> </div> </div> </div>Astrology Ritual.<br /> <br /> The Pattern Spiders feast on the suffering of sentinel being. This ritual involve the astrologer inflicting pain on another being after a successful prayer roll directs at the Pattern Spider, this give the torturer an additional dice on any of his next Astrology ritual per Health Level sacrificed. Autocthon's Loyal Servants loves the scream of the Seers most of all, inflicting a Health Level on Sidereal Exalted give the astrologer five additional dices instead.<br /> <br /> <b>Celestial-Maiden Scatters Flowers<br /> <br /> 670-Meridians Sealing Needle<br /> <br /> Opening of the Eight Channels</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-25T21:17:33-08:00","id":350376,"title":"","content":"<b>Opening of the Eight Channels</b><br /> Solar Athletics Charm (high essence?)<br /> <br /> The Solar understands that the body is a mere limitation. The Solar\u2019s anima explodes into a full bonfire as raging essence burns through his veins, annihilating flesh, muscle, and bone with indiscriminate passion. Every action during which this charm is active, the Solar\u2019s body begins to burn away into oblivion as his flesh is castigated by the voluminous power arcing through him. In exchange, the Solar is freed from the limitations of a mortal form \u2013 for a time, at least.<br /> <br /> Activating this charm causes the solar to take aggravated damage over time, with a massive amount of life taken when the charm is terminated.<br /> <br /> For the duration that this charm is active, the Solar has their base attributes massively increased. This increase is treated as fully natural for all purposes.<br /> <br /> (Idea was eight gates from naruto - thanks to deathsworn for the idea)<br /> <br /> <b>New</b><br /> Nihilistic Oblation Embargo<br /> or<br /> Seventeen Faces Shaped From Sand<br /> or<br /> Shrouded Blossom Euphony Mein","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4613-ohsaucy","user":"ohSaucy","date":". 12-26-2014, 12:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4613-ohsaucy","name":"ohSaucy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4613_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-25T23:43:30-08:00","id":350503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ohSaucy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=350376#post350376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shrouded Blossom Euphony Mien</div> </div> </div> </div>Dragonblooded Presence (Wood)<br /> <br /> Once spotted, a hidden bloom is all the more pleasantly disarming for the surprise. This Charm enhances any social influence that would make the Terrestrial come off as more appealing or pleasant to one or more individuals, provided those targeted have not already taken particular note of the Terrestrial. Noticing her presence or even light conversation is not always sufficient to draw the necessary attention, unless that mere presence is especially notable to the potential targets or they otherwise form a strong opinion about her. On a busy and crowded street, the Dragonblooded could likely use it freely when interacting with new people, however merely being obviously identifiable as a Dragonblooded will make her notable in contexts where Terrestrials are not the norm (e.g. signs of one's House heritage will likely stand out in a satrapy, but may not by themselves at a social gathering in the Realm).<br /> <br /> Until the end of the scene or until the Dragonblooded gives a target cause to find her unappealing, she treats such individuals as valid targets for further invocations of this Charm, and pays only 1 mote per invocation to do so. Individuals with Intimacies that would lead them to disfavor the Terrestrial -- such as a Solar or Lunar whose disdain for the Realm extends to all or most Dynasts -- may be affected by the first invocation, but not beyond it.<br /> <br /> New Charm:<br /> <i>Champions-As-Chattel Pronouncement</i><br /> OR<br /> <i>Spark in the Depths Exhalation</i><br /> OR<br /> <i>Summer's Harsh Snowfall</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T06:52:17-08:00","id":350633,"title":"","content":"Summer's Harsh Snowfall<br /> Sidereal Occult<br /> <br /> To be cursed by a Sidereal is to have Fate itself turn against you. The Sidereal chooses one target that she has touched in the last ten minutes. For the next three months or until the next Calibration begins (whichever is sooner) this target is plagued by horrible, impossible weather wherever he goes for a mile radius in any direction. A blizzard will follow them on the hottest days, rain will soak him in the frozen north, lightning will strike his ships on a sunny day, etc etc. The target will live through the weather itself, but can still be killed by others. Say, an angry mob that decides that person is cursed by the gods and needs to die to appease them.<br /> <br /> A god can see that this effect has been caused by a Sidereal and, while capable of removing it, will likely be heavily questioned by Heaven if he does so.<br /> <br /> Wine before Pearls Method<br /> or<br /> Bliss of Lover's Morning","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-27T23:35:47-08:00","id":352369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HalfTangible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=350633#post350633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bliss of Lover's Morning</div> </div> </div> </div>Reminds me a lot of the divine works charms in Roll.<br /> <br /> <b>Adorjan</b><br /> This charm targets the subject of one of the warlock's positive intimacies of love toward a single individual. The warlock blows a kiss, and if the subject is willing, they fall asleep until the following dawn. This charm creates a sorcerous link to the target; (which may be dispelled with countermagic using the warlock's essence as the requisite minimum) when the warlock's lover next awakens, no matter where they are or how they are, the warlock returns to their side exactly as they left them the previous day. Any non-magical changes to the warlock vanish when she reappears - mundane wounds (bashing and lethal damage) are no longer there. Any artifacts that the warlock is not attuned to are left behind, as are any new mundane objects.<br /> <br /> if the warlock or their lover should take fatal damage while this charm is active the magic instantly terminates and their lover wakes up as if from a brutal nightmare, with full and terrible knowledge of their lover's demise; they lose (lover's essence) willpower.<br /> <br /> I could go more with this mechanically but you get the idea. Must sleeeeeep.<br /> <br /> new<br /> <b>Inspired Amelioration Embrace</b><br /> <b>Twisted Noumenon Assertion Mantra</b><br /> <b>Mind-Fire Ascension Stance</b><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4613-ohsaucy","user":"ohSaucy","date":". 12-28-2014, 12:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4613-ohsaucy","name":"ohSaucy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4613_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-28T18:04:18-08:00","id":353302,"title":"","content":"<b>Mind-Fire Ascension Stance</b><br /> An Infernal Heretical Charm, combining the Mind-Hand Manipulation tree of She Who Lives in Her Name, with Cecelyene's Soul-Sand Devil Shintai. It carries the Form-type and Messianic keywords, and transforms the Infernal into a vaguely humanoid shape of living white fire that feeds on the adoration and loyalty of her followers. The Infernal counts as both material and immaterial, whichever is more beneficial at a given moment, and adds her Willpower to her soak. She adds her Cult score to the accuracy, damage, and defense of her telekinetic attacks, and treats them as normal unarmed strikes for all relevant purposes, including the Touch keyword and martial arts styles. There are rumors that this Charm bears some connection to lost Theion.<br /> <br /> new:<br /> <b>Chaff-Threshing Technique<br /> Dragon's Rage Awakened</b><br /> <b>Price-of-Knowledge Sacrifice</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-28T23:35:18-08:00","id":353538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WarDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=353302#post353302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Price-of-Knowledge Sacrifice</b></div> </div> </div> </div><b>Raksha Heart</b><br /> <br /> Expressing infinite magnanimity, the Prince of Chaos forever sets a secret beyond his own reach and within reach of his lessers -- for a price. In using this Charm, the raksha identifies some knowledge he possesses, attaches a price, and extrudes it in the form of a token. This token takes the form of a small ordinary object, with some visible reflection of the knowledge within (an engineering secret may appear as a small gear, while information on someone the raksha adores may appear as a small heart-shaped stone). From then on, the Fair Folk no longer knows this secret and automatically fails any action that depends on knowing it. Even if reacquiring these facts by any means, using them remains elusive; the raksha will forget this knowledge by the end of the scene and actions that depend on knowing it, while they may be attempted during this time, suffer a -4 internal penalty. Actions that do not depend on this knowledge but attempt to incorporate it -- such as threatening someone by name after having forgotten everything about that someone -- suffer only a -2 internal penalty.<br /> <br /> Anyone who holds the token instinctively gains some understanding of the knowledge it contains and the raksha's price for learning it. This price may either be a number of dots of Virtue or Willpower, or it may be a particular request for information. If the individual chooses to pay this price, it is deducted immediately as the secret knowledge floods the petitioner's mind. In the case of information, the individual is not mystically robbed of it, but must give it honestly and completely to the best of his or her knowledge; no exchange is possible if the individual simply cannot answer the question. Some Lords of Chaos are fond of exchanging select knowledge for basic identifying information and a deep personal secret or two, for use in later fun.<br /> <br /> Should the raksha own the token, he receives payment immediately. Dots of Virtue or Willpower provide the raksha with motes, Willpower, and gossamer, as though feeding with Ravishing the Created Form, and the raksha immediately learns any paid information. If the token has left the Fair Folk's ownership, he receives nothing, but becomes aware that an exchange has taken place, the general nature of the secret knowledge and price, and a general sense of its location. Should it reenter the raksha's possession, prices paid are transferred immediately. If it is destroyed before this happens, the Prince of Chaos learns of its general location, the prices paid and secret knowledge that were lost, and the Fair One becomes able to acquire the secret anew. If the raksha holds the token in his hand, he may draw it back into himself, immediately reacquiring this knowledge, but becomes unable to ever part with it again by means of this Charm.<br /> <br /> New Charm:<br /> <i>Taming the Wyld Serpent</i><br /> OR<br /> <i>Heart Bound by Seven Wings</i><br /> OR<br /> <i>Spark in the Depths Exhalation</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T13:27:49-08:00","id":355063,"title":"","content":"Spark in the Depths Exhalation<br /> <br /> The breath of a dragon can be stopped by nothing the mortal world can bring to bear, not even the seas. A fire aspect using this charm may ignore any and all penalties related to oceans and the sea for as long as the duration lasts. The Fire Aspect's abilities can not be limited by mundane water of any kind in any way. In addition, the Fire Aspect may breathe underwater so long as their anima is (i don't remember the term for this - 8-10 motes spent? blazing?). A fire aspect may instead spend 1 mote for each hour spent underwater.<br /> <br /> <i>Taming the Wyld Serpent</i><br /> OR<br /> <i>Heart Bound by Seven Wings</i><br /> OR<br /> <i>Sun and Moon Entwined</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T18:53:30-08:00","id":355299,"title":"","content":"<b>Heart Bound by Seven Wings</b><br /> One of the foundational Charms of Oramus, this power renders the Infernal able to pass through virtually any barrier as if it were not there, except those of his own devising. This includes both physical walls that he built himself or had built, and psychological barriers; if he ever acts against an Intimacy, or breaks a sworn oath, the Charm's benefits deactivate, and he suffers a penalty to all actions for the remainder of the scene. His anima display is permanently altered to include seven ghostly dragon's wings when flaring totemic. Later Charms expand the benefits this Charm offers, making it increasingly unattractive to suppress; at Essence 10, it is nearly impossible to go against an oath or intimacy Each upgrade charm makes the anima-wings more tangible and prominent, until they finally become physical appendages surrounding the Infernal, granting protection and restriction in equal measure.<br /> <br /> <i>Sun and Moon Entwined</i> or<br /> <i>Harvest of Fangs Technique</i> or<br /> <i>Honor Among Enemies Declaration</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T20:46:35-08:00","id":355394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WarDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=355299#post355299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[<i>Honor Among Enemies Declaration</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Lunar Charm (hell if I know what attribute... charisma? manipulation? perception?)<br /> <br /> edit: I'll try to spruce up the writing in the morning; it didn't come out very well <br /> <br /> Entering the Lunar's territory means obeying her rules, lest one be devoured. The Lunar can activate this charm as part of a social influence roll (spoken or written) and can be used in tandem with territory charms - using markings that qualify as social interaction such as totems, signs and skulls. In every case, she is declaring a taboo or a code of conduct that must be upheld. In the case of written messages, only the target of the message is affected by this charm. In the case of territories, all creatures that cross its borders are considered bound to the taboo as long as they remain inside.<br /> <br /> Examples include &quot;If you walk without rhythm, you won't attract the wurm&quot;, &quot;Abandon all hope, ye who enter here&quot; (do not speak of hope or escape), &quot;I will suffer no thieves in my presence.&quot; (do not steal), &quot;[skulls on spears]&quot; (do not come here) and &quot;We may hate each other, but there's no reason to be rude about it.&quot; (show me due respect).<br /> It is important to note that this charm focuses on the Lunar's intent, not on her wording; as such, direct messages work best. There is no limit to the complexity of the taboo, so long as it is intelligible from the conveying medium.<br /> <br /> Whenever a creature would break the taboo or code of conduct, the wind carries the smell of her blood and the sound of her heart to the Lunar - effects such as Furious Bloodhound Pursuit can be activated immediately, at a discount and as though the Lunar has just tasted the target's blood. For as long as the Lunar hunts the target, Willpower spent intimidating, scaring, tracking or eluding the traitor (re-establishing surprise count as eluding for this purpose) is worth one more success than usual, and successfully punishing the traitor allows the Lunar to roll her [something that isn't conviction]* to regain spent willpower at a rate of 1 per success; this can take her up to 3 higher than her normal maximum. When several perpetrators within a bound group break the code, the Lunar only enjoys the [something that isn't conviction] roll once all of them have been punished.<br /> <br /> Lastly, time spent hunting with this charm can count as time spent on the Sacred Hunt.<br /> <br /> * because virtues aren't going to be the same in 3e.<br /> <br /> next: <b>Palace of Misconstrued Echoes</b> or <b>Gossamer Fingertips Posture</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":".  Reordered and clarified a little. I'm tired so I might try again tomorrow. 12-30-2014, 11:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-31T00:04:17-08:00","id":355515,"title":"","content":"Whoa nelly, did this one get away from me. x_x It's all entirely too elaborate and gets the wrong kinds of both &quot;very specific&quot; and &quot;very vague,&quot; but I can't help finding it cool and neat. There's also the concern that it may not precisely fit with the name, but it probably gets a pass, as the name describes both a strong use for a deceptive Sidereal and a word of caution to one just trying to get to the bottom of things. When used for investigation, it's all the more potent with aid from Solar Sherlocke Holmes (and Solar Phoenix Wright?). I'm also veeeery sleepy now.<br /> EDIT: It still works as a Sidereal Charm, but I also see a pretty good case for making this an artifact or a spell, come to think of it. Eh. Sleep.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=355394#post355394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Palace of Misconstrued Echoes</b></div> </div> </div> </div><b>Sidereal Investigation</b><br /> <br /> Performing a kata, the Sidereal commits the motes for this Charm and traces a vertical line at least as tall as herself, with sufficient space to her sides. Her fingers leave a green trail in the air or on the surface, and large ornate double-doors, adorned with iconography relevant to Jupiter, fade into being on either side. The doors will open only at the Sidereal's touch, though there is no limit to how many may follow. On the other side is a memory, obscured by white light, until the particular memory is chosen. The Sidereal may either select one of her memories or appoint one of her visitors to voluntarily share one. Should the visitor decline, the Sidereal may select another visitor, choose a memory of her own, or end the Charm's effects. The individual providing the memory becomes known as the Charm's subject.<br /> <br /> The Sidereal and all visitors then observe the chosen memory as its subject knew and understood it. They may will a scene to play backwards and forwards as desired. They may walk around the scene and may make rolls to acquire additional information about it, but cannot interact with anyone or anything. None may learn things of which the viewer is unaware, but can surmise things whether or not the viewer understands or understood them. For instance, if an unknown speaker was remembered as hidden behind a curtain, walking around the curtain will not reveal the individual, but those with an ear for voices or accents may find a clue.<br /> <br /> There are additional notes of caution for this Charm. The scene is observed as the subject remembers it, and so there may be discrepancies if there has been tampering with these memories. This includes both supernatural tampering and having been convinced -- or convincing oneself -- of what was actually remembered. Should the subject be convinced of anything else that &quot;must have happened,&quot; the scene will adjust to reflect this. What's more, if the memory's subject wishes to obscure or fabricate any components of the memory, be they contexts, details, events, the presence of individuals, or the like, she may deliberately do so. However, all of these discrepancies -- whether from tampering with a memory or deliberate deception -- create flaws and contradictions, which can be detected with successful &lt;insert uses of the Investigation sub-system&gt; opposed by traits (typically Larceny and Manipulation) from the source of the obfuscation.<br /> <br /> If successfully and logically demonstrated, the scene adjusts to reflect the newly understood truth (e.g. &quot;He must have been stabbed from this angle, which means his blood could not possibly have ended up there!&quot; or &quot;With where you were standing, you would never (or must) have been able to identify the culprit's face!&quot;). However, should the subject choose to deliberately withhold information, the scene will reflect only that something is being withheld and its general nature, but not the exact information (e.g. it will be clear the subject knows a particular person's face, but is choosing to obscure this). Unless information is withheld or part of the memory has been magically removed, identifying and addressing all of these flaws can completely reconstruct the memory exactly as the subject observed it.<br /> <br /> When the Sidereal ends this Charm, all individuals still inside the gate find themselves walking out of it as the gate closes and fades away behind them. Individuals may freely enter or exit the gate as they please until the Sidereal ends the Charm. On doing so, the Sidereal may enhance a social influence action that depends on any information the memory reveals, which affects only those who are still in the memory. Any individual may make similarly enhanced social influence actions when the memory changes to reflect a successful use of the Investigation sub-system, to a maximum of that individual's Investigation.<br /> <br /> Once the Sidereal has observed a memory, she may call it back using this Charm as though it was a memory of her own. However, if flaws are identified and rooted out, but the subject is not present to fill in any blanks, these are automatically treated as though information has been withheld. This also means the Sidereal may serve as the subject of the memory for others, and may thus choose to introduce deceptions as normal (which visitors may suss out in the manner described above).<br /> <br /> <u>New Charm:</u><br /> <i>Rasp of the Unloved</i><br /> OR<br /> <i>Sun and Moon Entwined</i><br /> OR<br /> <i>Gossamer Fingertips Posture</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":"remarking on plausible Spell-/Artifact-ness. 12-31-2014, 03:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T10:36:36-08:00","id":368731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Gossamer Fingertips Posture</b> </div> </div> </div>This one's still in the ideation phase. I'd like to do something more interesting with it than a rehash of Someone Else's Destiny.<br /> <br /> Getimian Larceny<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Action: Reflexive<br /> Duration: Action<br /> cost: idunno. Something balanced. I'm not good at balance.<br /> <br /> The Getimian's pattern spiders wrap strands of gossamer fates around her fingertips, subtly tricking Fate into never responding to the Exalt's touch.<br /> <br /> When the getimian deliberately touches something with her hands, any effect that would trigger as a result of such contact doesn't occur. Traps remain unsprung, poison does not enter the body, the scolding heat of molten metal does not boil the skin, swords do not slice off fingers and marks do not feel fingers entering their pockets. Particularly clever or potent effects or magical effects specifically meant to detect such action may cause a clash of wills roll at storyteller discretion; in such case, the exalt benefits from [a bonus... +larceny?].<br /> <br /> Additionally, the charm has one of the following effects:<br /> Yin: if the character paid for this charm with her Yin pool, pattern spiders scurry along her hands and fingers, creating a cocoon around the moment of contact and dragging it into the deepest recesses of the exalt's soul, to consume and dissect. The exalt may &quot;store&quot; the effect for later, keeping the charm's mote cost committed.<br /> <br /> Yang: if the character paid for this charm with her Yang pool, she may redirect the effect unto anyone she is able to successfully touch with her fingertips (including the originator. This might mean a trap poisons the wrong target, a sword cuts itself or its owner, or someone else feels the thief's hand stealing from their pockets) - typically this requires direct contact, but attuned weapons and form weapons may be exempt from this. For [a surcharge] she may also unleash one of her stored effects, creating a burst of iridescent cobwebs and immediately ending the charm.<br /> <br /> This charm can be used to Clash barehanded against lethal and aggravated attacks.<br /> <br /> <br /> Next:<br /> Tyrants' Teeth, Lover's Mouth<br /> OR<br /> Rasp of the Unloved<br /> OR<br /> Sun and Moon Entwined<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T12:16:46-08:00","id":368826,"title":"","content":"Sun and Moon Entwined<br /> Solar Occult<br /> The Sun and Moon are companions eternal, gathering strength from each other for all time. The Solar seizes upon the bond he shares with his Lunar mate and uses it to channel his essence. The Solar gives up a dot of Essence (not a mote) to increase the Lunar's Essence by one. This move is permanent, but can be repeated once for each dot of Solar Bond the Lunar mate possesses. The lost dot of Essence can be repurchased with XP as normal. The Solar does not lose any charms, but must meet the prerequisites again in order to use them. The Solar may not perform this technique twice in the span of 5 months, causes the solar 3 health levels of damage, and leaves the solar unconscious for 5 hours.<br /> <br /> Fate's Cruel Kiss<br /> OR<br /> Tyrants' Teeth, Lover's Mouth<br /> OR<br /> Rasp of the Unloved","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":879,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","user":"HalfTangible","date":". 01-13-2015, 03:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T12:16:56-08:00","id":368827,"title":"","content":"Sun and Moon Entwined<br /> Lunar wits<br /> cost:-<br /> type: Permanent<br /> duration: Permanent<br /> prerequisite charms: none<br /> description: The strongest thing about adaptability is making your greatest weakness your greatest strength. When a lunar is dealing with their solar mate, the solar feels the lunar's undominatable feelings for kinship as well. The solar is considered to have the lunar's solar bond but toward his lunar mate. The experience cost is halved if the lunar has been affected by sun and moon method.<br /> <br /> <br /> Snatching defeat from the jaws of victory<br /> or<br /> Fate of all fools<br /> or<br /> For kingdom come, thy will be done","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T12:55:45-08:00","id":372813,"title":"","content":"<b>Snatching defeat from the jaws of victory</b><br /> Infernal (Ebon Dragon) charm.<br /> <br /> Standing triumphant over his opponent fills the Dragon's Shadow with sorrow, for he is about to once more lose the thing he loves.<br /> <br /> The infernal can activate this charm any time he vanquishes or is about to vanquish a foe to create a momentum-shifting turnabout - the target seems to gain the upper hand in a completely unforeseen manner, enough to triumph over the infernal, but not so much that escape is impossible. The situation need not be life-or-death. It can be as simple as a game of cards or as complicated as a days-long political debate.<br /> <br /> This victory is hollow however, and the defeat-that-never-was hangs in the target's shadow, slowly poisoning her soul. For as long as motes are committed to this charm, the target gains an appropriate sorcerously-charged negative intimacy towards the Exalt that pushes them to pursue them further (such as Punishment for transgressions, Revenge for an other slight, Obsession). Additionally, the Infernal's proximity pushes the target to unknowingly sabotage themselves in everything they do, increasing external penalty of most actions by +1. Any time the target would take a course of action that would indirectly go against the infernal or his goals, the penalty instead increases by +2. Going directly against the infernal or his plans increases the difficulty by the exalt's Essence rating, for a maximum of [something.. +5?] as long as they share the same Scene. Lastly, when the target obtains no successes, 2s follow the Rule of 1 (both 1s and 2s count as botches).<br /> <br /> This effect ends once the Infernal is about to take revenge on the target, at the beginning of the action that would decide the outcome.<br /> [essentially, in the same circumstances that allow its activation, preventing this charm from stacking with itself.]<br /> <br /> An infernal can only sustain as many activations of this charm as his Essence score.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Fate of all fools</b><br /> <br /> Upgrade to Snatching Defeat From the Jaws of Victory<br /> <br /> By spending [a surcharge] The infernal may activate this charm against a group, making it count as a single entity for the purpose of its prerequisite's activation limits. In this case, only the leader gains the relevant intimacy.<br /> <br /> Everybody in the group seems to desert the target, making the unit losing magnitude with every failed roll. Botches turn the mob against its former master - units split off and actively go against their now-hated leader.<br /> <br /> <br /> Next:<br /> <b>Below the Sea of Calm.</b><br /> OR<br /> <b>Tyrants' Teeth, Lover's Mouth</b><br /> OR<br /> <b>Duplicitous Filigree Adornment</b><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T14:02:13-08:00","id":372863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=372813#post372813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[<br /> <b>Below the Sea of Calm.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Kimbery Charm<br /> While the Sea who Marched Against the Flame is a being of insuperable passions, the full knowledge of their depths is to be known only at her own sufferance.<br /> Any infernal with this charm is momentarily aware of any Read Motivation action is taken upon them; while this knowledge fades instantly on its own, spending the mote cost of this charm retains it and makes a counterattack. The Warlock rolls Appearance + Presence against her target's Dodge MDV in retaliation; success momentarily fills the target with a wider scope of the Infernal's being than they intended: images swim through their mind's eye of a blur, comprised of snippets of Intimacies and creatures of the deep dark waters. This vision grants no further insights for the Read Motivation action, but it does fill the character with an Intimacy of Fear towards the Infernal which requires one willpower to be spent each scene it is eroded.<br /> If she uses this charm upon a Beloved target, they immediately become Reviled: those who are uncertain of Kimbery's love do not deserve it anyway.<br /> <br /> Next:<br /> Cultivated Jade Blossom Technique<br /> OR<br /> Embers of a Fallen Star<br /> OR<br /> Inescapable Nightmare Cry<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T21:54:16-08:00","id":373311,"title":"","content":"<b>Cultivated Jade Blossom Technique</b><br /> Dragonblooded crafting charm<br /> cost: variable mins: Craft 3, essence 2 type: dramatic<br /> Keywords: combo-ok<br /> duration: scene<br /> prerequisite charms: Shaping hand Style<br /> description: <br /> <br /> The Princes of the Earth can enrich their lands. By meditating in a field from one dawn to the next, a dragonblood both draws susteinance from the ground - making food and drink unnecesary for the duration - but also lends her own essence to the ground, enriching it and greatly nourishing any plants sown in the field. At the end of the charm any crop growing in the field is fully grown, matured and ready to harvest. In the case of this charm being used in orchards only the harvestable crop grows, not the bushes or trees being harvested from - unless the surrounding area was planted with for example apple seeds, in which case apple trees will grow, but will not bear fruit unless the charm is used again on them.<br /> <br /> The charm costs 4 motes per square mile x Essence of the Dragon-Blood.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T12:11:28-08:00","id":373660,"title":"","content":"<b>Embers of a Fallen Star</b><br /> Solar War/Performance/Bureacracy<br /> <br /> Even after a flame burns out, the embers may spark a new blaze, if they find fuel. This unusual Charm has no effect while the Solar lives; rather, it is taken as a contingency plan should death find them. It can be taken once for each of the above listed abilities, and allows the Solar's <i>hun </i>to linger, and use his other Charms from that ability on behalf of his followers for (Essence) days after his demise. At the end of the time, whether he has been properly avenged or not, the ghost is forced into Lethe and the lingering effects fade.<br /> <br /> <b>Inescapable Nightmare Cry</b><br /> or<br /> <b>Tyrants' Teeth, Lover's Mouth</b><br /> or<br /> <b>Wake of the Void Phoenix</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-18T05:49:55-08:00","id":374217,"title":"","content":"<b>Wake of the Void Phoenix</b><br /> Abyssal athletics charm<br /> Cost: +5 Mins: Ath 5, Essence 5 type: supplemental<br /> Keywords: combo-ok<br /> duration: scene<br /> prerequisite charms: On Wings of Night<br /> description:<br /> <br /> Abyssals leave death in their wake.<br /> When an abyssal takes flight with On Wings of Night, their anima sheds tiny flakes of necrotic tissue in its wake, poisoning the land the abyssal flies over.<br /> <br /> This poison remains after the charm ends for up to Essence number of days,and presents an environmental hazard to anything that stays in the poisoned land for more than a day.<br /> <br /> Void Phoenix Venom: Damage 1L/day Toxicity: Essence/2 (round up) Pentalty: -1<br /> <br /> Plants and trees wither after a week, but rain can wash the poison away - though that does concentrate the poison into the local waterways.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Dragon Butter Technique<br /> <br /> Heavenly Tongue Prana<br /> <br /> Stolen Kiss Understanding</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":588,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","user":"webkilla","date":". 01-18-2015, 08:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-19T17:01:54-08:00","id":375692,"title":"","content":"<b>Stolen kiss understanding</b><br /> Sidereal &lt;Something&gt; (I am not a homebrewer, especially for sidereals, someone else will have to figure this out from there.)<br /> <br /> Stealing a kiss with their tongue wrapped in a rice paper prayer strip, the sidereal gains insight into their partners heart. She learns his motivation, current virtue ratings, and any intimacies he holds. For an additional price of (Expensive) She may choose to usurp one of these intimacies, making herself the subject of that intimacy. If the sidereal was already the subject of an intimacy, she may opt to place the subject of the usurped intimacy in that one for (cheap), otherwise, the intimacy fades.<br /> <br /> <b>&quot;Convicted Flowers Beneath the Guilty Sky</b><b>&quot;</b><br /> <br /> Or<br /> <br /> <b>&quot;Teasing Mate Stance&quot;</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Currently Playing:</b> <i>A large, mixed splat game of <b>CofD</b>.</i> <b>As:</b> Seraph du Salomon, Voice on the concordance. Unsubtle man reluctantly participating in the business of Magi. Awakening 2E homebrew <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1338514-house-du-salomon-a-proximus-dynasty?_=1569864567692\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...=1569864567692</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","name":"Gryphon's Feather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2598_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"215"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-20T03:33:45-08:00","id":376029,"title":"","content":"<b>Teasing Mate Stance</b><br /> Lunar lewd charm<br /> Req: Appearance 3, Essence 4<br /> duration: scene<br /> <br /> The lunars have long wanted means to exert influence over their solar mates, in the same way that solars can on them. This was the result of one such experiment, created with a sympathetic solar in secret during the first age.<br /> <br /> The lunar rolls Cha or Manip (whichever is highest) + performance, doing an ancient dance that Luna once did to entice the UCS while in the presence of his solar mate. If the lunar gets more sucs than the solar has social DV, the solar gains an intimacy of lust towards the lunar, and for the rest of the scene has to spend 2wp to not pay attention to the lunar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T07:49:27-08:00","id":377234,"title":"","content":"<b>Convicted Flowers Beneath the Guilty Sky</b><br /> <br /> Terrestrial Circle Sorcery<br /> <br /> The sorcerer prepares a brew of rare and potently hallucinogenic herbs. A catalyst is prepared from a token tied to a sin or a crime, smeared in the sorcerer's blood and imbibed with the brew. The sorcerer names the sin or the crime, and can be as general or specific as desired; however, the spell doesn't heed names. &quot;Consorting with Maurvile the Cannibal&quot; would target anyone consorting with any cannibal.<br /> <br /> Invoking the scripture of the Guilty Maiden and cursing in all 5 directions, the sorcerer buries the token in the center of a town (or at a crossroads if outside of one).<br /> <br /> That same night and for [The Sorcerer's Essence] nights thereafter, small sickly-white flowers grow and bloom around the beds and doors of any and all who are guilty of the named sin or crime according to its wording. These flowers' pollen carries the effects of the brew, instilling hallucinations, terror and severe paranoia in the guilty. Most often, these hallucinations manifest as blood-streaked skies that sing the dirges of the guilty, and the sun and moon appear as inescapable eyes of celestial judgement.<br /> <br /> The sorcerer must be careful however - while flowers won't grow around the caster, their pollen is indiscriminate in its effects. If the caster is also guilty of the cursed sin or crime according to its wording, breathing in the flowers' pollen will have its full effect.<br /> <br /> Mechanically, all targets count as being afflicted with [a very potent and debilitating toxin that causes little damage]. This poison isn't supernatural however, and is subject to treatment, immunity and resistance as normal.<br /> <br /> Next:<br /> <b>Tyrants' Teeth, Lover's Mouth</b><br /> or<br /> <b>Duplicitous Filigree Adornment</b><br /> or<br /> <b>Inescapable Nightmare Cry</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 01-21-2015, 10:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T11:51:26-08:00","id":377404,"title":"","content":"Ah screw it. I have an idea for this.<br /> <br /> <b>Tyrants' teeth, Lover's Mouth</b><br /> <br /> Liminal charm<br /> type: permanent.<br /> cost: none (5 motes, 1wp)<br /> <br /> The Liminal may replace his own teeth with any of those he finds - be they human, shark or river dragon - by ripping out the old and jamming in the new. This allows them to replicate the special attacks of the creature's mouth as long as the vast majority of the teeth are part of that set. The Chernozem's mouth remains as inconspicuous as any human's, hiding the disproportionate geometry and razor-sharp lethality of their newly-acquired maw.<br /> <br /> For example, the Liminal could replicate a boar's or elephant's charge, a tyrant lizard's bite, a Comodo Dragon's venomous attack, or even a Giant Spider's mandibles.<br /> <br /> This charm's cost need only be paid when the Liminal wishes to make use of the special attacks endowed by his monstrous teeth, at which point the Liminal must take a misc. action for the maw and teeth to take their positions in a grotesque display of popping joints, jutting bones and dripping ectoplasm. Once activated, the teeth are activated for the rest of the scene.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: also this:<br /> <br /> <b>Duplicitous filigree Adornment</b><br /> <br /> Getimian Craft<br /> <br /> The Getimian rolls Intelligence + Craft and fashions a temporary Filigree out of one of her personal pattern spiders, which looks like a small, beatifully intricate clockwork mechanism with a perceived Resources rating of the Getimian's Essence Rating. An exceptional success on the craft roll adds 2 to this value, to a maximum of 5. The decoration affixes itself flawlessly to any surface and adjusts its aspect to complement any outfit as the patter spider adjusts its shape and color. This newly created object may be given as a present to anyone, though its destruction means the destruction of one Getimian's pattern spiders, causing one level of unsoakable aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> The filigree subtly tugs at the fates of conversations and endeavours, having one fo the following effects depending on the mote pool used to activate it:<br /> <br /> <b>Yin:</b> The filigree dulls the interest of anyone interacting with the bearer, making them treat everybody's intimacies as one level weaker for the purposes of Social Influence - they simply don't find the character's word interesting in the slightest.<br /> <br /> <b>Yang:</b> The filigree augments the resonance in the bearer's words, allowing her to treat the intimacies she wishes to exploit in others as being one level higher. At storyteller's discretion, this may reawaken old (read: abandonned and forgotten) Defining Intimacies at the weakest level.<br /> <br /> (hey, if you can have combat bonuses in Dodge, you can have Social bonuses in Craft).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Next:<br /> <b>Duplicitous Filigree Adornment</b><br /> or<br /> <b>Inescapable Nightmare Cry</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 01-21-2015, 04:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T12:55:02-08:00","id":377469,"title":"","content":"<b>Inescapable Nightmare Cry</b><br /> <br /> Abyssal Presence<br /> <br /> The Deathknight unleashes a powerful shout in a dark language known only to the dead. The Abyssal rolls [Manipulation + Presence] against every one in Range. All targets with MDVs less than the Abyssals rolled successes come under a fear effect that prevents them from fleeing from the Abyssal and take a penalty to their DVs. The penalty can be offset by paying one WP, the inability to flee by paying 3 WP over the scene.<br /> <br /> Next:<br /> <b>Belligerent Essence Invocation</b><br /> or<br /> <b>Fallen Sky Technique</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Life before Death, Strength before Weakness, Journey before Destination.&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">&quot;I will protect those who cannot protect themselves&quot;</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4172-marros56","name":"Marros56","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4172_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T13:11:56-08:00","id":377481,"title":"","content":"<b> Fallen sky technique</b><br /> <br /> Isidirous charm (didn't want to look up spelling)<br /> type reflexive<br /> cost: [x]<br /> <br /> The infernal does not fall, he brings the sky with him. When the warlock would take damage from falling and/or knockback the damage is also inflicted onto what he hit. If this was a structure (which it likely is) the damage is multiplied by essence and ignores mundane soak, a repurchase at essence [x] makes the damage on the warlock ignored so only what he landed on is damaged, at essence [x] this also ignores the soak from magical materials and the damage is multiplied by essence times two.<br /> <br /> Thy kingdom come thy will be done<br /> or<br /> Face to fist method<br /> or<br /> There once was a maiden...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T13:31:44-08:00","id":377508,"title":"","content":"Thy Kingdom Come, Thy Will be Done<br /> <br /> DB Integrity<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> <br /> The Children of the Dragons know that there is wisdom in the words of those who stand above them. The Exalt swears an oath to themselves to uphold a superior's belief. (The Superior can be a DB Ancestor, Solar Commander, Etc.). This grants a bonus to MDV against attempts to turn them against the principle.<br /> <br /> Next:<br /> Dying Light Rekindled<br /> or<br /> Spirit-Forging Cataclysm","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Life before Death, Strength before Weakness, Journey before Destination.&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">&quot;I will protect those who cannot protect themselves&quot;</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4172-marros56","name":"Marros56","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4172_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T13:45:38-08:00","id":377518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=377481#post377481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Face to fist method</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's Isodoros by the way.<br /> <br /> Isodoros Brawl Charm<br /> type: Reflexive<br /> <br /> A fighter is taught to always raise his shields against the strikes of his enemies. But Isodoros knows that this is simply a sign of weakness, and those that are actually strong don't bother to waste the steel of their weapons on the steel of another.<br /> Whenever the Infernal is struck at melee range, he may automatically parry and perform a counterattack upon his opponent. This attack is always applied to the limb or the weapon the person used to attack the Infernal with. The damage of this counterattack is [Essence+Brawl] in Bashing damage.<br /> If the Infernal's soak is high enough that the attack inflicted upon him does no damage, Face to fist method deals lethal damage instead,<br /> <br /> Isodoros needs a charm where someone can break their own hand punching superman in the jaw.<br /> <br /> Next:<br /> Forged from Flesh and Steel<br /> <br /> Approaching Glacier Consternation<br /> <br /> There are No Innocents<br /> <br /> Edit: Sorry Marros56, I was typing out my charm while you posted yours.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","user":"While My Guitar","date":". 01-21-2015, 04:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T14:33:11-08:00","id":377544,"title":"","content":"<b>Dying Light Rekindled</b><br /> <br /> DB Dodge.<br /> <br /> Duration: [dodge+specialty] actions?<br /> <br /> The exalts wounds burn with the light of her anima, conferring uncanny reflexes and agility.<br /> For each lethal or aggravated wound, the Exalt adds one yard to her movement rate and one to her dodge rating for [dodge+specialty] actions, up to normal dice-adder limits. The Exalt can use this extra movement during a dodge attempt, seeming to flicker out of the way of attacks. In an action where she has used her full movement (including the extra), she may apply that many dice as a bonus to her raw damage as her attack bursts with the same light that gives her new-found energy (capped by Dodge). This immediately ends the charm.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Approaching Glacier Consternation</b><br /> <br /> DB Presence (water-aspected)<br /> <br /> Type: supplemental<br /> Duration: [presence + specialty] actions?<br /> <br /> With a well-placed glance, the Dragons' chosen chill the veins of their rivals, plaguing them with the inevitability of a crushing defeat. The dragonblood activates this charm in tandem with an Intimidation attempt (usually Charisma or Appearance + Presence). If successful, the afflicted feels an overwhelming and oppressive urge to back away from the dragonblooded whenever he draws near. If the target cannot back away they suffer a penaly to their actions equal to [distance covered in yards capped by Presence + specialty] as their blood stiffens and their breath draws shorter. The feeling is not unlike a mix of claustrophobia and drowning.<br /> <br /> <br /> Next:<br /> <b>Faux-fire Trick</b><br /> or<br /> <b>Twitching Shadows Maneuver</b><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 01-21-2015, 05:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T14:50:42-08:00","id":377551,"title":"","content":"<b>Faux-fire Trick</b><br /> DB performance charm<br /> <br /> Cost: 8<br /> <br /> Duration: scene<br /> <br /> Tricks of light, fire and spectacle are all tools of the trade for an entertainer chosen by the dragons. This charm grants Performance/2 auto-sucs in performances rolls.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Spawn-Altering Strike</b><br /> or<br /> <b>Unoriginal Charm Name</b><br /> or<br /> <b>Tear-Soaked Deathcry Deceit</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T17:10:12-08:00","id":377617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=377518#post377518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: Sorry Marros56, I was typing out my charm while you posted yours.</div> </div> </div> </div>No worries, these things happen.<br /> <br /> <b>Unoriginal Charm Name</b><br /> <br /> Sidereal...Craft, I guess?<br /> <br /> When the Maidens chose to empower their own chosen with 100 great events they gave their champions dominion over fate itself, allowing them to use powers most minds could not comprehend... and this one. It lets the Sidereal do... stuff... and do it better, kinda? Venus may have been a bit tipsy when she came up with this one.<br /> <br /> Fury-Born Excellence Stance<br /> or<br /> Innocent Guilt Declaration","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Life before Death, Strength before Weakness, Journey before Destination.&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">&quot;I will protect those who cannot protect themselves&quot;</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4172-marros56","name":"Marros56","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4172_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T11:56:51-08:00","id":378260,"title":"","content":"<b>Innocent Guilt Declaration</b><br /> <br /> Dragonblooded Bureaucracy<br /> <br /> Defending an other (or himself) in court (or in front of a mob), the Dragonblooded expertly plucks the heart strings of his audience and explains that the defendant's actions were simply an innocent mistake, or that they had noble goals, such that the audience is swayed to show magnanimous mercy and look the other way, no matter how severe the defendant's actions were. This supplements an Instill action to create an intimacy similar to &quot;Childlike Innocence&quot; which the Dragonblood can then exploit, allowing the Instill action to benefit from its own soon-to-be intimacy.<br /> <br /> Next: <b>Tiny Universes Mantra</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T10:09:30-08:00","id":401995,"title":"","content":"<b>Twitching Shadows Maneuver</b> - Solar Stealth<br /> <br /> Instant, 1 action, supplemental<br /> <br /> The Solar acts with such speed and subtlety that even shadows struggle to keep up.<br /> While this charm is active, the solar seems to be doing nothing at all - engaging in pointless banter, keeping on with whatever he was doing (writing, showering) or just standing there. This charm permits the Solar to roll Dexterity + Stealth and to perform a single Action's worth (5 or 6 ticks) of actions under the guise of mundanity. He could, for example, dash to a podium, steal the crown it holds and dash back to his starting position, while seemingly not having moved or done anything at all. The difficulty to notice the Solar's actions is [his stealth successes = his essence]. This charm can be reactivated at the beginning of the next action to extend its effects, for a maximum of [the Solar's Stealth] consecutive activations.<br /> <br /> If when this charm ends the solar is in a different location than when it started, his image seems to vanish in a puff of dust at the end of that action.<br /> [cue Homer Simpson vanishing in a puff of dust at the mention of doughnuts]<br /> <br /> This charm can explicitly be comboed with charms of other abilities.<br /> <br /> ===========================================<br /> <br /> <b>Tear-Soaked Deathcry Deceit</b> - Abyssal Performance<br /> The abyssal makes a great show of mournful heartbreak at the death of a person (at the moment of their death or when the topic is brought up). These crocodile tears are so convincing that as long as the charade is upheld, onlookers are convinced that the Abyssal bears a positive Defining Intimacy towards the deceased. Their attempts to exploit that intimacy however (even if in a positive manner, such as offering condolences) suffer from a penalty equal to the bonus such an exploitation would incur. Every failed attempt feeds The Lover's empty heart with warmth and compassion, robbing the target of a point of willpower and providing the Abyssal with a cumulative +1 Appearance bonus (to a maximum of +Essence) for as long as motes remain committed.<br /> <br /> <br /> Next:<br /> <b>Tiny Universes Mantra</b><br /> OR<br /> <b>Fury-Born Excellence Stance</b><br /> OR<br /> <b>Forged from Flesh and Steel</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T18:56:23-08:00","id":402743,"title":"","content":"<b>Fury-Born Excellence Stance</b><br /> Solar Martial Arts<br /> <br /> This charm may only be used when the Solar currently has at least five health levels of damage. For the rest of the scene, any attack roll the Solar makes where the number of succeses are greater than (11 - Valor - Compassion) wounds as if every dice roll was a 10. At the end of the scene, the Solar takes an additional 5 health layers of damage. If at any point during the scene the Solar reaches a point where this end-of-scene damage would kill him, the charm ends but he does not take the damage; Instead, he immediately falls unconscious and cannot use this charm again for 10 years.<br /> <br /> <b>Tiny Universes Mantra</b><br /> OR<br /> <b>Pheremones of Spring Method</b><br /> OR<br /> <b>Forged from Flesh and Steel</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T19:31:25-08:00","id":402782,"title":"","content":"<b>Forged from Flesh and Steel</b> - Celestial Circle Sorcery<br /> <br /> Devised by the Queen of Fangs as a weapon of terror and destruction (when the time arises for such things), she has thoroughly lost control of its distribution; it graces the libraries of many Lunar and Sidereal sorcerers alike. The servant created by this spell's power is a versatile, reliable companion.<br /> <br /> Using a hammer made of the bones of an earth elemental, the sorcerer beats steel plates into a rough facimile of a skeleton (or a suit of armor) in a ritual that lasts six hours. The light of the full moon is preferred for such an endeavor, for the steel flows like quicksilver under her hammer under Luna's gaze and hardens as the moon sets, but with enough strength and determination it may be done at any time.<br /> <br /> Her own flesh weaves itself into the construction, spinning into iron-tough joints and ligaments that allow the construct to move with great speed and strike with great strength. Seals of blood are inscribed into it, and a rudimentary intelligence awakens and a baleful red flame glows where its eyes would be. This construct is utterly loyal to the sorcerer, but is not particularly bright and usually extremely literal in its interpretation of commands. (If told not to kill anyone, it may maim a mortal in the way of its objective and explain, &quot;he'll live.&quot;)<br /> <br /> In an additional component of the ritual, traces of blood or shed skin from an enemy may be powdered and incorporated into the blood seals. If this is done, the construct forever knows the direction in which its quarry can be found. When created in this manner, it can't be bargained with. It can't be reasoned with. It doesn't feel pity, or remorse, or fear. And it absolutely will not stop, ever, until they are dead.<br /> <br /> <b>Tiny Universes Mantra</b><br /> or<br /> <b>Pheromones of Spring Method</b><br /> or<br /> <b>Lessons in Scarlet</b><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","name":"Guancyto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T08:13:31-08:00","id":403339,"title":"","content":"<b>Tiny Universes Mantra</b><br /> <br /> Raksha Cup, requiring that one charm that lets you Shape inside people's dreams.<br /> Costly enough to only be used once in a while, because setting it up might be a huge pain for the ST. Like... 10 motes, 5 gossamer and 1 willpower.<br /> <br /> <br /> Having perfected the art of Shaping the Soul, the Raksha recognises mortal souls for what they truly are: a myriad of worlds, all twisted upon themselves. When inside a Creation-born's dreams, the Raksha spends a scene invoking the Mantra of Tiny Universes to reveal the true splendor of the target's Soul and rolls [Manipulation + Craft (Glamour)], contested by the target's [Willpower + Integrity + Wyld Resistence Bonus]. If successful, the Raksha can Quest against that mortal's soul as though it were an Unshaped - the storyteller makes up Actors and Graces based upon the mortal's virtues, essence and willpower. Effects that protect the target's soul from Shaping permit a Clash of Wills rolls. Directly touching iron protects the target from the effects of this charm.<br /> <br /> The Raksha can gain the usual benefits from doing so: gaining or improving Graces, Treasures, Spells, Behemoths and Oaths. Mortals are left permanently deranged by this process - their relevant virtues lose a number of dots equal to the new rating of the Raksha's relevant Artifact (so if it was raised to 3, the victim loses 3 points in the relevant virtue) and that virtue's channels are emptied completely.<br /> <br /> This is a Crippling effect that cannot be healed without magic.<br /> <br /> [Fairfolk get to play Disgaea 3 with mortals]<br /> <hr />I always feel like a prick when I pick up my own names, so here, have another.<br /> <br /> <b>Pheromones of Spring Method</b><br /> Sidereal Serenty (Performance? or... Socialize? haven't read Sidereals in a while)<br /> The sidereal temporarily summons the aspect of the season of love upon an area. For the rest of the scene, animals act as though they were in heat, flowers release pollen and people are more open to amourous encounters.<br /> <br /> For the scene, the sidereal can pluck the strands of fate that bind people, creating a metaphysical melody that allows everyone within the area to be treated as having a strong positive intimacy of &quot;Seeking a realtionship&quot; - this relationship need not be specifically amourous, it might also be friendship or short-lived lust, whatever is most appropriate for the individual. If an appropriate intimacy already exists, it is treated as being one level higher. If it's already Defining, then this charm has no further effect on that target.<br /> <br /> [cue Bow-chicka-wow-wow background music played on Fate Strands by a Sidereal]<br /> <br /> <br /> Next:<br /> <b>Mouse Commands Arrow</b><br /> OR<br /> <b>Cloak of Shades and Regrets</b><br /> OR<br /> <b>Bureaucrats' Demands Form</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T09:14:57-08:00","id":403371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=403339#post403339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Mouse Commands Arrow</b></div> </div> </div> </div><b>Solar Bureaucracy</b><br /> <br /> Though none may ever notice a mouse's nibble on an arrow, little can more affect its trajectory. When issuing a directive appropriate to her station or petitioning for such from a superior, the Solar receives a bonus on attempts to make this appear small, innocuous, and inappropriate to investigate. In addition, the difficulty increases on investigative actions that would conclude the directive was inappropriate. A Solar undercover in an enemy command center might have an easy time of ordering equipment moved around a few barracks, and then remain above suspicion when it just so happens to put arms and firedust stores in disastrous locations when those barracks are invaded.<br /> <br /> <u>New Charm:</u><br /> <b>Cloak of Shades and Regrets</b><br /> OR<br /> <b>Lessons in Scarlet</b><br /> OR<br /> <b>Trumpet Blaring Denunciation</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T08:39:03-08:00","id":404502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Guancyto</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Lessons in Scarlet</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Fire-Aspect Linguistics.<br /> <br /> 2m per paragraph, supplemental, indefinite<br /> <br /> The Exalt infuses her writing instrument with scarlet essece - the blood of Hesiesh - that marks the page briefly before disappearing. As long as motes remain committed to this charm, the essence-ink remains invisible and undetectable except through effects that can percieve essence (and even then, effects like Measure the Wind don't offer enough precision to read the message, though All Encompassing Sorcerer's Sight would.)<br /> <br /> Burning the medium that the message was written on releases the essence (and the commitment), creating luminous fire glyphs that hang in the air for a second before disappearing. Though its appearance is brief, the message lingers in the vision and memory of any onlookers long enough to absorb its full meaning, no matter how long the text was.<br /> <br /> Releasing the motes committed to this charm may set the medium ablaze, triggering the described effect, may simply erase the message, or make it appear as normal writing (a mixture of burn and charcoal marks) at the Exalt's discretion.<br /> <br /> Edit: on second thought, this might be better as a longer-lasting, reactivate-able sorcery enchantment or something... hmmm <hr /><br /> <br /> <b>Cloak of Shades and Regrets</b><br /> <br /> 1st circle Necromancy.<br /> <br /> The Necromancer restrains a ghost and shoves her whole arm down the throat of a ghost while performing the mudra of past regrets. As she pulls her hand out, the ghost is simultaneously turned inside out and transmogrified into a shimmering cowl of pitch-black ectoplasm interwoven with Soulsteel thread.<br /> <br /> Wearing the cowl cloaks the Necromancer in spectral shadows. Anyone catching even a glimpse of the caster has their deepest regrets come to the forefront of their minds and feel old wounds anew. This serves to drive attention away from the caster, imposing [some internal penalty due to grief and distraction] on most actions.<br /> <br /> Anyone who would gaze directly upon the swirling Shades sees the Necromancer as a black blotch in their vision that absorbs all light - resembling a localized spot of blindness more than a person - and is overcome with grief, increasing the penalty by [a bit].<br /> <br /> Additionally, the Necromancer counts as being invisible for enemies wishing to engage in combat.<br /> <br /> The cowl persists until it is exposed to light more intense than a bonfire (such as sunlight or a Solar's totemic anima flare), or direct contact with fire (at which point it burns as readily as dry paper. A Fire Dragonblood's anima flux counts.)<br /> <br /> <br /> Next:<br /> <br /> <b>Trumpet Blaring Denunciation</b><br /> OR<br /> <b>Author's choice</b> (including different takes on anything i've already written)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 02-13-2015, 02:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T16:45:07-07:00","id":441960,"title":"","content":"Over a month this has sat stagnant? This simply will not do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=377518#post377518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are No Innocents</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Solar Socialize</b><br /> <br /> This Charm supplements a Lawgiver's call for leniency or forgiveness of a crime, faux-pas or other infraction that has been committed by herself or by another. Should she appeal to a Major Intimacy among those she hopes to convince, using relevant hypothetical circumstances that might lead them or one they care for to commit the infraction themselves, those individuals may not &lt;insert some relevant social action&gt; and must pay an additional Willpower if attempting to resist it. Should she appeal to a similar incident in which one of her targets actually showed near to the same level of leniency or forgiveness as that requested, that target receives the same penalty and may not spend any Willpower at all to resist being persuaded.<br /> <br /> <u>New Charm:</u><br /> <b>Black Cat Erudition</b><br /> OR<br /> <b>Bell Tolls Thirteen</b><br /> OR<br /> <b>Blue Roses Under Heaven</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T07:20:22-07:00","id":447657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Black Cat Erudition</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunar Appearance, scene-long, somewhat-equivalent of Mastery of Small Manners<br /> <br /> The Lunar expresses supernatural assurance and volition in her body language, appearing to be so learned and noble as to be above rudeness and petty slights. Whenever the Lunar's actions would offend a character, that character convinces themselves that the Lunar's offence is meant as something greater - philosophical commentary, artistic expression, light-hearted parody or the like. This charm doesn't give any explicit control over the perceived meaning, though circumstances and context can definitely provide guidance.<br /> <br /> For example, spitting on an expensive tiger-peacock rug may be taken as a commentary on the extreme contrast between the host's exuberance and the poverty of the exploited peasants seen outside.<br /> <br /> (Not sure what mechanics this should have, but the possibility of the Lunar's charade being ousted should be included. It's no fun if they never realize that they've been played for fools.<br /> - He's not a philosophical genius, he's just been fucking with you!<br /> - HAW HAW! See ya! *flies away*)<br /> <br /> Next:<br /> <b>Twice-Dining Raptor Procession</b><br /> or<br /> <b>Paper Tiger Unfolding</b><br /> or<br /> <b>Blue Roses Under Heaven</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 03-18-2015, 10:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T14:22:54-07:00","id":448272,"title":"","content":"<b>Paper Tiger Unfolding</b><br /> <br /> Solar linguistic charm<br /> <br /> essence 3 Linguistics 4 - costs 4 essence - supplemental, combo ok<br /> <br /> <br /> All Solars are mighty. Their words are law. Even when penned, their words appear mighty and carry the force of their writer in such a way that they cannot be denied. If the solar is powerful enough, his written word cannot even be gainsaid.<br /> <br /> This charm allows the user to commit essence in order to make their written social attack undodgable. At essence 4 the charm's effect expands to also make such written attacks impossible to parry.<br /> <br /> Only the heretics who shield their eyes from the words and rightous messages of the Solars are safe","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T17:29:58-07:00","id":471875,"title":"","content":"Had to dig back a bit to avoid one I dug and did not suggest, but we're back!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ohSaucy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=350376#post350376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nihilistic Oblation Embargo</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Sidereal Medicine</b><br /> <br /> The Reckoners understand that the prayer and sacrifice of the living helps to feed the restless dead, and so may choose to sever these threads in several ways.<br /> <br /> By committing 5 motes, the Sidereal may trace an approximation of The Corpse constellation with a circle around it on the ground, at least two feet in diameter. Once complete, a violet flame runs along the constellation while another runs along the circle, until both flicker out. So long as these remain undisturbed, within [Essence] miles, all prayers and sacrifices devoted to ghosts are instead received by Heaven. The Sidereal also gains an Overdrive pool, which fills with 1 mote for each sacrifice valued at Resources 3 or greater, and per effective dot of the Cult Background it captures in prayer. Should she choose, the Sidereal may gain an intuitive understanding of the nature of these prayers and sacrifices (general location of its occurrence, contents and intended recipient, etc.). Ghosts who enter the area may detect the unnatural obstacle to mortal worship with a successful &lt;insert roll&gt; (and then sense its absence), but cannot precisely pinpoint its center or source.<br /> <br /> The Sidereal may instead choose to commit only 1 mote, setting her hand on or offering a prayer before a shrine, altar, or other such place of worship. This act leaves a small tracing of The Corpse on the place of worship -- visible only to Essence detection -- and targets only prayer and sacrifice facilitated through this place of worship. Any ghosts to whom this place of worship was erected or dedicated may detect the interference as above, with a one-die bonus on the roll. Such aware ghosts may detect the small tracing of The Corpse, even if they could not normally see or sense Essence. In all other respects -- including ending the effect by disturbing the tracing -- this barrier to worship functions like the original version.<br /> <br /> Lastly, the Sidereal may commit 3 motes when making contact with the ghost directly, etching its corpus with a tracing of The Corpse -- invisible as the place of worship version -- and capturing all worship it would otherwise receive. The affected spirit receives a three-die bonus on detection, and can remove it only with magic to dispel a curse or by venturing into the Labyrinth. In all other respects, this functions like the previous two versions.<br /> <br /> <u>New Charm:</u><br /> <b>Bells Toll Thirteen</b><br /> OR<br /> <b>Blue Roses Under Heaven</b><br /> OR<br /> <b>Kaleidoscopic Memory Auger</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T08:32:32-07:00","id":472821,"title":"","content":"<b>Kaleidoscopic Memory Auger</b><br /> Raksha Cup, 7m 1wp<br /> <br /> Upon Ravishing a target, the Raksha may make a Reflexive Shaping Action, regardless of timing constraints, in which she sets the scene according to one of her target's memories. A proper Stunt in this way robs the target of [its rating] Willpower points and converts them into points of Gossamer which can immediately be spent to activate Assumption or Mutation charms as long as they are congruent with the memory. If the target doesn't have enough remaining willpower, the remainder is converted from her Compassion channels. Any remainder after this is lost.<br /> <br /> Using this power with a Stunt rated at 2 points also allows the Raksha to Reflexively deactivate a single Assumption-type charm as though the Raksha was in the Wyld. A 3-point stunt allows the deactivation of any number of assumptions.<br /> <br /> Next:<br /> <b>Blue Roses Under Heaven</b><br /> OR<br /> <b>Salt and Poppies Bargain</b><br /> OR<br /> <b>Cloud-Cracking Clash</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T19:14:18-07:00","id":473651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=472821#post472821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Blue Roses Under Heaven</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Astrological effect, Performance<br /> <br /> With a song to the Venus, the Sidereal's anima banner takes on an azure brilliance (regardless of his caste), and he temporarily winks out of existence. Over the next scene a garden manifests in the area, whether erupting through the ground or simply shimmering into being. <br /> <br /> As long as he maintains this effect, the Sidereal exists as the garden itself, drawing lovers, artists, and dreamers to himself. He temporarily appears in his Resplendent Destiny to maintain the grounds, but the world and the visitors pay him no heed. While he spends time as a muse, the Exalt resists the efforts those who would investigate him, track him, or seek to do violence upon him or those who visit him. <br /> <br /> The difficulties implicit in existing as architecture, as well as inspiring those who attend him, are taxing duties: The Sidereal has only an hour a week to attend to his own affairs.<br /> <br /> NEXT:<br /> <br /> <b>Bottomless Sea Sorrows</b><br /> <br /> OR<br /> <br /> <b>Wicked Whisper Innoculation</b><br /> <br /> OR<br /> <br /> <b>Radiant Ecstasy Mask</b><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T12:05:50-07:00","id":476185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=473651#post473651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Wicked Whisper Innoculation</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Dragon-Blooded Integrity (Simple, Indefinite) <br /> <br /> Just as Meru resists any attempt move its foothills, the chosen of Pasiap resist attempts to undermine their beliefs. Upon activating this Charm, the Exalt chooses up to (Essence) Intimacies. For as long as the Charm remains active, she doubles her MDVs against any attempt to erode those Intimacies. <br /> <br /> Next up:<br /> <br /> <b>Hopes and Ambitions Vitrified</b><br /> <br /> OR<br /> <br /> <b>Champions-as-Chattel Pronouncement</b><br /> <br /> OR<br /> <br /> <b>Radiant Ecstacy Mask</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Playing 3e and miss Anathema? Try my web app, <a href=\"https://www.lotcastingatemi.com\" target=\"_blank\">Lot-Casting Atemi</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/553-hushnowquietnow","name":"hushnowquietnow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar553_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T01:30:00-07:00","id":476769,"title":"","content":"(Writing these for the stopgap system I've been using with my group to fake EX3. Makes me wonder how close my predictions are gonna come. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> HOPES AND AMBITIONS VITRIFIED (Sidereal Integrity, Reflexive)<br /> <br /> For those who understand that all things must come to an end, they also understand that some things are forever; others can be made so.<br /> If someone attempts to erode or appeal to one of the Chosen's intimacies with an influence attempt, the Sidereal may instead use this charm to form a crystalline tear &quot;containing&quot; their intimacy, separating it from themselves. The Exalt no longer feels the effects of that intimacy for as long as it is held in this glasslike structure; love turns to apathy, as does hate, he simply has removed that intensity of feeling from himself. If pressed to his temple, the gemstone melts and the intimacy returns to his personality at the same level of intensity it was before using this charm, although if the stone is destroyed the intimacy itself as well as the intense feelings associated with it are gone forever.<br /> <br /> If fashioned into a piece of jewelry and worn by someone other than the Maiden's Chosen, it instills in them the same intimacy contained inside for as long as it is worn.<br /> <br /> CHAMPIONS-AS-CHATTEL PRONOUNCEMENT (Gentimian Presence, Indefinite)<br /> <br /> The Fate-Lost know better than any other how jarring the loss of prestige and status can be, when replaced by the neverwhen.<br /> The Gentimian may use this charm to make a statement to all present, forcing a Presence+Manipulation Roll that must exceed their target's Resolve; each success adds one year and a day onto the duration. Each person affected by this charm is given a glimpse into a possible fate, for as long as the duration lasts, believe a person of high status, standing or respect selected by the Gentimian to be the opposite; in the minds of those affected, Kings become beggars, generals become cowards, and famed courtesans become common street-whores.<br /> <br /> STAR SHATTERING STRIKE<br /> <br /> OR<br /> <br /> UNHOLY CENTER OF WISDOM<br /> <br /> OR<br /> <br /> MASTER-FLIRTS-WITH-THE-BARMAID","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Need some Tunes for your Exalted Game? <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1071249-exalted-tunes\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...-exalted-tunes</a><br /> Want some help managing your PCs? <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/882498-new-anathema-character-management-anathema-reincarnated\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...a-reincarnated</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2442-arian-dynas","name":"Arian Dynas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T14:09:17-07:00","id":499375,"title":"","content":"Star-Shattering Strike<br /> (Infernal, Ophidian)<br /> The Infernal shreds Fate with her bare hands, tearing destiny asunder; for a year and a day, the target of the blow is free from all presumptions of himself and of Heaven: <br /> * He exists outside of Fate, unable to be predicted or affected by Sidereal astrology.<br /> * While his Virtues, Intimacies, and Motivation continue to exist, and he expresses them as he sees fit, they no longer compel him nor defend him. For the duration of this charm, such numinous attributes of his character are prone to fluctuate<br /> * The successful damage inflicted by the strike is treated as successes on a Disguise roll; those who knew him before may find his hazy nirvana renders him difficult to recognize.<br /> <br /> NEXT:<br /> Radiant Ecstasy Mask<br /> OR<br /> Master Flirts with the Barmaid<br /> OR<br /> Bells Toll Thirteen","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T15:48:39-07:00","id":499457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=499375#post499375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Radiant Ecstasy Mask</div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereal Socialize<br /> <br /> The sidereal chooses a target (which may be herself) whose strand she coats in the Essence of Venus for a time, rolling Manipulation + Socialize. Until this charm expires, any attempt to intuit, read or otherwise understand the target's emotions that doesn't beat this threshold reveals only ecstatic happiness, no matter what emotion the target wishes to convey. This effect is layered on top of the target's own efforts if she wishes to further conceal her feelings, leaving the investigator's leftover successes to contend with the target's own subterfuge.<br /> <br /> Next:<br /> <b>Lettuce Leaves Sprint</b><br /> Or<br /> <b>Bell Tolls Thirteen</b><br /> Or<br /> <b>Unfolded Reflections Trajectory</b><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T12:24:10-07:00","id":517237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=499457#post499457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Unfolded Reflections Trajectory</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Lunar Perception, variable cost<br /> <br /> Luna's light is unbound by geometric conventions. As the Lunar prepares for an attack, she can activate this charm to treat all reflections as straight lines to her target. Distance weapons are effortlessly reflected off such surfaces - even off of water. With [extra expenditure] the Lunar may launch a Melee or Martial Arts attack, directing it through the surface; This attack only has a chance to hit if the target is within appropriate range of their reflection.<br /> <br /> Next:<br /> <b>Confounding Dilemma Inflection</b><br /> Or<br /> <b>[Aspect]-Adorning Chakra</b><br /> Or<br /> <b>Ten Thousand Discoveries Spirit</b><br /> Or<br /> Author's Choice","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T16:26:43-07:00","id":528211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=517237#post517237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Ten Thousand Discoveries Spirit</b></div> </div> </div> </div><b>Lunar Intelligence</b><br /> <br /> The Lunar pursues all there is to know with a rare passion and drive, and grows invigorated by the act of finding. The character acquires an overdrive pool of ten motes, which can be filled only through great acts of discovery, such as in research on something particularly obscure, being one of the first in ages to set eyes on a place or thing, or ferreting out a very well-hidden secret. Each such discovery directly from someone else's research adds 2 motes to this pool, while those uncovered personally add 4.<br /> <br /> In addition to the usual uses for overdrive pools, these may also be spent on actions directly related to making a discovery (be it an Investigation roll, a Survival roll to reach somewhere remote, a Presence roll to intimidate out a secret, or a Stealth roll to spy on a conversation) or overcoming a direct obstacle to such (clearing a doorway to research materials, or Stealth to slip by a guard on the way to a prisoner who knows something).<br /> <br /> Normally, the character may make no more than one discovery per scene. The exception is when in the Wyld or some other chaotic or dreamlike realm: there, per scene, the character may receive the benefit for a number of discoveries about the place or its inhabitants equal to her Intelligence score. Wise raksha have learned the hard way to give such driven Lunars an especially wide berth.<br /> <br /> (Aaand in a system without overdrive, I guess... Hard to say, EX3 unseen, but I hear Willpower's harder to come by, so maybe that would do it?)<br /> (EDIT: Or, going with Fata-Ku's excellent suggestion, discoveries add to a pool of dice, which may be spent on a one-to-one basis to increase the die level of a character's stunt, including all other rewards (not counting XP for a 3-die stunt). This pool of dice cannot hold more than 10 dice at a time, and these dice cannot push a stunt beyond 3-dice. However, these dice may still be spent freely to enhance actions directly related to blah-diddy-blah)<br /> <br /> New Charm:<br /> <b>Bell Tolls Thirteen</b><br /> OR<br /> <b>Confounding Dilemma Inflection</b><br /> OR<br /> <b>Mile in Someone Else's Shoes Understanding</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":"caveat based on Fata-Ku's good idea. 05-27-2015, 03:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T08:12:24-07:00","id":529965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=528211#post528211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (Aaand in a system without overdrive, I guess... Hard to say, EX3 unseen, but I hear Willpower's harder to come by, so maybe that would do it?)<br /> <br /> New Charm:<br /> <b>Bell Tolls Thirteen</b></div> </div> </div> </div>(In the absence of overdrive, i suggest just a pool of dice, like the Raksha Style background)<br /> <br /> <b> Bell tolls thirteen </b><br /> <br /> Labyrinth circle necromancy<br /> <br /> The necromancer Shapes a sickly green-and-black necromantic circle that hangs in the air as though affixed to an invisible wall. A ritual mace made of bone, salt and chalcedony is then used to strike the circle (the necromancer needn't be the one to perform the strikes) which rings out in deafening tones, sending necrotic waves along the circle's plane for [Essence x 100] yards for one full turn after every strike.<br /> <br /> Anything (being, object or structure) that comes into contact with these waves suffers unsoakable damage equal to the striker's Strength + Weapon + Necromancer's Occult rating at least once and thereafter with every wave that it remains in contact. Buildings erode steadily under this effect and do not get the benefits of their natural Hardness.<br /> <br /> Anything slain or destroyed by this effect manifests at the adjacent point in the underworld as a grave good, effigy, structure or ghost, as appropriate, belonging to the necromancer, though it is possible to dedicate such destruction to another entity.<br /> <br /> On the thirteenth strike or at the crack of dawn (whichever comes sooner), the spell concludes, shattering the mace, releasing one final ear-shattering ring and dealing all cumulated damage to its wielder - this damage is a side-effect, not a cost, and can be readily soaked or redirected through other magic.<br /> <br /> New charm:<br /> Toxic Mannerisms Exhalation<br /> OR<br /> Confounding Dilemma Inflection<br /> OR<br /> Mile in Someone Else's Shoes Understanding","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T16:54:53-07:00","id":534950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=529965#post529965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New charm:<br /> Toxic Mannerisms Exhalation</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Eclipse (Presence)</b><br /> <br /> The Eclipse defuses tension in the room. With laughter, a swift jibe, or an airy wave of the hand, she dismisses an opponent's words- slightly influencing all Extras nearby to do the same. This Charm does not use unnatural mental influence and can be parried.<br /> <br /> New Charm: <i>Crouch of the </i><i>Laughing Tiger</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T06:43:24-07:00","id":535528,"title":"","content":"Chrouch of the Laughing Tiger - Lunar manip charm<br /> <br /> After defeating an opponent, but not outright said opponent, a lunar can humiliate her quarry with the scathing might of the laughing moon.<br /> <br /> By repeatedly crouching over her downed and helpless foe, the lunar gains +1 dice to all social interactions with individuals who have an intimacy towardss the downed foe: For those with positive intimacies its a +1 to manipulation rolls, and for negative intimatices its a +1 to charisma rolls.<br /> <br /> Next charm: Monkey Snatches Lowest Fruit","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T07:53:04-07:00","id":535579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>webkilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=535528#post535528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Next charm: Monkey Snatches Lowest Fruit</div> </div> </div> </div>Solar larceny<br /> As long as essence is committed to this charm the lawgiver can find enough unattended coin purses, chips of jade and trade fodder to make any number of resource 1 purchases.<br /> <br /> Next: Unstoppable Mask of the Conqueror Technique<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6228-canis-vulgaris","name":"Canis Vulgaris","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6228_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T04:40:16-07:00","id":536804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Canis Vulgaris</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=535579#post535579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Next: Unstoppable Mask of the Conqueror Technique</div> </div> </div> </div>Evocation of Permanence, an intricate faberg\u00e9-style Orichalcum and Soulsteel mask.<br /> <br /> The mask blares in a display of a setting sun in black chains and manifests a tyrannical visage or glory and violence on the Exalt's face which shines like a second sunset for [essence] miles. All who gaze the hues of this display instinctively know only this: an unstoppable juggernaut of conquest is coming.<br /> <br /> For the rest of the scene, anyone within the area who bears a positive intimacy towards the Exalt enjoys the benefits of being a fearless automaton. Additionally, all of the Exalt's actions that relate to warfare (e.g. commanding a unit, assembling an army etc.) get get 10-again (reroll 10s for additional successes). Enemies of the Exalt subtract any rolled 1s from their successes.<br /> <br /> Next:<br /> <b>Blink-step</b><br /> OR<br /> <b>Leaping Lightning Distraction</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 06-02-2015, 08:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T12:13:32-07:00","id":554661,"title":"","content":"<b>Leaping Lightning Distraction</b><br /> Air-aspect Dodge<br /> Type: Supplemental.<br /> <br /> Lightning courses through the air, transporting the Exalt in a blinding flash of elemental Essence. This charm supplements a Defend or a Defend Other action, allowing the Exalt to move up to their Dash range and use their Dodge DV in place of their Parry DV for the purpose of Defend Other as the flash of light and threat of electrocution dissuade the attacker. For the latter effect to work, the attacker must see the flash of lightning. Normally this charm is too quick to block out by simply shielding ones eyes, but surprise-negating charms or fore-knowledge of this charm's activation may allow a reflexive contest of Wits+Awareness vs. the Exat's Dex+Dodge.<br /> <br /> -------<br /> <br /> (set-up for the next one) Clever-Hands: Black wraps made of Chthonic Leather studded with Black Jade. (despite the name, they can be worn on any part of the body around which they can wrap. On the hands they count as smashfists, on the feet they count as god-kicking boots)<br /> <br /> Main effect: Clever-hands offers a pool of 5 successes that can be used to supplement any ability roll as long as the user isn't seen. These successes refill when the bearer successfully completes an action without any witnesses at a rate of 1 success per unsuspecting character within the same room or Essence x 10 yards (whichever is smaller). Extras do not count, and battle-groups count as a single character for this purpose.<br /> (further Evocations might extend this pool)<br /> <br /> <b>Blink-Step</b><br /> Evocation of Clever-Hands<br /> Cost: \u00af\\_(\u30c4)_/\u00af enough to curb abuse<br /> <br /> This evocation was discovered (developed?) by a Night-Caste investigator-spy who chose to wrap Clever-Hands around her shins and ankles.<br /> <br /> The world is taken aback by the subtelty of the user's movement, and all blink in unison in an attempt to understand. Using her movement action to activate this effect, the Exalt renders all opponents effectively blind for a single tick, long enough to perform an action - they are completely unable to open their eyes. This time goes unnoticed, and seems to be no longer than a normal blink.<br /> <br /> <br /> Next:<br /> Salamander's Coal Burrow<br /> or<br /> Impeccable Boredom Inscription<br /> or<br /> Battles Not Yet Lost Paradigm","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 06-14-2015, 03:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T14:40:53-07:00","id":554884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=554661#post554661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Salamander's Coal Burrow</div> </div> </div> </div>Dragon-Blooded, Fire Aspect Presence<br /> <br /> The warmth of Hesiesh fills the room with an ambient glow, causing all who witness the Dagon-Blooded's Anima to feel at ease. Those who spend at least ten minutes meditating or simply lounging in the presence of a Fire Aspects full Anima Bonfire gain the following benefits that last for the rest of the day:<br /> <br /> Wound penalties are reduced by 1, to a minimum of -1.<br /> <br /> Penalties to MDV from stress or hardship are removed.<br /> <br /> Characters heal one -0 Health level.<br /> <br /> At Essence X, the Dragon-Blooded may meditate on the lessons of Fire and apply these benefits to themselves.<br /> <br /> (Mechanics are probably poor, but fire as a source of comfort and wellbeing is intriguing to me)<br /> <br /> <br /> Next:<br /> Pearlescent Anima Nova<br /> or<br /> Rainbow of a Thousand Jewels<br /> or<br /> Thirteen Gardian Ghosts Stance","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T10:37:30-07:00","id":582484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=554884#post554884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pearlescent Anima Nova</div> </div> </div> </div>Dragonblooded Integrity<br /> 5m 1wp<br /> elemental, Emotion, Shaping<br /> <br /> As water and wind steadily eat away stone and bark to leave behind only smooth flowing edges, so too the children of the Dragons erode their own social bindings.<br /> This charm allows the Dragonblood to direct her Anima Flux to erode Intimacies. For the rest of the scene her anima flux instead erodes intimacies that other characters hold towards the exalt or that the exalt holds towards other characters, with each damage success instead applying a level of intimacy erosion. The Exalt chooses whether this power erodes positive or negative intimacies during this charm's activation, and may not choose both. For every character in range, each level of erosion only applies to one appropriate intimacy chosen at random or by the storyteller.<br /> <br /> At storyteller's discretion, this charm may be used to do away with other forms of social or mental obligation, such as social backgrounds or mental merits. This charm can be comboed with other effects that extend the Exalt's elemental influence, such as [that war charm that creates a fire tornado]. At essence 5+ this charm can erode Wyld Mutations at a rate of one point for every 3 successes.<br /> <br /> Next:<br /> <b>Unfolding Nightmare Sequence</b><br /> or<br /> <b>Rainbow of a Thousand Jewels</b><br /> or<br /> <b>Thirteen Gardian Ghosts Stance</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T03:52:58-07:00","id":609245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=582484#post582484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Unfolding Nightmare Sequence</b></div> </div> </div> </div><b>Abyssal Investigation</b><br /> The deathknight weeps black smoke at the site of a recent murder or other tragic crime. The events of the crime manifest in the smoke, jittery and dreamlike, granting useful insight to herself and a derangement to those around her; later, when she pronounces guilt, they may rid themselves of the derangement by taking justice into their own hands.<br /> <br /> Next: <b>Ride the Whirlwind</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T04:40:09-07:00","id":609256,"title":"","content":"What the hell, all is quiet on the Western Front.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=609245#post609245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Ride the Whirlwind</b></div> </div> </div> </div>This says Dragon-Blood to me, but that's boring. Sooooo<br /> <br /> <b>Sidereal Ride</b><br /> 5m, 1 wp<br /> <br /> The Chosen of Journeys, when pressed, may force all paths to collapse so they may end their travel. This Charm supplements an action to reach a given location. The Sidereal must already be on the journey when he invokes this Charm. Circumstances conspire to allow him to arrive at that location much faster, but a truly amazing and circuitous set of happenings allows it. For example, if the Sidereal desires to cross &quot;to the other side of town,&quot; then a building might partially collapse on cart, causing it to see-saw violently upward, propelling the Chosen into the air. Then he might fall into the local aqueduct, which sluices him across most of the town, only to drop him into a fountain. When he steps out, some cows in the market stampede, pushing a set of barrels in front of him, that he then rights out of town.<br /> <br /> As Fate conspires to aid the Sidereal, other paths and journeys are delayed. For this reason, this Charm may only be used once in a given area per scene. Further, it is Obvious to any other Chosen of the Maidens that this Charm was used.<br /> <br /> The travel time for the Sidereal is reduced by a factor of (Essence+Ride). if any other Ability rolls are required (such as the Sidereal riding a horse, or piloting a ship), all difficulty penalties are negated. if this Charm is used to run away from an encounter, apply (Essence) automatic successes to any contested rolls.<br /> <br /> <br /> Next: Auspicious Conclusive Time Marking Meditation ( <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RIkajmoNr5I\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RIkajmoNr5I</a> )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T05:51:08-07:00","id":609292,"title":"","content":"Auspicious Conclusive Time Marking Meditation<br /> <b>Type: </b>Lunar<br /> <b>Attribute:</b> Perception<br /> Time, like all linear things of Creation, begins to break down upon exposure to the Wyld. By spending 2m, a Lunar traveling in the Middlemarches or Deep Wyld can can create a small bubble of quicksilver essence the size of a small hut. This bubble perfectly reflects the current season and time of day in Creation, including phenomena such as eclipses and Calibration. This temporally linear bubble will only last for one hour of Creation-time before dissipating into the madness of the Wyld, but the Lunar who invoked this charm can invest an additional 1m/hr to keep the bubble intact against the ravages of atemporal madness outside.<br /> <br /> <b>Silver-and-Gold Attunement Matrix</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6872-kallipolis","name":"Kallipolis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T12:46:33-07:00","id":609847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kallipolis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=609292#post609292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Silver-and-Gold Attunement Matrix</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Fairfolk Heart<br /> <br /> The Noble Raksha has experienced the powerful stories of the chosen of the Sun and Moon, and were shaken, and were awed. Their hated enemy had shown them what possibilities they lacked; yet impossibility is nothing to the tides of chaos. Using this power while touching a Solar or Lunar exalt, one of the fair folk can forge a mutation of passion deep within themselves which inexorably ties them to Creation and to that chosen, replicating (though not replacing) the bond that Solars and Lunars share in a limited capacity - this new bond only goes one way, the chosen exalt is in no way affected.<br /> <br /> In addition to the effects of Solar Bond, the Raksha becomes immune to calcification as long as they directly interact with or touch their chosen exalt (whether beneficially or antagonistically). At the end of any such scene, the Raksha may gain points of Gossamer equal to her highest stunt as long as that stunt interacted with their chosen exalt in some way.<br /> <br /> Lastly, the Raksha gains the ability to awaken Adamant-level evocations in artifacts made of magical materials that correspond to their chosen exalt's bond-mate. (i.e. choosing a Lunar allows the fairfolk to awaken adamant evocation in Orichalcum artifacts; choosing a Solar allows the same for Moonsilver Artifacts).<br /> <br /> Next: <b>Destiny-Sabotaging Riddle</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T13:52:46-07:00","id":609900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=609847#post609847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Destiny-Sabotaging Riddle</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Qaf Charm<br /> <br /> Speaking a strange koan, the Exalt gives the target a preoccupying question. In addition to inflicting a -1 internal penalty to non-reflexive actions, the character exists outside of Fate until she can answer this intellectual burden.<br /> <br /> This anomaly is something the Loom of Fate tries to address; curious omens and strange portents in the guise of bizarre coincidences are drawn to the target of this charm, all of them having relevance to the Infernal's question, but the target of the charm suffers an increased penalty \u2013 up to the Exalt's Essence \u2013 to notice them, let alone register their meaning.<br /> <br /> Next: Solemnities of the Iron Word<br /> OR<br /> Gaoler's Book of Secrets","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T05:57:55-07:00","id":610711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=609900#post609900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Next: Solemnities of the Iron Word</div> </div> </div> </div>Elloge charm.<br /> <br /> The Exalt, standing amidst the seas of Chaos, speaks the name of what she desires, and the Wyld separates into that which was named. Something so created is metaphysically iron, for so long as it continues to exist, which is so long as the Exalt commits a number of motes equal to the Resource value of that which was created (minimum of one). However, for that same duration, the Exalt cannot use, by speech or by writing, the word she spoke in the act of creation, for that word is no longer within her.<br /> <br /> Next:<br /> Celestial Headdress Inversion","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />If you want to play Thomas Edison, you'd better be up to the task of carrying all of civilization through the Renaissance and Industrial Revolution, <i>while the Sidereals and Dragon-Blooded are shooting at you</i>.","edited":{"userid":591,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/591-jorlem","user":"Jorlem","date":". 08-01-2015, 09:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/591-jorlem","name":"Jorlem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar591_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T10:15:37-07:00","id":611000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jorlem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=610711#post610711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Celestial Headdress Inversion</div> </div> </div> </div>Getimian Socialize<br /> <br /> The plans of heaven are vile, oligarchic chains upon the masses. Using this charm, a Getimian can liberate the unwitting slaves, and even turn them against their puppeteers.<br /> The getimian designates a target (which may be an individual or a group), relinquishing one on his own Pattern Spiders per point of Magnitude (to a minimum of 1). These spiders tend to the looms of the targets, interfering with Heaven's (and any other creature capable of altering Fate) plans.<br /> <br /> Whenever the target is subject to a Shaping or Astrology effect, the source of the effect gains points of Paradox for every die landing a 1 in their rolls, even if they are not normally capable of gaining Paradox.<br /> <br /> Fueling this charm with the Getimian's Yin pool allows the group to treat its own 1s as successes as long as their actions directly or indirectly go against any Fate*, Shaping or Sidereal Astrology beset upon them.<br /> <br /> Fuelling this charm with the Getimian's Yang pool allows the group to benefit from the positive effects of Fate, Shaping and Astrology as though they always met the appropriate conditions.<br /> <br /> * this includes non-mechanically-enforced decisions made by the bureau of destiny.<br /> <br /> Next: <b>Murder of Owls Congregation</b> or <b>Codex of Eyes and Lips</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T15:36:08-07:00","id":611417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=611000#post611000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Codex of Eyes and Lips</b></div> </div> </div> </div><b>Celestial Circle Sorcery Spell</b><br /> <br /> Fashioned by a Sorcerer with a greater fondness for books than for people, this spell allows one to turn pieces of another's body into a record of all they learned. When cast, a faintly glowing circle inscribes itself on the ground or floor nearby. Into this, the Sorcerer then sets body parts from one with knowledge she seeks, and then concludes the spell. The circle and the matter placed within it vanish, and create a tome, a Codex of Eyes and Lips. Within is knowledge appropriate to the experiences of the body parts used. This takes the form of a firsthand account of all of the individual's experiences as though the individual had written them, and in whatever language the individual would have chosen. This is instead in a language the Sorcerer knows if the individual was unable to read, write, or even communicate in an easily understood manner. Regardless of whether one knows the language, a reader is aware of a deeper truth to be reached with focus. Doing so allows the reader to perfectly experience the scene exactly as the individual once did, seeing through their eyes, knowing the words they spoke, and feeling any tactile sensation, as appropriate to the body part.<br /> <br /> These words and experiences are limited to what the parts chosen could have experienced. Most obviously, eyes will give vision and lips will give the individual's words (as well as any tastes), but without ears, there will be no sound. Sorcerers with much obsession or caution, and little compassion, may prefer not to worry about missing subtle details (such as a smell, or a bit of pain, pleasure, or textural information) and instead choose to sacrifice the individual. So long as the body dies within the circle, it will vanish and its complete experiences will be recorded.<br /> <br /> As an alternative, a Sorcerer may instead inflict damage equal to 1L to a chosen piece of the body, though this will provide only about a scene's worth of time. If the Sorcerer knows what she seeks when she removes this piece and it exists to be found, she receives her wish. If her request is impossible or she makes no such request, the individual may choose the account or it will instead default to an experience prominent in the individual's mind at the time. This prominent memory is often of the painful injury just received, so Sorcerers tend to be careful about this.<br /> <br /> The book is surprisingly well laid out and makes its information intuitively simple to find, though some poring over it may be needed. The words can be transcribed, and remain as perfectly accurate as the written word can be, but the copy will lack the mystical experiential option. These experiences are only possible through the flesh, blood, and bone used to create the tome, traces of which can be found all throughout its leather, ink, and pages.<br /> <br /> <u>NEXT:</u><br /> <b>Shackles of the Beast</b><br /> OR<br /> <b>Rising Star Crescendo</b><br /> OR<br /> <b>Field of Poppied Hopes</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T16:00:43-07:00","id":611425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=611417#post611417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Field of Poppied Hopes</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Celestial Circle Sorcery<br /> <br /> Those of weak will caught within this sorcerer's blinding anima find themselves in a field of the most beautiful flowers. Sniffing a one of these flowers provides the character with a glimpse into their own heart, their own desires stripped of all pretense. This either frees them from mundane and magical distractions that stand in the way of these hopes, or paralyze them with fear as their are confronted with their darkest lusts.<br /> <br /> <u>NEXT:</u> <b>Lounging Demon-Emperor Decadence</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/899-the-free-man","name":"The Free Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar899_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T18:27:02-07:00","id":611563,"title":"","content":"I'll have to be boring and obvious, I fear.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Free Man</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=611425#post611425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Lounging Demon-Emperor Decadence</b></div> </div> </div> </div><b>Infernal Survival</b><br /> The Infernal constructs a shelter by mundane means, and the monster in her Essence settles in. Simple wood turns to brass and bone; cloth or leaves becomes rich black silk; the bare earth splits to vomit soft petals of a pleasant spicy scent.<br /> Inside this palatial hovel, certain of her other Survival Charms are reduced in cost or extended in duration, allowing her to rest securely and eat well. Any guests, wanted or otherwise, suffer a minor derangement if they assault the resting Exalt.<br /> If she leaves her shelter for any length of time, it crumbles into verdigris and tatters, becoming mundane again.<br /> <br /> NEXT: <b>Ousted Sultan Smiles</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":97,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","user":"The MG","date":". 08-01-2015, 09:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T10:47:52-07:00","id":615293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=611563#post611563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Ousted Sultan Smiles</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Lunar Manipulation<br /> Duration: One full Lunar Cycle.<br /> <br /> When someone reveals the Lunar's nature or intentions (examples include outing them as a shapeshifter, revealing the Lunar's dishonesty or unmasking the Lunar's disguise), the Lunar may commit motes to this charm to slip a sliver of their essence into the target's mind. While this charm is in effect, the Lunar may use their Manipulation excellency to supplement the target's social rolls to appear like a righteous hero castignating a foul villain.<br /> <br /> The target of this charm always counts as a valid target for intention-reading and sense-riding Charms, such as Sense-Borrowing Method or Predator is Prey Mirror, despite any range considerations (such as touch or line of sight). At ST discretion, other dramatically appropriate charms may share this benefit, such as charms that affect dreams or inflict hallucinations.<br /> <br /> Next: <b>(Element) Kirin Expression</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T06:47:39-07:00","id":642919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=615293#post615293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Next: <b>(Element) Kirin Expression</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Dragon-Blooded Ride. Prerequisites: Dance of the Jade Bridle, Elemental Halo's Mercy. The Princes of the Earth are attended by fantastic elemental beasts, scaled water-horses, lightning hawks and fiery-maned simhata. This Charm targets a familiar suitable for riding. The creature is permanently made immune to its masters anima as per Elemental Halo's Mercy, enjoys the benefits of its master's anima effect (but not anima flux), and gains 10 points of mutations as it warps into a legendary beast. Its physical Attributes each increase by one and it can heal and soak lethal damage as a supernatural being. However, it remains a suitable target for all of the Dragon-Bloods Ride Charms, regardless of keyword limitations.<br /> <br /> Next:<br /> <b>Blinded Eye Panopticon</b><br /> Or: <br /> <b>Five Seasons of the Dragon</b><br /> Or: <br /> <b>A Winner At The Game of Life</b><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":2093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","user":"Crumplepunch","date":". 08-28-2015, 11:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T09:05:29-07:00","id":643034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=642919#post642919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Blinded Eye Panopticon</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Alchemical Municipal Charm<br /> <br /> There are those who cannot be allowed to roam free in Autochthonia, yet cannot be destroyed--whether as a matter of practicality or literal immortality. Fortunately, the Great Maker has an answer.<br /> <br /> Taking the shape of a foreboding yet sleek soulsteel tower, the Panopticon is a scant five meters in diameter; while few can claim to have seen the inside, the glimpses from when these prisons open up suggest that the charm is capable of folding space upon itself to greatly expand its carrying capacity.<br /> <br /> Prisoners kept inside the Panopticon are rapidly sedated, and the structure extends a Personality Override Spike into their nervous system before connecting them to other structures to maintain their relative health. Each point of Magnitude within the Panopticon requires an additional mote of Essence be committed to its activation.<br /> <br /> While captive, prisoners will continue to dream as normal; the Metropolis with this charm installed may use Personality Override Spike or any of its expansions upon them while they do so.<br /> <br /> Next:<br /> <b>Skein-of-Thoughts Tapestry</b><br /> OR<br /> <b>Sky-Darkening Sorrow</b><br /> OR<br /> <b>Five Seasons of the Dragon</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T10:25:29-07:00","id":643161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=643034#post643034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Sky-Darkening Sorrow</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Abyssal Performance Charm (or Void Circle Necromancy Spell, maybe?)<br /> <br /> Drawing the Essence of loss, deep into her chest, the Abyssal lets loose a few keening notes, piercing through all who here it, and vomits forth an unnatural darkness to blot out the Sun, Moon, and Stars. This umbra is corrosive, and erodes the flesh of any whose essence is not aspect to the Underworld.<br /> <br /> Next:<br /> <b>Five Seasons of the Dragon</b><br /> OR<br /> <b>Cascading Hell-Lotus</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/58-lokisenna","name":"Lokisenna","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T14:31:18-07:00","id":653033,"title":"","content":"<b>Five Seasons of the Dragon</b><br /> Dragonblooded Survival charm<br /> Enhances the previous [Element] Dragon Season (which allowed the Exalt to alter the weather, pulling away from or pushing it closer to its element)<br /> Allows the Exalt to call upon the Five Dragons of the Seasons, causing a regional weather change according to ANY element. This might make the weather gods become very angry with the Exalt.<br /> <br /> <b>Cascading Hell-Lotus</b><br /> Infernal Martial Arts Charm from the Abominable Soul Vortex Style<br /> Allows the Infernal to cast forth her Soul Vortex, causing all within [radius] yards to manifest their Anima Banner by burning the required number of motes. During Essence rounds, all Exalts present are required to burn this number of motes. They may use them to power Charms in the following rounds, but are not required to.<br /> <br /> <b>Delightful Shards of Dance</b><br /> AND/OR<br /> <b>Ecstasy Within the Ranks</b><br /> AND/OR<br /> <b>Moon and Sun Forge</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7661-segmarian","name":"Segmarian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T14:44:51-07:00","id":653039,"title":"","content":"<b>Delightful Shards of Dance</b><br /> Solar Performance<br /> Keywords: Illusion, Obvious, Combo-OK, other stuff<br /> Prerequisite: Phantom-Conjuring Performance<br /> <br /> For each (cost) paid when activating this Charm, the Solar projects a shining copy of himself from his anima, up to (Essence) copies. These golden phantasms repeat and/or accompany his motions and words with perfect choreography as the Exalt enacts a dance, chant, or musical or theatrical performance. Their actions and words need not be the same as the Solar's own, but all of the copies will enact the same role as each other. For each copy, add (bonus) to any effects this performance produces, other than unnatural mental influence. For (bigger cost) the Exalt may also enhance an unnatural mental influence effect of his performance by (smaller bonus).<br /> <br /> (Spontaneous musical number! Make your own chorus from nowhere out of shininess!)<br /> <br /> Next:<br /> <b>Skein-of-Thoughts Tapestry</b><br /> OR<br /> <b>Ecstasy Within the Ranks</b><br /> OR<br /> <b>Moon and Sun Forge</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 09-05-2015, 05:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T17:01:14-07:00","id":658642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=653039#post653039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Ecstasy Within the Ranks</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Celestial Circle Sorcery<br /> <br /> With open arms, the sorcerer makes the Mudra of Unrestrained Serenity over an area. A warm, skin-toned mist rolls out of the caster's robes and onto the area, lingering and heavily obscuring terrain until dispersed by wind. Though it may move with air currents, it remains contiguous for at least a scene.<br /> <br /> Within, living creatures see shapely silhouettes, hear sounds of passion and smell odors of ecstasy. Before every action, units caught in the area roll for rout at an increasing difficulty. Failure indicates combatants leaving the unit to indulge in primal pleasures with what they believe to be subjects of their desire. Only once the mists pass to they realize that what felt like warm caresses and inviting shapes were, in reality, tree stumps, rocks and the occasional cactus.<br /> <br /> Gods, Demons, Fairfolk and Elementals related to passions or pleasures revel when this spell is cast, as it gives them both a banquet and a show.<br /> <br /> <br /> Next:<br /> <b>Courage-Consuming Conflagration</b><br /> OR<br /> <b>Skein-of-Thoughts Tapestry</b><br /> OR<br /> <b>Moon and Sun Forge</b><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T19:15:19-07:00","id":658776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=658642#post658642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Courage-Consuming Conflagration</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Dragon-Blooded Presence, prerequisites Glowing Coal Radiance, Passion Transmuting Nuance. The Terrestrial inflicts an Emotion effect of fear on an enemy, inflicting penalties to attack. Used against the leader of a group of extras, this Charm can force a rout check.<br /> <br /> <b>Casting the World's Shadow</b><br /> OR<br /> <b>Chasing the Fading Ember</b><br /> OR<br /> <b>Skein-of-Thoughts Tapestry</b><br /> OR<br /> <b>Moon and Sun Forge</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T20:23:32-07:00","id":658855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=658776#post658776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Chasing the Fading Ember</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Solar Awareness:<br /> <br /> The Chosen of the Sun always find their target, even as they try to hide in the shadows. This charm allows the Solar to perfectly track an enemy in the dark as long as they got at least a glimpse of them in light, be it a candle or torch. Even if the light disappears, the Solar still sees the target as a glowing outline of Essence.<br /> <br /> <b>Perverse Propaganda Technique</b><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T19:59:09-07:00","id":662591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=658855#post658855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Perverse Propaganda Technique</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Solar Linguistics<br /> <br /> The Solar Storyteller spins a yarn so compelling and widespread that any facts that do not fit its narrative are pushed out of the public's consciousness. The Solar's player picks up to [Essence] Facts that define the narrative, rolls Manipulation + Linguistics and records the result. A Fact can be almost any statement, such as &quot;The Fairfolk just want hugs&quot;, &quot;The cold is a hoax&quot;, &quot;Mountains aren't real&quot; or &quot;The Dragonblooded are nothing more than mortals in fancy get-ups&quot;.<br /> <br /> Whenever the Solar interacts with a character as part of this campaign and that character's Parry DV is less than the Solar's recorded successes, the Solar can treat that character as having internalized those Facts as though they were intimacies. Actions the character performs that support or are supported by the Facts are treated as ordinary or even heroic, even when they would otherwise be scandalous or downright callous.<br /> <br /> Next:<br /> <b>Seven-Fingered Accusing Palm Atemi</b><br /> or<br /> <b>Nine Faces Deception</b><br /> or<br /> <b>Thirteen Murders' Parliament</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-11T08:57:20-07:00","id":697315,"title":"","content":"<b>Nine Faces Deception</b><br /> <br /> Solar Larceny - Reflexive<br /> <br /> some motes (+1wp the first time it's used in a scene)<br /> <br /> The Solar's identity doesn't exist if there's no one there to see it, their art of disguise honed to such perfection that personas can be applied instantly and reflexively. When no eyes are on the Solar - when alone, in darkness or during the blink of an eye - the Solar can instantly perform a dramatic Disguise action that's worth an hour of preparation. This charm doesn't give the solar automatic knowledge that they're being observed, rather the solar is aware of opportunities to activate this charm once they've decided to use it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Casting the World's Shadow</b><br /> Or<br /> <b>Skein-of-Thoughts Tapestry</b><br /> Or<br /> <b>Moon and Sun Forge</b><br /> Or<br /> <b>Seven-Fingered Accusing Palm Atemi</b><br /> Or<br /> <b>Thirteen Murders' Parliament</b> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-11T09:16:38-07:00","id":697342,"title":"","content":"<b>Thirteen Murders' Parliament</b><br /> <br /> Abyssal Investigation. Upon slaying a fellow sentient being, a pale reflection of the victim's Essence is imprinted into the Abyssal's anima. These shades are not truly ghosts and have no substance beyond the Abyssal's Essence and are visible and audible only to the Abyssal and each other. Their memories of their former lives are fragmentary at best, but whatever skills they had in life remain as sharp as ever. They will serve and advise the Abyssal as best they can as though they are ghosts bound with a Summon Ghost spell.<br /> <br /> I think there are enough Charm name suggestions unresolved for us to be getting on with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":2093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","user":"Crumplepunch","date":". 10-11-2015, 12:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T01:49:44-08:00","id":774616,"title":"","content":"Well, 3e is out now, so lets get this show on the road again!<br /> <br /> Infernal Stealth, Ebon Dragon<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Casting the World's Shadow</b></span></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 12m; <b>Mins:</b> Stealth 5, Essence 3<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Mute<br /> <b>Duration:</b> One Scene<br /> <b>Prequisite Charms:</b> Spreading Ink-Black Wings<br /> Light seems to fade at the Warlock's presence, shadows stretch into long, unnatural shapes and grow black as ink. The Infernal is at home within these shadows and gain the following benefits.<br /> She may hide in one of these shadows, gaining one automatic succes to her Stealth Roll when she does so. She can hide in the shadow of any object that is at least her size, she can not, however, hide in her own shadow. As long as she remains within these shadows, she may perform rush actions as long as she and the person she is rushing are both located within the same shadow.<br /> <br /> Ebby seems like the type who likes using shadows. So he has Charms that lets him make his own<br /> <br /> <b>Omnidirectional Defense Protocol<br /> <br /> Evading Lightning Declaration<br /> <br /> Altar-Shattering Strike</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T10:46:29-08:00","id":774905,"title":"","content":"Solar hero style charm<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Altar-Shattering Strike</b></span></span></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5m; <b>Mins:</b> Martial Arts 5, Essence 4<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Combo-ok, enhanced<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prequisite Charms:</b> Heaven Thunder Hammer, Hammer on Iron Technique<br /> <br /> During the primordial many gods and spirits betrayed Creation. The Solars punished them greatly, especially when they found their cults and covens. After the primordial war this charm was used to break up and discourage ancestor cults that worshiped ghosts, as it was often seen as blasphemy to the heavenly circle of reincarnation.<br /> <br /> This charm, when used with an unarmed attack that hits the sanctified alter of a god, doesn't just break the alter as if struck by Sledgehammer Fist Blow, but through the strands of fate and essence that bind an altar to a god, the attack also hits that very god - though not in a form enhanced by Sledgehammer Fist Blow, that only applies to the physical altar.<br /> <br /> Any altar struck, be it a giant solid stone block, or a delicate arrangement of demonic crystals, will break and lose its connection to the god, spirit, demon, ghost or whatnot being worshiped, so only a single blow can be sent through to the target of such worship. Wise Solars made sure their fury felt in such situations.<br /> <br /> To qualify as an altar, an object has to have been consecrated by by a proper priest or shaman (ST approval required) - Zenith Caste Solars can in this way consecrate altars to the UCS, but using this charm to strike the Most High... well, there is no record of it <b>[Records expunged by orders of the Maiden of Battles and Maiden of Endings, and the Unconquered Sun]</b><br /> <br /> <br /> New charm names:<br /> <br /> <br /> Lily reaches to the sky<br /> <br /> Peony spreads its leaves<br /> <br /> Shade of flowering vines","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":588,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","user":"webkilla","date":". 11-26-2015, 03:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T19:34:47-08:00","id":778761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>webkilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=774905#post774905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Peony spreads its leaves</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Solar Melee<br /> Permanent (Withering only) ; Melee 4, Essence 2<br /> <br /> When activating Peony Blossom Technique, the player may spend 3* Initiative to have her Anima lash out in a wave of blades or shards of blazing obscidian against all targets within close range. The attack is rolled once and is applied against the defence of all applicable targets. The Solar only gains initiative from the last damage roll of this attack.<br /> <br /> *not sure if this is an appropriate cost<br /> <br /> Next:<br /> <b>Evading Lightning Declaration</b><br /> or<br /> <b>Lies and Half-Truth Snare</b><br /> or<br /> <b>Omen Cipher Methodology</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T14:02:15-08:00","id":1052754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>webkilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=774905#post774905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Shade of Flowering Vines</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Terrestrial Survival Charm.<br /> <br /> Flooding an area with Wood Essence, one of the Dragon Blooded makes her surroundings more hospitable. Spending a scene in meditation, the Terrestrial's Essence calls forth vegetation that forms a loose shelter out to Medium range, flowering and fruiting in minutes. Within this canopy, the Exalt is protected from the general climate, and may make rolls to forage for food at simple difficulty. She does not have the same immunity to acute environmental hazards such as storms, but this charm grants an extra die to cope with these or any other Survival rolls she may make while abiding in her shelter.<br /> <br /> Next:<br /> <b>Evading Lightning Declaration</b><br /> or<br /> <b>Skein-of-Thoughts Tapestry</b><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T14:49:17-08:00","id":1052795,"title":"","content":"Evading Lightning Declaration: Terrestrial Bureaucracy, Air.<br /> Dragons do not fear greater dragons... just... healthily respect the problematic consequences of their wrath. This creates a dramatic action in which the Terrestrial espouses their and/or their organization's innocence, rightness of action, and blamelessness in the face of a mishap or other problem that would risk their superiors' wrath.<br /> <br /> I submit the name...<br /> Twenty-Three Counterfeit Daiklaves Attitude.<br /> (If you get what obscure, dumb little thing that's a reference to, you get a Slim Jim.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T11:29:34-08:00","id":1053340,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#008080\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Twenty-Three Counterfeit Dailklaives Attitude</b></span></span></span></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 6m; <b>Mins:</b> Larceny 5, Essence 3<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Combo-ok, illusion, compulsion<br /> <b>Duration:</b> action<br /> <b>Prequisite Charms:</b> [something that makes sense]<br /> <br /> A key element of larceny is deception. Of course, deception doesn't always mean staying hidden - sometimes it means being at the center of attention, unwanted or not. When everyone is looking, it is sometime wisest to not be seen holding what they're looking for, even if it means that they think less of you, as that can be key to returning to the shadows.<br /> <br /> This charm, which was also known in the First Age as &quot;Brightest Light Hides Many Shadows&quot;, creates an illusion effect around the Solar focused on a specific handheld item currently carried. This can be a gleaming daiklaive, or a very heavy stack of jade talents, someone you just kidnapped, or that glass of celestial wine you weren't supposed to take. The effect of the charm causes the Solar to appear as if only being in the possention of something... else - something random, but inconsequential. A stolen piece of jade jewelry? No, that's just a cheap glass knock-off.<br /> <br /> If this charm is used when stealing something, any onlookers will get the impression that it was a fake duplicate that has been stolen, and they will rest assured that the thief is a fool... at least until they're proven wrong the hard way.<br /> <br /> To use the charm, the Solar rolls Manip+Larceny, with her permanent essence score in extra successes. Anyone seeing or otherwise perceiving the Solar steal something, or carry something that the Solar doesn't want you to see, for that action, will not become suspicious or raise the alarm. This compulsion to think so lasts the rest of the scene, but the charm only yields this effect for the duration of a single action.<br /> <br /> It should be noted that this charm specifically works even when someone is looking for something specific, and thus cannot be fooled by simpler charms that require people be unaware of you to begin with, though it might lead to later social faux pas when it becomes heard that a master thief was spotted having stolen a whore's stained rags instead of the Scarlet Empress's evening gown.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The next name on the chopping sword:<br /> <br /> 1) Flowers speak of water and rain<br /> 2) Bloodstar<br /> 3) Flaying the puke wolf","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T13:16:00-08:00","id":1053388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>webkilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=1053340#post1053340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[1) Flowers speak of water and rain</div> </div> </div> </div>Dragon-Blooded Sail, but a Wood Aspected Charm.<br /> The Dragon knows when it's time to sail, and when it's time to seek shelter.<br /> Using this charm requires the Dragon-blooded to be in a place with at least some amount of plant life, as adjudicated by the ST.<br /> Upon using it, she gains knowledge of the next 24 hours of weather, but only if it's not being influenced magically.<br /> In addition, she gains half her sail in bonus dice on all Survival actions to seek shelter.<br /> <br /> Let's see... <br /> \u2022 Feed the Machine<br /> \u2022 Your Fate is Thrice Sealed.<br /> \u2022 Battlefields Like Gameboards","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8097-wern212","name":"wern212","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8097_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T14:05:17-08:00","id":1053411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wern212</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=1053388#post1053388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022 Battlefields Like Gameboards</div> </div> </div> </div>Dragonblooded War charm, Earth aspected<br /> 6m 1WP, Indefinite<br /> The exalt draws the battlefield and all units into the dirt or sand, and in doing so codifies the rules of the game. Any battlegroup or individual combatant he can see, draws and who is on the ground (or a mount that is) becames known to the exalt in great detail. He becomes fully aware of the strength of their bravery and loyalty, their weapons and ammunition stocks, standing orders and most practiced tactics. Upon completion of the drawing, the exalt may make a Wits+War roll with automatic successes equal to his essence to detect and reveal any battlegroups or combatants concealed or hidden within the drawn battlefield. Such units will be added to the drawn gameboard automatically. He and any unit he commands cannot be surprised by mundane means by any battlegroups or combatants drawn onto the game board for the duration of the charm. Individual combatants may still use any stealth magic they might have access to after they are drawn onto the board.<br /> The drawn game board will endure mundane weather effects, but magical erosion or any deliberate attempt to stomp it out by a sentient being automatically destroys the drawing and ends the charm prematurely.<br /> <br /> <br /> New charm ideas:<br /> - Gravesoil's comfort method<br /> - Mountain slaying impact Prana<br /> - Twice forgotten secrets Technique<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I thank the Devs for the great game of Exalted!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12735-bjornthefellhanded","name":"BjornTheFellhanded","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12735_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"327"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T01:00:50-08:00","id":1053688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BjornTheFellhanded</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=1053411#post1053411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Gravesoil's comfort method</div> </div> </div> </div>Abyssal Presence Charm<br /> The Deathknight must sometimes create a facade that they care about the living. This charm aids in such attempts.<br /> This charm increases the Deathknights appearance by one. In addition, while the charm is active, the Abyssal loses the Hideous Merit, if she has it.<br /> Finally, this charm provides a single bonus die that does not count as dice added by charms on any attempt to convince people you are living.<br /> <i>Alternative final benefit: the charm provides a bonus die that does not count as dice added by charms on any attempt to calm, befriend or seduce an undead creature that desires to be among the living, such as most ancestor ghosts </i><br /> <br /> New charm names:<br /> \u2022 Cresent Rose Prana<br /> \u2022 Twin-Tailed Assault<br /> \u2022 Hideous Beauty Revelation","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8097-wern212","name":"wern212","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8097_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T08:19:17-08:00","id":1053826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wern212</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=1053688#post1053688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> \u2022 Twin-Tailed Assault</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunar Wits charm<br /> If the Lunar is the victim of an attack he may activate this charm to first make a wits + stealth roll to make his counterattack unexpected.<br /> This Decisive counter attack automatically knocks the target prone if used in response to an unexpected attack.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> -Cascading Tonal Resonance<br /> -Unbridled Rebuke<br /> -Violence begets Violence Attitude<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-10T06:59:28-08:00","id":1060857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=1053826#post1053826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> -Cascading Tonal Resonance<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Cascading Tonal Resonance (Solar Performance Charm)<br /> One mote per two dice, Indefinite, Supplemental<br /> Prerequisites: Masterful Performance Technique, Essence 2<br /> The notes from a Solar's heart are not like the chaotic yelps of normal mortals. Every note ever sung is in perfect resonance with the the Solar's soul, compounding infinitely to propel the entire piece to majesty that softens evens the coldest heart of a Northern god or drive a forest hermit into furious battle. The Solar spends one mote each time when they sing, activating this charm. As long as the mote stays committed, the Solar gains two Charm dice on Performance rolls that involve singing in some way, which are cumulative with any motes committed from a previous performance. The Solar may only commit motes to this Charm equal to their Essence.<br /> <br /> -Infuriating Trickster Method","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13056,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13056-slipspace2","user":"SlipSpace2","date":". 03-11-2017, 08:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13056-slipspace2","name":"SlipSpace2","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-10T08:02:52-08:00","id":1060878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SlipSpace2</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Infuriating Trickster Method</div> </div> </div> </div>DB Presence, scene-long, simple<br /> Cost: something like 3m 1wp<br /> Fire warms and consumes, air shifts gusts, water pushes and pulls; wood nourishes and poisons; even seemingly supportive earth gives way under one's feet, collapsing into to deadly caverns.<br /> <br /> With this Charm, the Dragonblood takes on this metaphorical duality of his element - evasive and inscrutable, yet direct and invisibly deadly - against a chosen target. While this Charm is active, the dragonblood gets +2 charm-dice on Presence-based Social Influence meant to misdirect or Inspire that target. On an appropriate Stunt, this bonus increases by one extra charm-success.<br /> <br /> <s>Additionally, this bonus applies to the Initiative roll of misdirection-based Gambits such as Distract.</s><br /> <br /> In combat, Distract grants the receiver an additional free point of Initiative, 2 on an applicable stunt.<br /> <br /> Next:<br /> All Things Have Faces Perception","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 03-10-2017, 11:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-12T15:02:08-07:00","id":1061619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=1060878#post1060878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All Things Have Faces Perception</div> </div> </div> </div>Siderial Investigation<br /> <br /> The Siderial can read a god's intimacies in the things under its purview- for example, they might study a river to determine how its spirit feels about the Bureau of Destiny, or study the progression of a disease to determine how its spirit feels about the Solar Exalted. This is modeled as a Read Intentions action with a penalty, carried out over a length of time determined by the essence of the god so observed, ranging from a hour for an essence 1 god to many years for an essence 10 one, as the broad purviews of powerful gods require extensive study to read. Jupiter herself cannot be read in this way, although given enough time and skill the other incarnae can.<br /> <br /> -Inexorable Eccentric Exposition","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12816-diagrapher","name":"diagrapher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12816_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T16:34:41-07:00","id":1062543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>diagrapher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=1061619#post1061619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Siderial Investigation<br /> <br /> The Siderial can read a god's intimacies in the things under its purview- for example, they might study a river to determine how its spirit feels about the Bureau of Destiny, or study the progression of a disease to determine how its spirit feels about the Solar Exalted. This is modeled as a Read Intentions action with a penalty, carried out over a length of time determined by the essence of the god so observed, ranging from a hour for an essence 1 god to many years for an essence 10 one, as the broad purviews of powerful gods require extensive study to read. Jupiter herself cannot be read in this way, although given enough time and skill the other incarnae can.<br /> <br /> -Inexorable Eccentric Exposition</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> this one is good","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T06:42:31-07:00","id":1063827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>diagrapher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=1061619#post1061619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Inexorable Eccentric Exposition</div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereal Linguistics -<br /> <br /> Communication binds and connects. With this knowledge, the Vizier uses a fact--any fact--to tie her fate to another's. The Sidereal's train of thought seems to jump and turn and ramble, turning a sentence into a saga which fate will inevitably interrupt: one or the other will be called elsewhere, a third party may change the subject, or disaster might strike. Regardless, the point of this convoluted narrative continues to bind the two, and the the Sidereal may take advantage of this, gaining 2 non-charm dice to track the target or investigate them until the next scene they meet. The sidereal is subject to a compulsion playing upon a Minor Principle to continue where she left off. This charm may be extended through repeated use, but even the craftiest Sidereal's wit can hold out for only so long. Every time the Exalt uses this charm on a target, she rolls Manipulation + Linguistics to avoid getting to the point. Failure means she comes to the end of her gordian knot of narrative; and cannot use this charm on a target for the rest of the Story.<br /> <br /> * Hideous Beauty Revelation<br /> * Skein-of-Thoughts Tapestry<br /> * Moon and Sun forge","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T15:02:06-07:00","id":1074335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=1063827#post1063827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* Skein-of-Thoughts Tapestry</div> </div> </div> </div>Evocation of Night Quill, a hooked sliver of White Jade adorned with nigh-invisible strands of Starmetal, reminiscent of a knitting needle.<br /> <br /> Type: light<br /> Tags: Special*, Thrown (Short), Poisonable, Subtle, Concealable<br /> <br /> * Night Quill always stays with its owner. After being thrown, a slight tug on its Fate Strand instantly returns it to its owner's hand as long as such a path is physically possible.<br /> <br /> <b>Skein-of-Thoughts Tapestry</b><br /> cost: 4m<br /> Type: Supplemental (any roll to touch, or Thrown)<br /> Keywords: Shaping?, Psyche?<br /> Duration: Scene<br /> <br /> With a touch of the needle or of the hand, the attacker rolls Manipulation + Socialize against the target's Resolve and, on a success, snares two of the target's intimacies, knotting them together as a weaver tying off strands. For good or ill, one intimacy cannot be thought of without the other.<br /> <br /> For Social Influence rolls where both intimacies align, use the higher of the two and add one level (up to Defining). In cases where they compete, simply add one and subtract the other. If it's ever unclear whether the knotted intimacy would apply positively or negatively, the choice goes to the wielder of Night Quill.<br /> <br /> For situations where either one of the knotted intimacies is called upon for any purpose (including Decision Points and Charms like Fists of Iron), successfully justifying both bolsters the chosen intimacy by one level for the purpose of that effect, otherwise the intimacy cannot be used.<br /> <br /> Next: Cloud-Minded Wondering Prana","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":".  typos 04-06-2017, 06:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T13:10:40-07:00","id":1101711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=1074335#post1074335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Next: Cloud-Minded Wondering Prana</div> </div> </div> </div>Charm of Fog Under Water, an Exigent of the God of weather.<br /> The charm requires the Exigent to spend a scene contemplating clouds or weather phenomenon.<br /> After the scene is done, the Exigent may attempt a Lore or Investigation roll they previously failed again, assuming the roll was made to overcome some puzzle or riddle.<br /> This charm can only be used once per puzzle or riddle, per story.<br /> <br /> Next: Inner Devil-Body Unleashed (Or Inner Devil-Body Released, whichever you prefer).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8097-wern212","name":"wern212","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8097_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T02:05:22-07:00","id":1101890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wern212</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/163144-forum-game-what-does-this-charm-do?p=1101711#post1101711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Inner Devil-Body Released</div> </div> </div> </div>Inner Devil-Body Released<br /> Ultimate Charm for the Masquerade Murder Style<br /> The monstrous image created by the False Flag Frenzy form charm becomes more than a false seeming, it becomes a fully realized persona with exp equal to 80 percent of your own, minus the exp for dots and charms of the Masquerade Murder Style. This effect includes a physical transformation. The Persona lacks any Masquerade Murder Style charms instead having an equal number of charms from a different style as the Base character has in Masquerade Murder. This style is chosen when you learn Inner Devil-Body Released charm, and the persona has as many dots in that style as the base character has in the Masquerade Murder style. The Persona can make use of other form charms normally despite being the result of a modification of a form charm, however the motes committed to the False Flag Frenzy form charm must stay committed or the persona fades and the base character re-emerges. The Persona gains exp sufficient to keep it at 80 percent of the Base Character's total, and cannot be modified by persona charms the stylist learns that are not from the Masquerade Murder Style. <br /> <br /> \u200bNext: Steel Imprinting Method, Akashic Impression Prana, or Flesh Administration Authority","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11837-a-not-quite-simple-soul","name":"A Not Quite Simple Soul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-18T09:58:09-07:00","id":1261315,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Void Circle Threadomancy, Activate!!</span></b><br /> <br /> Flesh Administration Authority<br /> Liminal Manipulation Charm<br /> <br /> The living are meat. Meet has needs independent of the spirit. The spirit may object, but the meat is what moves it around, and the Chernozem can bypass one to speak directly to the other.This charm treats any social roll appealing to a basic need or want of the body* as appealing to a Minor Principle, even if their would-be desires are currently sated: hunger can still appeal to a man coming fresh from a harvest feast, and a scribe fresh from a night's slumber can be convinced to take a nap. With a repurchase at Essence 3+, this charm explicitly works its magic across language barriers and upon living bodies currently or permanently devoid of their own will.<br /> <br /> \u200bNext: Steel Imprinting Method, Akashic Impression Prana, or Hideous Beauty Revelation","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-19T23:05:50-07:00","id":1261733,"title":"","content":"'Tis a brave one indeed, to brave the Labyrinth to awaken this beast. Let's see, then....<br /> <br /> <i><b>Akashic Impression Prana</b></i><br /> <br /> Sidereal Athletics Charm<br /> Cost 10m, 1wp<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Keywords: Travel<br /> With the mastery of the Maidens' methods, distance is more a suggestion than a law. By making a slight tapping gesture before her, the Vizier can rush a number of range bands, up to her (Essence) instantly, so long as she possesses line of sight to her desire destination. For longer or more difficult travel, the Vizier must rely on more advanced magic.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Hideous Beauty Revelation</i></b><br /> <br /> Lunar Charisma Charm<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> <br /> For a split second, the Steward unveils the awe-inspiring heart of Luna inherent in all of her Chosen; that single thread of protean terror to devour, survive and adapt, refining their form into a terrifying aspect of this vision. Faced with such an awful, naked truth, few have the heart, or the stomach, to oppose them. The Lunar makes a (Charisma+ Performance) Roll versus the opposing groups' Resolve, and all enemy groups must save versus their pertinent intimacies , lest they flee the scene. In battle, any opposing battle groups must immediately check versus routing, regardless of battle strength. This power is a dole-edged sword, however, as allied groups must also check versus this attack, although those who possess an intimacy towards the Lunar gain non-charm dice to their resist roll equal to the strength of their intimacy level.<br /> <br /> Next: Mountain as Molehill Methodology, Steel Imprinting Method or Knowing Siren Atemi","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1586,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","user":"Dietaku","date":". 10-20-2018, 02:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-22T16:23:00-07:00","id":1262250,"title":"","content":"<b>Mountain as Molehill Methodology</b>: Lunar Manipulation, psyche effect that temporarily convinces an individual to downplay or ignore something they have witnessed in the scene that violates one of their principles.<br /> <br /> <b>Steel Imprinting Method</b>: Dragon-Blooded Resistance, Earth Aspect. The Terrestrial attunes herself to the composition of a metal or stone weapon that has struck her during the scene, increasing her soak against attacks from it for the rest of the scene. A Wood aspect activation functions on wooden weapons.<br /> <br /> <b>Knowing Siren Atemi</b>: Dragon-Blooded Stealth, Water Aspect, allows the Terrestrial to make a stealth attack from plain sight on a target, provided she has instilled a positive intimacy towards herself during the scene.<br /> <br /> Next: any or all of the following: Dance of the Black Jade Tiger, Bridge-Building Stride, Perfection of the Twelve Rings, The Sword that Slays Sankhara.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-29T07:30:14-07:00","id":1263351,"title":"","content":"Bridge-Building Stride<br /> Requirements: Essence 4, Craft (stonemason or carpenter 5)<br /> Cost: 4s 1wp<br /> Type: reflexive<br /> Prerequisite charms: a craftsman needs no tools.<br /> Effect: this charm enhances the prerequisite, - allowing the solar to instantly finish a major structure project. As long as he doesn't interrupt his work after paying the initial cost, he can build a structure at the speed of his movement, assembling any pieces of it he can reach, even using it reflexively to stunt in combat (such as building a wall behind himself during a disengage attempt, or building a ramp to charge at a much larger enemy. )<br /> <br /> Next: closed fist counter-argument technique.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23788-braininthejar","name":"Braininthejar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-10T14:16:35-08:00","id":1266270,"title":"","content":"<b>closed fist counter-argument technique: </b>\u200bdragon blooded manipulation, fire aspect. allows for a dragon blood to add intimidation dice to total dice pool for social rolls for 1 scene<br /> <br /> Next: Memories of Past Glories, Soothing Cemetery's Grace.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24794-gadrial","name":"gadrial","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}